or so, so \"近6个月\" relative to real today (2026) would be empty! The planner asking \"是指2017年的最后6个月还是其他时间段\" is actually a REASONABLE clarification given \"近\" is relative).\n\nHmm — actually, from a pure product logic standpoint: the user asked turn 1 about 2017 monthly sales. Turn 2 says \"近6个月\" — the planner interpreted it and asked whether it means 2017-07~12 or another range. That's defensible behavior (近 = relative to now; data ends 2017-10/11/12). It's not necessarily a context loss. BUT the user expects continuity.\n\nKey question: did turn 2's context actually include turn 1's history? I should check rather than speculate:\n- The context engine has a `ContextConversationSummaryModel` and history manager. In production, `build_context_engine` — I need to look at what it wires for history/store. If the production engine's store is in-memory per-process or reads from PG conversation messages, that determines continuity.\n- Also the screenshot's question itself says \"是指2017年的最后6个月（7月至12月）\" — interesting: the planner knew 2017's last 6 months is 7-12月. That knowledge could come from the context (previous answer listed 2017-01..12!) or from the data catalog. Actually 7-12月 is just calendar knowledge, not necessarily from context. But mentioning \"2017年的最后6个月\" as an OPTION suggests it did see the 2017 context — a generic planner without context would probably ask \"哪个时间范围？\" without proposing 2017-07~12 specifically. Hmm, it proposed exactly \"2017年的最后6个月（7月至12月）\" — that strongly suggests it DID see the previous turn's 2017 monthly data. If context were lost, it wouldn't know to propose 2017.\n\nSo my hypothesis: context continuity is actually working (the planner proposed the 2017-07~12 option precisely because it saw the previous turn), and the ask_user is the planner being cautious about the relative term \"近\". The D-slice capabilities allow ask_user (`PlannerCapabilities(allow_ask_user=True)`).\n\nBut wait — the user's deeper point: \"并没有连贯起来\" (didn't connect). Maybe they expected: since turn 1 established 2017 as the year of interest, turn 2's \"近6个月\" should auto-resolve to the last 6 months OF THAT DATASET/2017 context without asking. That's a planner-quality / context-injection expectation, not a finalization bug.\n\nBefore answering, I should verify what the context actually contained for turn 2. How? Check:\n1. `context_build_runs` table (ContextBuildRunModel) — records context builds with build_id, maybe token counts and selected items. Let me check its schema — it may store the request/payload.\n2. The log pasted: after 分析计划生成, extract_keywords... The context engine built context for turn 2 — the context_build_runs row would show whether conversation history was included.\n\nLet me investigate the code: `build_context_engine` factory + how history is loaded (ConversationHistoryManager with a store — production store?). Let me read `app/agent/context_engine/factory.py`.\n\nThen check the context_build_runs table for the latest build of conversation 22c249b8.\n\nPlan:\n1. Read factory.py to understand production context wiring (does it read PG history?).\n2. Query context_build_runs for turn 2's build to see what went in (if the table has payload info).\n3. Answer the user: either (a) context IS connected — the 2017 option in the clarification proves it; the pause is the planner treating \"近\" as ambiguous relative time, which is by design (and arguably correct since \"近6个月\" relative to real-world today vs data time differs); or (b) if context actually missing — that's a bug to fix.\n\nAlso note: the previous D7 acceptance ran two independent questions; follow-up continuity (\"按品类拆分上一题的结论\") was in my checklist as question 3 — designed to verify exactly this. The user hit the continuity question early at question 2.\n\nLet me look at the factory and the context build record.","startTime":1791428023741,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023741},{"id":"2427f215-a5ee-4a67-884e-4a497d702b15","type":"TEXT","end":true,"co