erminal quickly before finalizing the design. If cancelled runs emit run.cancelled, I could extend the blanket: `if ((runCompleted || runInterrupted) && ...)` with interrupted → keep latestStatus except running→? hmm.\n\nSimplest robust choice: for terminal interrupt events (run.cancelled/run.timeout), also set blanket success? No — wrong.\n\nAlternative: leave it. Cancelled traces showing in-flight spinning is a minor cosmetic edge; the run-level status (开始执行 red? the run.cancelled event lands in whichever step group) communicates termination. Actually — where does run.cancelled land? harnessStep(\"run.cancelled\") → not matched → \"Harness 运行\" step (STEP_ORDER index -1 → sorted last). So the \"Harness 运行\" group shows failed (red X from run.cancelled). Mid-flight modules spin forever. Meh.\n\nBetter: extend the terminal blanket to cancelled/timeout: when run.cancelled/run.timeout present, freeze: modules whose latest is running → keep? Can't express \"interrupted\" with existing 5 statuses. I'll not over-engineer; note it as known cosmetic edge in the reply (cancelled 轮次的中间模块会停留在转圈状态). Actually — hmm, I could map \"running at interrupt\" to... \"partial\"? Amber alert — \"部分完成/被中断\"! partial fits semantically: 模块没跑完被中断 → amber AlertCircle. Blanket: if runInterrupted && latestStatus === \"running\" → \"partial\"? That's elegant: interrupted modules show amber ⚠ (中断), completed ones keep 绿勾, failed keep 红. And runCompleted blanket unchanged.\n\nIs that over-engineering beyond user ask? It's 3 lines and makes cancelled traces honest. The user cares about correct status at every granularity (\"那个模块走完了就是状态进行更新\"). For cancelled runs, \"走完的翻绿，没走完的标黄\" matches their intent. I'll include it — small and principled. Hmm wait — but partial is also used for tool partial results (amber). Reusing for \"被中断\" is consistent enough (amber = 未完整).\n\nLet me implement:\n\n```ts\nfunction statusForEvents(events: DebugEvent[], fallback?: RunStatus, runCompleted = false): RunStatus {\