t if backend API still responds"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nHTTP 200 in 0.026641s\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"s1dap4","output":"HTTP 200 in 0.026641s\n","exitCode":0,"inBackground":false}}}]},{"id":"6aab5a2d5f656e21e78d7bf3","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":36332},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"8c16d956-64a5-4b65-b0f2-5bc386597daf","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The API responds instantly (26ms) — **the event loop is alive and healthy**. So no sync blocking. The run coroutine is genuinely `await`ing something that never resolves, with no network connection open.\n\nWhat awaits without a network connection?\n1. An asyncio task waiting on a Future/Event that never fires.\n2. A queue.get() that never receives.\n3. **A connection pool checkout waiting for a free connection** — e.g., a DB/embedding client pool where all connections were lost and the acquire waits forever.\n4. An HTTP client waiting on a pooled connection that died (rare).\n5. **The embedding client call** — if the LLM provider connection dropped mid-request without timeout... but then there'd be a connection in some state (maybe not — if TCP was closed, aiohttp would error out, not hang).\n\nHmm — wait. What about `asyncio.gather(*(search_one(term) for term in terms))` — each search_one: `aembed_query` (LLM API HTTPS call) then `repository.search` (Qdrant/ES). No connections to 443 or Qdrant/ES right now. If aiohttp session had no timeout, a dropped connection would eventually raise... \n\nWait — actually, hold on. Maybe the embedding provider call is hanging at the DNS/connect phase? No connection shown though — DNS resolution wouldn't show as TCP.\n\nHmm, let me think differently. What does the frontend show? \"工具与事件 11\" — the SSE stream is alive? The tool has been \"executing\" for 5+ minutes. The tool timeout! `timeout_seconds = request.tool_call.timeout_seconds or spec.timeout_seconds` — query_timeout_seconds = 300 (5 min). `asyncio.wait_for(tool.execute(value), timeout=300)` — the tool started at ~11:04:46 (planner completed ~11:05:00, action committed, tool started ~11:05:00 per DB updated_at 11:05:00). 300s from 11:05:00 = 11:10:00. **It's 11:09:20 now — the 5-minute tool timeout will fire at ~11:10!**\n\nSo the design anticipated this: `asyncio.wait_for` cancels the hung tool → tool_timeout → retry or error result. max_tool_retries=2. So even if the subgraph is stuck, at ~11:10 the tool times out and the loop handles it (retry → probably hangs again 5 min → retry → final failure → run fails with FAILED status).\n\nSo: wait ~1 minute and see if the tool timeout fires at 11:10. Actually by the time I respond it may already have fired. Let me check the run status NOW — if it's past 11:10, check whether wait_for fired (status changed, error recorded, or retry in progress).\n\nActually wait — I should check right now what time it is and the run state again. Let me poll the DB. Also — the deeper question remains WHY the subgraph coroutine hangs with no open connection. Possibly `aembed_query` uses a client with no timeout and the HTTPS connection got blackholed (macOS network change? VPN?). With no ESTABLISHED connection, the TCP retransmission would still show a socket (SYN_SENT). No socket at all = the await isn't on a socket... \n\nOH WAIT. I bet I know what it is! `asyncio.wait_for(tool.execute(value), timeout=timeout_seconds)` — when the timeout fires, wait_for CANCELS the inner task. But the query_graph's `astream` async generator... cancellation of a LangGraph astream with pending nested tasks... LangGraph's astream uses its own task management (PregelLoop). Cancelling mid-stream can hang if the generator's cleanup awaits something un-cancellable... but that's AFTER the timeout fires (11:10), not before.\n\nRight now (pre-timeout): the coroutine awaits something without an open socket. Ideas:\n- `asyncio.gather` on search_one tasks → `aembed_query` → httpx AsyncClient with... hmm.\n- Actually maybe the embedding client is a \"auto_llm_client\" with internal queue/worker that lost its connection?\n\nWhatever the root cause of the hang, the SYSTEM DESIGN handles it: tool timeout at 300s → cancel → retry ×2 → fail. Let me just verify the timeout fires: check the run now (should be ~11:10+).","startTime":1791428023743,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023743},{"id":"1f1e141d-1202-49cc-9556-b190bbfbbcfd","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"API 26ms 响应——事件循环是活的，没有同步阻塞；协程是在 `await` 一个永远不回来的东西（且没有对外连接）。但注意：**工具有 300 秒超时兜底**（`query_timeout_seconds: 300`，工具 11:05:00 启动 → 11:10:00 应触发 `asyncio.wait_for` 取消）。看看现在跑到哪了："},{"id":"call_7fdfd63d5c454c3a9e3e3d61","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"date \"+%H:%M:%S\" && psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U z523 -d agent_app -c \"SELECT status, phase, iteration, last_error, updated_at AT TIME ZONE 'UTC' AS updated_utc FROM harness_runs WHERE run_id='c1dab3bb-7a12-4b2e-9af8-49b5e7e78c52';\" 2>&1 | head -12","description":"Re-check run status after tool timeout window"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\n11:11:13\nERROR:  column \"last_error\" does not exist\nLINE 1: SELECT status, phase, iteration, last_error, updated_at AT T...\n                                         ^\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"acn0hx","output":"11:11:13\nERROR:  column \"last_error\" does not exist\nLINE 1: SELECT status, phase, iteration, last_error, updated_at AT T...\n                                         ^\n","exitCode":0,"inBackground":false}}}]},{"id":"6aab5a521ca25a5d690423f7","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":5287},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"call_e021b4d1177c44cfbe8c1a33","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_co