nd yaml), harmless.\n\nNow the check for dimension at startup: lifespan is async → after `embedding_client_manager.init()`, do `await embedding_client_manager.verify_dimension(settings.qdrant.vector_size)` — embed \"ping\" and compare len. Fail-fast: raise RuntimeError → lifespan fails → app won't start. Log clear message.\n\nDesign of embedding_client.py after change:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Embedding 客户端管理器。...\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nfrom typing import Optional, Union\n\nfrom langchain_core.embeddings import Embeddings\nfrom langchain_huggingface import HuggingFaceEndpointEmbeddings\nfrom langchain_openai import OpenAIEmbeddings\n\nfrom app.core.config import EmbeddingConfig, settings\n\n\nclass TimeoutHuggingFaceEmbeddings(HuggingFaceEndpointEmbeddings):\n    \"\"\"本地推理服务的硬超时包装；挂起时快速失败而不是无限等待。\"\"\"\n\n    timeout_seconds: float = 30.0\n\n    async def aembed_query(self, text: str) -> list[float]:\n        return await asyncio.wait_for(super().aembed_query(text), timeout=self.timeout_seconds)\n\n    async def aembed_documents(self, texts: list[str]) -> list[list[float]]:\n        return await asyncio.wait_for(super().aembed_documents(texts), timeout=self.timeout_seconds)\n\n\nclass EmbeddingClientManager:\n    \"\"\"管理 Embedding 服务客户端的初始化与复用\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, config: EmbeddingConfig):\n        self.client: Optional[Embeddings] = None\n        self.config = config\n\n    def _local_url(self) -> str:\n        return f\"http://{self.config.host}:{self.config.port}\"\n\n    def init(self):\n        \"\"\"显式初始化客户端，避免模块导入时立即建立外部连接\"\"\"\n        if self.config.provider == \"dashscope\":\n            self.client = OpenAIEmbeddings(\n                model=self.config.model_name,\n                dimensions=self.config.dimensions,\n                api_key=self.config.api_key,\n                base_url=self.config.base_url,\n                timeout=self.config.timeout_seconds,\n                max_retries=0,\n                chunk_size=self.config.batch_size,\n            )\n        else:\n            self.client = TimeoutHuggingFaceEmbeddings(\n                model=self._local_url(),\n                timeout_seconds=self.config.timeout_seconds,\n            )\n\n    async def verify_dimension(self, expected: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"启动自检：实际向量维度必须与 Qdrant 集合配置一致，防止静默的垃圾检索。\"\"\"\n        if self.client is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Embedding 客户端尚未初始化\")\n        vector = await self.client.aembed_query(\"embedding 维度自检\")\n        if len(vector) != expected:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Embedding 维度不一致：模型返回 {len(vector)} 维，Qdrant 集合配置 {expected} 维\"\n            )\n```\n\nWait — OpenAIEmbeddings parameter for timeout: in langchain_openai ≥0.1, the param is `timeout` (alias request_timeout deprecated). Signature: OpenAIEmbeddings(timeout: Optional[float] = None, ..., max_retries: Optional[int] = None, chunk_size: int = 1000, dimensions: Optional[int] = None, api_key, base_url). Pydantic model — check field names: `dimensions`, `chunk_size`, `max_retries`, `timeout`... Actually in langchain_openai embeddings base.py: fields include `client`, `async_client`, `model`, `dimensions`, `chunk_size`, `deployment`, `embedding_ctx_length`, `allowed_special`, `disallowed_special`, `openai_api_base` etc. The timeout param: `request_timeout` was renamed `timeout` in newer versions (with alias). Let me verify quickly by inspecting model_fields — I have the venv.\n\nAlso DashScope compatible-mode embeddings: does `dimensions` param work on text-embedding-v3 via OpenAI compatible API? Yes — DashScope supports the `dimensions` parameter for text-embedding-v3/v4 in compatible mode.\n\nAlso async support: OpenAIEmbeddings.aembed_query uses AsyncOpenAI — fine. timeout applies.\n\nOne concern: OpenAIEmbeddings `check_embedding_ctx_length` — by default True, which tokenizes with tiktoken and splits by ctx length — for non-OpenAI models this can mangle text?? For OpenAIEmbeddings with non-OpenAI endpoints, there's a known issue: `check_embedding_ctx_length=True` uses tiktoken to tokenize (cl100k_base) and sends token arrays — DashScope expects raw text input, and sending token IDs fails or produces wrong results! Common fix for DashScope/Qwen via OpenAIEmbeddings: `check_embedding_ctx_length=False`. Yes — important. With check_embedding_ctx_length=False, it sends the raw text strings.\n\nLet me set `check_embedding_ctx_length=False`.\n\nNow EmbeddingConfig:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass EmbeddingConfig:\n    \"\"\"Embedding 服务配置。\"\"\"\n\n    # dashscope：云端兼容模式；local：本地推理服务（TEI）。\n    provider: str\n    # provider=local 时的本地推理服务地址。\n    host: str\n    port: int\n    # provider=local 时的本地模型名。\n    model: str\n    # provider=dashscope 时的远程模型与维度；维度必须与 Qdrant vector_size 一致。\n    model_name: str\n    dimensions: int\n    api_key: str\n    base_url: str\n    # 单次批量请求的文本数量上限。\n    batch_size: int\n    # 单次 embedding 调用的硬超时；服务挂起时快速失败而不是无限等待。\n    timeout_seconds: float\n```\n\nDo I keep retry_count/retry_backoff_seconds? grep consumers: `settings.embedding.retry` — earlier grep for \"settings.embedding\" showed only batch_size and model consumers. Are retry fields used anywhere? Let me grep to be sure. If unused, drop them from config to keep it clean (\"不做没必要的兼容\" style). But yaml comment mentions them; they're likely legacy. I'll grep and if unused, remove from yaml+config.\n\nyaml:\n\n```yaml\nembedding:\n  # dashscope：云端千问向量化；local：本地推理服务（需要 Docker，占运行内存）。\n  provider: dashscope\n  # provider=dashscope 时的配置；维度必须与 qdrant.vector_size 一致。\n  model_name: text-embedding-v3\n  dimensions: 1024\n  api_key: ${oc.env:DASHSCOPE_API_KEY,\"\"}\n  base_url: ${oc.env:DASHSCOPE_BASE_URL,https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1}\n  # 单次批量请求的文本数量上限；DashScope 上限 10，留余量。\n  batch_size: 6\n  # 单次 embedding 调用硬超时；超时后工具直接失败，不做重试。\n  timeout_seconds: 30\n  # provider=local 时的配置。\n  host: 127.0.0.1\n  port: 8081\n  model: BAAI/bge-large-zh-v1.5\n```\n\nmain.py lifespan