th 10 items. That matches the screenshot (the drawer opened from within the 构建上下文 step card).\n\nHmm wait, but the screenshot shows \"节点：context_engine / 10 个返回项\" with items from both rounds. And planning drawer with 4 items. Yes.\n\nSo the user's proposal: group by iteration (轮次). The user says \"应该是sql查询完毕后有回到了loop，所以应该是第二轮\" — i.e., after SQL query done, loop returns → second round: context rebuild + replan. The tab should reflect this loop structure.\n\nMy opinion: agree. The harness's mental model is the loop: 每一轮 = 构建上下文 → 规划 → 执行动作。The tab called \"步骤返回\" showing merged node groups doesn't convey the round structure.\n\nDesign proposal:\n- Top level of 步骤返回: 轮次 (iterations). \"第 1 轮\"、\"第 2 轮\"... plus non-iterative bookends (开始执行/最终收口/运行结果).\n- Inside each round: the existing step groups (构建上下文 → 任务划分 → 执行工具) in time order, with their node groups.\n\nImplementation: events already carry `iteration` in payload (makeEvent stores whole event as payload). Wait — actually is iteration top-level in the SSE event or nested? `_emit` signature: let me check. If `_emit(run_ref, \"context.started\", phase=..., iteration=...)` puts iteration at top level of the emitted event dict, then frontend `event.iteration` is top-level, and safePayload copies it into payload. In makeEvent I can read `event.iteration` directly (StreamEvent has index signature [key: string]: unknown).\n\nBut do the tool-internal bridged events (tool.progress from query_data's graph nodes) have iteration? Those come through writer.custom → tool_runtime publishes them... The tool progress events are emitted by the tool execution context. Do they carry iteration? Possibly via tool.started/tool.completed events (which have iteration?) — need to check tool_runtime._publish_result / tool.started emit. And writer.custom events — source={tool}:{node}, type=tool.progress — may not have iteration.\n\nFallback design that avoids backend changes AND avoids fragile inference: derive the round for every event by