每次 _emit 都带），但 tool.progress 桥接事件没有；所以统一用边界推断：遇到 `context.started` 轮次 +1，之后的事件都归这一轮。\n   - 步骤返回顶层改为：第 1 轮 / 第 2 轮 …（每轮一个卡片，副标题显示该轮干了什么：构建上下文 → 任务划分 → 执行工具），点开里面是现在的节点分组。\n   - 轮次外的固定环节（开始执行、最终收口）单独成组放最前/最后。\n\nWait — should I double-check that tool.started/tool.completed also lack/presence iteration? Doesn't matter for inference design. Keep plan as inference-only — one mechanism, no compatibility branching.\n\nHmm, actually one design question: should 顶层 be 轮次 and inside be steps, or should it stay steps with round suffixes? My recommendation: 轮次 top-level. The 进度 tab already gives module/node real-time status; 步骤返回 becomes the \"loop replay\" view. This is a clean separation of concerns.\n\nAlso should mention: 收口轮 — the last round ends with finalization instead of a tool; it naturally lives inside 第 2 轮 (or the round where planner decided to finish). Fine — actually finalization events (finalization.*) carry their own iteration value from the finalization record. With inference they'd land in the last round. Good.\n\nAnd run.started/run.completed (开始执行/运行结果)? They have iteration=0 probably (run.started emitted with iteration=0 at line 127-149 area... run.started is emitted before first increment; iteration=0). So 开始执行/运行结果 land in round 0 → present as \"准备\" group before 第 1 轮? Simpler: keep STEP_ORDER bookend steps (开始执行、运行结果) as standalone groups outside rounds. Actually with inference: run.started (iteration 0) arrives before first context.started → round 0. Label round 0 as \"开始执行\"? Hmm — simplest presentation: rounds numbered by context build count: 第 1 轮 starts at first context.started; everything before = \"准备阶段\" group at top; run.completed/最终收口 — run.completed arrives at the end → belongs to last round. But run.completed is more of a run-level bookend... it can stay in the last round without harm, or filter it into the tail \"运行结果\" group. I'll keep details light in the reply and decide during implementation.\n\nEstimate: the change is contained in execution-panel.tsx: makeEvent/appendExecutionEvent adds round tracking (or a derive helper applied in buildStepGroups — better: compute rounds in buildStepGroups from the ordered events array, keeping appendExecutionEvent untouched). Actually cleaner: buildStepGroups receives ordered events; walk once, assign round index per event, group by round → within round, reuse existing step grouping. No change to appendExecutionEvent needed since sequence order is already the array order. \n\nI'll present this concisely and ask for confirmation (\"按这个改？\"). The user asked opinion — give it, then offer to implement immediately. Keep it short: diagnosis confirmation + proposal. No need for AskUserQuestion tool; a plain question at the end suffices (their pattern is replying \"ok\").","startTime":1791428023743,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023743},{"id":"d17600c7-658f-4ed6-8c64-5b2894365d80","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"你的判断是对的。把两份截图的时间线对起来看：\n\n- **第 1 轮**：构建上下文 12:20:15–33 → 任务划分 12:20:33–41 → SQL 查询（query_data，约 12:20:41–12:21:20）\n- **回到 loop，第 2 轮**：构建上下文 12:21:20–30 → 任务划分 12:21:31–55 → 收口\n\n而“步骤返回”现在是按步骤名把所有轮次合并（`buildStepGroups` 按 `event.step` 分组，`nodeGroups` 再按节点名分组），所以第 2 轮的“开始构建上下文”直接拼在第 1 轮的“上下文构建完成”后面——确实不符合“步骤”的语义，loop 的结构完全丢了。\n\n我的看法：**顶层应该按轮次组织**。harness 的执行模型就是“构建上下文 → 规划 → 执行动作”循环，每轮一个卡片（第 1 轮 / 第 2 轮……副标题写这轮干了什么），点开里面才是现在的节点分组；开始执行、最终收口这类跨轮环节单独放首尾。这样“步骤返回”和“进度”两个 tab 也就分工明确了：进度看模块实时状态，步骤返回看 loop 回放。\n\n实现上有个现成的便利条件：后端 controller 每次 `_emit` 都带 `iteration` 字段（controller.py:1133），但 query_data 内部桥接出来的 `tool.progress` 事件没有这个字段。所以统一用边界推断最干净——**遇到 `context.started` 轮次 +1，之后的事件都归这一轮**，纯前端改动，不碰后端，也只用一套机制。\n\n按这个改？"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789619607032},{"id":"401c356f-7fa4-4c8a-81f4-b290533dc0be","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"你感觉这样会更清晰吗？","payload":{"query":"你感觉这样会更清晰吗？","rawMessage":"你感觉这样会更清晰吗？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/clients/embedding_client.py","name":"embedding_client.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"d6749b3b-e9d1-4fdd-888c-5d0454bf83c6","requestedAt":1789619685781,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"401c356f-7fa4-4c8a-81f4-b290533dc0be"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]},"taskReminderInjected":true},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789619685792},{"id":"167f67d6-58aa-48f8-b9e7-60825ec4534e","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"401c356f-7fa4-4c8a-81f4-b290533dc0be","reportedId":"eac06ef8-7bb0-4279-814e-b44d75272c0e","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":35.4,"contextUsed":90620,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":667,"totalDuration":27070},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aab6dea5f656e21e78db2e8","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":26403},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"434c59d7-0796-497e-955b-a4868ba3fb1a","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks \"你感觉这样会更清晰吗？\" — \"Do you feel this would be clearer?\" They're asking for my honest assessment of whether the round-based grouping would actually be clearer, not just agreeing with them.\n\nLet me genuinely think about this rather than just saying yes.\n\nArguments FOR round-based grouping (轮次顶层):\n1. Matches the harness execution model — the loop IS the structure. Each round = context → plan → act.\n2. Answers the natural user questions: \"为什么构建上下文出现了两次？\" → because there were two rounds. \"SQL 查完后发生了什么？\" → round 2 started.\n3. The tab is called 步骤返回 — \"步骤\" should reflect execution order/rounds.\n4. With merged grouping, you can't tell which round a return item belongs to without reading timestamps carefully.\n\nArguments AGAINST / potential downsides:\n1. Extra nesting level: 轮次 → 步骤 → 节点 → 事件. For a simple run (1 round, 1 tool), the round layer adds a pointless wrapper. Most runs are actually 1-2 rounds.\n2. The 进度 tab already shows real-time module status. The 步骤返回 tab's original purpose is \"返回值查看\" — seeing what each step returned (payloads). Deep nesting makes reaching a payload more clicks.\n3. Round 2 in this run only had context + planning + finish — the \"round\" is mostly a replay artifact.\n\nBut overall — yes, I think it's genuinely clearer, because:\n- The merged view actively misleads (second \"开始构建上下文\" looks like a duplicate/error).\n- Timestamps are the only way to reconstruct rounds currently — that's the UI's job, not the user's.\n- The common case (this project's analysis runs) is 2-3 rounds; the loop story is the main thing to communicate.\n\nHowever, I should be honest about the trade-off and propose mitigations:\n- Keep it flat-ish: round card subtitle shows the round's step chain (构建上下文 → 任务划分 → query_data) so you often don't need to expand.\n- Single-round runs: don't show \"第 1 轮\" wrapper — just show steps directly (only add round grouping when 轮次 ≥ 2). This avoids the useless wrapper for simple runs. Hmm — is that a \"看起来就不靠谱的判断逻辑\"? No, it's reasonable: conditional structure based on actual content. But it does create inconsistent UI between runs. Alternative: always show rounds but auto-expand single round. Actually simpler and more consistent: always group by round. The user hates 不靠谱判断逻辑 but conditional grouping isn't unreliable — still, consistency wins; auto-expand round 1 when there's only one round.\n\nAlso worth noting what does NOT change: 进度 tab stays module-based (real-time status), 全部事件 stays flat. So the division of labor: 进度 = 实时状态, 步骤返回 = loop 回放, 全部事件 = 原始流水.\n\nMy honest answer: yes, clearer, with reasoning, plus the two design details (round subtitle summary; single-round handling). Keep it short — this is a conversational design discussion, not an essay. Then ask if I should implement.\n\nActually the user has now asked twice for my opinion (\"你感觉呢\", \"你感觉这样会更清晰吗\") — they're probing whether I actually believe it or am just agreeing. I should give a real answer with the trade-off, maybe a small sketch of what the panel would look like. A tiny ASCII sketch could help communicate. Keep concise.","startTime":1791428023743,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023743},{"id":"7456202d-1448-4b8a-b307-016826d36a17","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"会的，我说下真实判断，不只是顺着你的说法。\n\n**现在的视图有个实际问题**：它不只是“不清晰”，是会误导——第 2 轮的“开始构建上下文”紧跟在第 1 轮的“上下文构建完成”后面，看起来像重复执行或出了 bug，用户得自己看时间戳才能还原出 loop 结构。这个还原工作应该由 UI 做，不该甩给看面板的人。\n\n**按轮次分组后，视图直接回答了两个最自然的问题**：\n- “为什么构建上下文出现了两次？\" → 因为跑了 2 轮\n- “SQL 查完之后发生了什么？\" → 回到 loop，第 2 轮重新构建上下文、重新规划\n\n结构变成：\n\n```\n第 1 轮  构建上下文 → 任务划分 → query_data   ✓\n  ├─ 构建上下文 (context_engine)\n  ├─ 任务划分 (planning_agent)\n  └─ SQL 查询 (query_data 内部步骤)\n第 2 轮  构建上下文 → 任务划分 → 收口         ✓\n  ├─ ...\n```\n\n轮次卡片副标题带上这轮的步骤链，多数情况不用展开就知道整轮干了什么。\n\n**一个要承认的代价**：多一层嵌套，单轮的简单 run 会显得“包了一层没必要的壳”。我的处理是单轮时不渲染“第 1 轮”这层包装，直接展示步骤——这不算不靠谱的分支，是按内容决定结构。\n\n三个 tab 的分工也更明确了：**进度**看模块实时状态（不动），**步骤返回**看 loop 回放，**全部事件**看原始流水（不动）。\n\n要我按这个改吗？"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789619713055},{"id":"4d8aea0b-969e-42d8-9bcc-4f4369eb36e5","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"那你感觉进度tab需不需要改变一下呢？当然不展示详情还是就是单节点，不会回溯这种","payload":{"query":"那你感觉进度tab需不需要改变一下呢？当然不展示详情还是就是单节点，不会回溯这种","rawMessage":"那你感觉进度tab需不需要改变一下呢？当然不展示详情还是就是单节点，不会回溯这种","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/clients/embedding_client.py","name":"embedding_client.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"d710167b-cf15-4dc9-b463-803889499246","requestedAt":1789619795923,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"4d8aea0b-969e-42d8-9bcc-4f4369eb36e5"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789619795975},{"id":"bf2f7a6a-a183-405c-89d5-1558076f2297","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"4d8aea0b-969e-42d8-9bcc-4f4369eb36e5","reportedId":"6ecd583b-fa6a-43a7-99fa-d0366aae3733","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":36.31,"contextUsed":92961,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":437,"totalDuration":52139},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aab6e58cdf0c54e273200ee","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":51704},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"21f5c675-759e-4f2e-81f1-109981e4c157","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"那你感觉进度tab需不需要改变一下呢？当然不展示详情还是就是单节点，不会回溯这种\"\n\nTranslation: \"Do you think the 进度 (Progress) tab needs to change too? Of course it doesn't show details, it's still single nodes, won't do this kind of backtracking/retrospection.\"\n\nSo the user is asking my opinion on whether the Progress tab should also change, with their own leaning stated: Progress tab stays simple — single node, no details, no \"回溯\" (no historical rounds replay).\n\nLet me think about what the Progress tab currently shows. From my earlier work (real-time status updates):\n- ProgressView shows modules grouped by node (context_engine, planning_agent, tool modules, loop_controller, finalization) with real-time status derived from events\n- Each module: pending → spinner → success/failed icon\n- Module/node/child-node status updates the moment each completes\n\nThe current Progress tab has the same \"merge all rounds\" issue in a sense: context_engine module covers both rounds. But the user's point: Progress tab is a status board — it shows the CURRENT state of each module, not a history replay. \"不会回溯\" — it doesn't need to show round 1 vs round 2; it shows \"构建上下文 ✓, 任务划分 ✓, SQL 查询 ✓, 当前: 第 2 轮构建上下文...\" \n\nSo does the Progress tab need to change? Let me think about what's actually displayed and whether the merged-round model hurts it:\n\n1. In Progress tab, when round 2's context build starts, the context_engine module flips from success back to running (spinner), then success again. Is that confusing? Actually that's semantically correct for a status board: \"构建上下文\" is currently running again. A status board shows current state — like a CI pipeline showing stages.\n\n2. Should it show round progress like \"第 2 轮\"? The user suggests no — keep it simple, single node per module, no history. \n\nMy honest opinion: mostly agree with the user — the Progress tab's job is real-time status at a glance, and per-module status is the right granularity. BUT there's one genuinely useful piece of loop information missing in the Progress tab: which iteration you're on / overall progress. When the run is in round 2, the panel shows... what? If modules flip back to running, a viewer might wonder if it's a retry/loop. A tiny, cheap addition solves this: show current iteration in the header area (e.g., \"第 2 轮 · 最多 8 轮\") or a subtle round badge on a module that has re-entered running state.\n\nActually wait — let me reconsider. There's a subtlety with the merged module model in Progress tab: status derivation uses ALL events of the module. When round 2 context.started arrives, context_engine module goes running → success. Fine. But if round 1 had a failure in a tool and round 2 succeeds, what does the module show? statusForEvents: failed check first → module shows failed even though the run moved on and eventually succeeded. That's actually wrong for a status board! The status board should show the LATEST state, not \"any failure poisons the module forever\".\n\nHmm, but wait — in a single run, if query_data failed in round 1, does the loop do a round 2? Tool failure → observation recorded → planner sees failure → may retry with new tool call (round 2). So query_data module would have failed event (round 1) + success event (round 2). Current statusForEvents shows \"failed\" (failed check first). But the truth is \"最终失败了\" or \"重试后成功\". For a status board, showing the latest round's status (with maybe a retry count badge) is more accurate.\n\nSo my answer: Progress tab keeps its current shape (module grid, no details, no round history) — agree with the user. Two small refinements worth doing:\n1. Module status should follow the LATEST round (latest-wins) instead of \"any failure sticks\" — so a round-2 success after a round-1 failure shows success (with maybe \"重试\" hint). Actually currently: failed check first — this was designed when modules = one-shot. With multi-round runs, latest-wins is more truthful for a status board. Hmm, but careful: if round 1 tool failed and round 2 planner decided to finish without retrying that tool, latest context/planner events succeed but the tool module should still show failed. Latest-wins per module works: tool module's latest event is the failure (no round-2 tool event for it) → failed. Context module's latest is round-2 success → success. That's exactly right.\n2. Optional: a small \"第 N 轮\" indicator in the panel header (from max context.started count) so the loop is visible without restructuring. And maybe a spinner on a module that was previously success and re-entered running — that already works with latest-wins.\n\nIs #1 actually a change from current behavior? statusForEvents: \"failed check first → explicit event.status → derived\". Let me recall... From summary: `statusForEvents`: failed check first. So yes, currently any failed event in the module makes the whole module failed. For harness runs with retries across rounds, that's stale. But hold on — is that right? Let me think about what failed-first was protecting: the execution panel where a failed sub-step should stay visibly failed even after subsequent progress events. For the 步骤返回 tab that's fine (history). For the 进度 tab (status board), latest-wins is the correct semantic.\n\nHmm — but do I want to change statusForEvents for Progress only? The 步骤返回 rework will restructure grouping anyway. I can scope: Progress tab module status = latest round wins (derive from the module's most recent round of events); 步骤返回 keeps per-round statuses.\n\nWait, one more consideration — should Progress tab show anything per-round at all? The user says \"不会回溯这种\" (no backtracking). So no round rows. Just: current status per module. My answer: agree, keep it a status board; only fix the \"old failure sticks forever\" issue (latest-wins), and optionally surface 第 N 轮 subtly in header. Don't add round structure, don't add details.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether even the \"第 N 轮\" header badge is worth it. The user's philosophy: 优雅, no unnecessary stuff. The round info: when you watch a run live and context spins again, you might wonder \"why again?\" A tiny \"第 2 轮\" text answers it. Cheap, one line. I'd recommend it but mark it optional — actually per my instruction to give a recommendation not a menu: recommend it as part of the change (it's 3 lines of code: count context.started).\n\nHmm wait, actually — is there an existing header in ProgressView showing run status? There's the panel header \"执行过程\" + tabs. Th