he payload include the error message? Other failure events: planner.failed payload? Let me check what planner.failed carries — line 585-596 area: `self._emit(command.run_ref, \"planner.failed\", ..., payload={...})`. Let me look at what it includes to be consistent. From earlier grep: lines 585, 596 emit planner.* with iteration. Let me read that region to match the payload style for failure events.\n\nAlso _emit itself swallows emit failures (try/except) ✓ safe.\n\nNote: HarnessDeadlineExceeded — the timeout raises at the CALL SITE (`_await_with_deadline(self._build_context(state), state)` — wait_for wraps the coroutine; if deadline hits mid-build, wait_for cancels the inner task → CancelledError inside _build_context at the await point → caught by `except Exception`? NO — CancelledError is BaseException in 3.8+, NOT Exception. So deadline cancellation won't be caught by except Exception ✓ good (no false context.failed on deadline).\n\nBut wait — asyncio.wait_for cancellation: when wait_for times out, it cancels the inner coroutine and raises TimeoutError to the caller. The inner coroutine gets CancelledError raised at its await point. `except Exception` won't catch CancelledError ✓. So context.failed only on real build errors ✓.\n\nAlso — client disconnect during build → request cancelled → task.cancel() → CancelledError inside build → not caught ✓ → run cancelled path ✓.\n\nNow the frontend edits. Let me be precise about each dead-mapping removal:\n\n1. STEP_ORDER (line 103-106):\n```ts\nconst STEP_ORDER = [\n  \"开始执行\", \"构建上下文\", \"任务划分\", \"提交动作\", \"执行工具\",\n  \"记录观察结果\", \"等待用户确认\", \"最终收口\", \"运行结果\",\n];\n```\n→\n```ts\nconst STEP_ORDER = [\n  \"开始执行\", \"构建上下文\", \"任务划分\", \"提交动作\", \"执行工具\",\n  \"等待用户确认\", \"运行结果\",\n];\n```\n\n2. mainStep (lines 131-139):\n```ts\n  if (type === \"action.committed\") return \"提交动作\";\n  if (type.startsWith(\"tool.\")) return \"执行工具\";\n  if (type === \"observation.recorded\") return \"记录观察结果\";\n  if (type.startsWith(\"c