级终态兜底；前端只做类型推导 + 族内配对，零死代码。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789621950405},{"id":"b60b969a-7827-4554-ad00-d49a56521777","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"我们现在的项目能成为harness了吗","payload":{"query":"我们现在的项目能成为harness了吗","rawMessage":"我们现在的项目能成为harness了吗","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"1fcba8b6-6a0e-4f51-9762-3651f050ca0f","requestedAt":1789627832808,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"b60b969a-7827-4554-ad00-d49a56521777"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789627832932},{"id":"0b7005cb-95d3-404b-862d-071a26d0c636","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"b60b969a-7827-4554-ad00-d49a56521777","reportedId":"047927ad-b38d-4012-b952-3dc99b7cae3b","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":68.75,"contextUsed":175989,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":826,"totalDuration":61801},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aab8db91ca25a5d6904b7ad","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":60976},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"86411c18-f4d3-4f98-8fc2-221475fbcb6c","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"我们现在的项目能成为harness了吗\" — \"Can our project now be considered a harness?\"\n\nThis is a conceptual/architectural assessment question. They're asking whether the current implementation now qualifies as a proper \"agent harness\" — the term we've been using throughout (Data Agent Harness, Loop Controller, HarnessEvent, etc.).\n\nLet me think about what defines an agent harness and honestly assess the current state based on everything I know about this codebase:\n\n**What is an agent harness?** The term (popularized by Anthropic's building effective agents, and the SWE-bench / agent engineering discourse) refers to the scaffolding around an LLM that provides:\n1. **A controlled execution loop** — the agent doesn't free-run; each step goes through a controller\n2. **State persistence & resumability** — checkpoints, recoverable state\n3. **Deterministic guardrails** — budgets, timeouts, deadlines, iteration limits\n4. **Observability** — event streams, traces, auditability\n5. **Tool runtime isolation** — validation, idempotency, result storage\n6. **Human-in-the-loop** — confirmation gates\n7. **Finalization guarantees** — cleanup, resource release, ledger\n8. **Failure containment** — retry policies, controlled failure paths, no fake results\n\nNow let me honestly assess what THIS project has, based on all the work done:\n\n**What's in place (strong):**\n1. **Loop Controller** (M5) — explicit state machine: BUILD_CONTEXT → PLAN → VALIDATE_ACTION → EXECUTE_TOOL → RECORD_OBSERVATION → loop; planner retries, tool retries (per action_id), max_iterations=8\n2. **State persistence** — PostgreSQL harness_runs, running-state saves at every loop boundary, LangGraph checkpointer, fencing tokens (owner_id + fencing_token + lease_expires_at — concurrency protection), action_seq\n3. **Deadlines** — deadline_at persisted, checked at every loop boundary (`_check_deadline`), per-call `_await_with_deadline`, per-tool timeouts (query 300s, analyze 900s, report 600s), run timeout 1800s\n4. **Finalization Ledger** — fixed order: prepared → history_saved → checkpoint_saved → released → formation_submitted → completed; reconcile endpoint for interrupted finalization; FinalizationFailure never fakes terminal states (keeps running/finalization scene for reconcile)\n5. **Event system** — HarnessEvent unified model (iteration, action_id, source, phase), SSE with heartbeats, full trace persistence to conversation turns (save_execution_trace), replay via history\n6. **Cancellation** — client disconnect → task cancel → finalize as CANCELLED with shield\n7. **Tool runtime** — registry, input validation, timeout wrapping, artifact store, retryable/unrecoverable error classification, no fake results\n8. **Confirmation gates** — needs_user pause, confirmation records, repeat-confirmation protection\n9. **Resilience** — embedding hard timeout no-retry, dependency failures → unrecoverable → immediate fail path\n10. **Vertical E + finalization recovery tests** — 184 passing\n11. **Context engine** — memory/knowledge/evidence assembly with token accounting\n12. **Planner** — structured NextAction output, invalid action feedback loop\n\n**What's still missing or weak (honest gaps):**\n1. **D8 build_report** — recently added, user still self-testing acceptance scenarios A/B/C\n2. **Memory formation** — formation submitted in ledger, but the memory side (episodic/semantic) is still young; memory collections just cleared\n3. **Observability beyond events** — no metrics (the SDD mentions harness.run.duration etc. — not implemented), no structured logging correlation? (logs exist with run_id)\n4. **Concurrency/active_run** — exists (active_run release), but multi-user concurrent runs testing (用例 5) not done\n5. **Authentication** — dev-user only, no real auth\n6. **Replay/resume from interruption** — pause/resume semantics recorded in todolist; reconcile exists but replay test not done\n7. **Error taxonomy completeness** — some, but skill/eval coverage unknown\n8. **The \"harness\" front-end observability** just became first-class (round grouping, statuses) — done today\n9. **Evaluation/benchmark loop** — no eval harness for agent quality\n10. **Multi-run orchestration** (parallel tasks within a run?) — planner does sequential tasks via query_data internal tasks; harness loop is single-action-per-iteration\n\nSo: is it a harness? Honestly — **the core harness architecture is in place and it's already more rigorous than most \"agent frameworks\" demos**. The distinguishing harness properties (controlled loop, persisted recoverable state, fencing, deadlines, finality guarantees, event stream, no-fake-results) are all real and tested. What separates it from a *production-grade* harness is operational maturity: metrics, auth, concurrent-run hardening, evals, and the remaining D8 acceptance.\n\nI should answer with an honest assessment: yes for the architectural definition — with a concrete checklist of what qualifies and what's still open. Keep it structured but not bloated. The user likes direct, honest assessments with clear criteria.\n\nFormat: short verdict, then \"已经具备的\" checklist (mapped to harness-defining properties), then \"还不算的\" gaps with what to do next. Should be in Chinese. Moderate length — this is a substantive question deserving a real answer, but avoid padding.\n\nMaybe a compact table or bullet groups. Let me write it.","startTime":1791428023744,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023744},{"id":"c297fbd3-8ea5-4af2-8593-73b96e12d92f","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"按 harness 的定义逐项对一下，给你个诚实的答案：**核心架构已经是了，离“生产级 harness”还差运营成熟度。**\n\n## 已经具备的（harness 的定义性特征）\n\n| 特征 | 现状 |\n|---|---|\n| 受控执行循环 | Loop Controller 显式状态机（构建上下文→规划→校验→执行→观察），Planner 永远不直接碰工具 |\n| 状态持久化与恢复 | harness_runs + 每个循环边界落库 + LangGraph checkpointer + fencing token 防并发写入 |\n| 预算与边界 | deadline_at 持久化 + 每个循环边界检查 + 单调用 deadline + 工具/分析/报告各档超时 + max_iterations=8 |\n| 终局保证 | Finalization Ledger 固定顺序 + reconcile 端点 + FinalizationFailure 不伪造终态 |\n| 可观测性 | 统一 HarnessEvent（iteration/action_id/source/phase）+ SSE 心跳 + 全量 trace 落库可回放 |\n| 人审闸门 | confirmation 暂停/恢复 + 重复确认防护 |\n| 工具运行时隔离 | 注册表 + 入参校验 + 幂等键 + artifact store + retryable/unrecoverable 分类 + 不伪造结果 |\n| 失败遏制 | 今天刚补完的最后一块：生命周期配对完整（context.failed）、失败路径全有终态、前端无死代码 |\n\n这最后一条其实有象征意义——**事件流的生命周期闭合是 harness 和“裸奔 agent”的分界线**。之前 context 崩溃只有 run.failed 兜底，现在每个阶段都有自己的终态，链路上没有任何“静默失踪”的执行片段。184 个测试里 vertical E 和 finalization recovery 覆盖的正是这些最难写对的部分。\n\n## 还不算的（运营成熟度，不是架构问题）\n\n1. **可观测性的上半场**：有事件流但没有 metrics（SDD 里规划的 `harness.run.duration` 那套一个都还没埋）\n2. **认证**：还是 dev-user，无真实登录\n3. **并发演练**：多用户同时跑的用例 5 没做，fencing/active_run 只被单运行测试覆盖\n4. **恢复演练**：reconcile 端点在，但“收口中断 → 重放”的端到端测试没写\n5. **D8 收尾**：build_report 验收场景你还在自测\n6. **评测闭环**：没有 agent 质量的 eval 集——这是“能跑”和“跑得好”的分界\n\n**一句话结论**：作为架构，它已经是 harness——循环、状态、预算、终局、观测、人审六件套都在且有测试背书。剩下的不是“成为 harness”的问题，而是“上线一个 harness”的问题：metrics、auth、并发和恢复演练、D8 收尾。下一个最值得做的单点是 **metrics 埋点**（事件流已经在那了，埋点几乎是白捡的），要动工说一声。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789627895006},{"id":"396b5bc1-7464-4dfb-becb-adedcefdd8e3","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":" metrics 埋点是什么意思？","payload":{"query":" metrics 埋点是什么意思？","rawMessage":" metrics 埋点是什么意思？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"4dedcfb8-3654-487c-a9a1-f6613e84318a","requestedAt":1789628131405,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"396b5bc1-7464-4dfb-becb-adedcefdd8e3"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789628131418},{"id":"d591f602-8d8f-46d6-9b6b-c5db3c79267a","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"396b5bc1-7464-4dfb-becb-adedcefdd8e3","reportedId":"5f66cf08-9a50-4868-9b35-203310ea8f2e","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":69.23,"contextUsed":177230,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":806,"totalDuration":41844},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aab8ee45f656e21e78e1328","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":41022},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"c5ebf6c6-954c-48a5-92ec-c946d0c6e498","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks a simple conceptual question: \"metrics 埋点是什么意思？\" — \"What does metrics instrumentation mean?\"\n\nThis is a conversational/educational question. Explain what metrics instrumentation (埋点) means in this context — concretely, tied to THEIR project. No tools needed. Keep it clear and concrete, using their codebase as examples.\n\nExplain:\n1. 埋点 = instrumentation = embedding metric-recording calls at key points in code\n2. Metrics vs logs vs events/traces — the three pillars. They already have: logs (text, for humans debugging) and events (SSE stream, for frontend display + replay). Metrics = numeric aggregates over time, for machines/dashboards/alerting.\n3. Concrete examples from THEIR SDD (the docs already list them — data_agent_harness_incremental_sdd.md line 4360 mentioned `harness.run.duration`, `harness.iteration.count`, `harness.run.status`, `context.build.duration`, `planner.token_usage`, `tool.call.duration`, `tool.retry_count`, `memory.formation.status` etc.)\n4. What it enables: p95 latency dashboards, error rates, token cost per run, alerting (e.g. tool failure rate spike), capacity planning\n5. How it works technically: a metrics library (prometheus-client) — counters/gauges/histograms, exposed at /metrics endpoint, scraped by Prometheus, viewed in Grafana\n6. Why I said \"almost free\": the event stream already flows through HarnessEventWriter — the emit points are exactly where you'd add metric recording; hooking there gives full coverage without touching business logic.\n\nConcrete example with their code:\n\n```python\n# 现在\nself._emit(run_ref, \"context.completed\", ...)\n# 埋点后\nCONTEXT_BUILD_DURATION.observe(monotonic() - started)  # histogram\nRUN_STATUS_COUNTER.labels(status=\"completed\").inc()    # counter\n```\n\nAnd what a dashboard would answer: \"这周 analysis run 的 p95 耗时多少？\" \"tool_timeout 错误率有没有涨？\" \"每次 run 平均烧多少 token？\"\n\nExplain log vs metric distinction simply:\n- 日志：发生了什么（给人和排障）\n- 事件流：给前端的实时展示和回放\n- 指标：可聚合的数字（给监控系统和报警），比如\"最近一小时工具失败率 3.2%\"\n\nKeep it compact — this is an explanation, not an essay. Use one small code example and 3-4 example questions metrics answer. End with what implementation would look like in their stack (prometheus-client + /metrics endpoint), but don't over-detail.","startTime":1791428023744,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023744},{"id":"ddcd3406-0c3a-4d0a-bffb-367d8fb033f9","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"“埋点”就是在代码的关键位置插入**指标记录调用**——把系统行为变成可聚合的数字，持续积累。\n\n先分清你现在已有的两类东西和缺的这类的区别：\n\n| | 形态 | 给谁看 | 回答的问题 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 日志 | 文本行 | 人（排障） | “这次 run 为什么挂了” |\n| 事件流（你已有的） | 结构化 JSON，SSE + 落库 | 前端展示、回放 | “这一轮执行过程是什么样的” |\n| **指标（缺的）** | 数值序列，随时间累积 | 监控系统、报警 | “这周所有 run 的 p95 耗时是多少” |\n\n事件流是“每一笔的明细”，指标是“千万笔聚合后的曲线”。你不会翻一万个日志文件找规律，但一眼能从曲线上看到“周二下午 tool_timeout 错误率突然从 0.5% 涨到 8%”。\n\n具体到你的项目，埋点长这样——在现在 emit 事件的地方多加一行：\n\n```python\n# controller.py 里现在就有 _emit\nself._emit(run_ref, \"context.completed\", ...)\n# 埋点后同一位置多记录数字\nCONTEXT_BUILD_DURATION.observe(time.monotonic() - started)   # 直方图：构建耗时分布\nTOOL_CALL_TOTAL.labels(tool=tool_name, status=\"failed\").inc()  # 计数器：按工具按状态计数\n```\n\n跑起来后暴露一个 `/metrics` 端点（`prometheus-client` 一行代码），Prometheus 定时来抓，Grafana 出图。\n\n有了它你能直接回答的问题，现在都得靠手写 SQL 翻库：\n\n- 分析类 run 的 p95 耗时 vs 上周，是变快了还是变慢了\n- 哪个工具失败率最高、重试率最高\n- 单次 run 平均烧多少 token（planner.token_usage）——成本核算\n- 今天有没有 run 触发 deadline（报警规则：有就发通知）\n\n你的 SDD 里其实早就规划好了指标清单（`harness.run.duration`、`tool.retry_count`、`memory.formation.status` 那张表，data_agent_harness_incremental_sdd.md:4360），只是还没实现。\n\n我说“几乎是白捡的”是因为：埋点的位置 = 现在的 `_emit` / `_publish_result` 调用点，事件流已经把“哪里该记”标好了，不需要改任何业务逻辑，在 HarnessEventWriter 和 tool runtime 的出口处加十几个 `.observe()/.inc()` 就全覆盖了。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789628173522},{"id":"9f8ac5ea-cb08-42bb-93e9-943891315f02","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"那你打算，这些数据怎么展示呢？","payload":{"query":"那你打算，这些数据怎么展示呢？","rawMessage":"那你打算，这些数据怎么展示呢？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"0dfa4bc9-d6df-4530-9756-6c94a0d65c2b","requestedAt":1789628301032,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"9f8ac5ea-cb08-42bb-93e9-943891315f02"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789628301045},{"id":"8da8c58c-6189-4f14-a89d-c0eafb87b6be","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"9f8ac5ea-cb08-42bb-93e9-943891315f02","reportedId":"f43f260d-ec88-4afe-b7c4-d9025ffa5857","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":69.94,"contextUsed":179057,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":540,"totalDuration":59960},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aab8f8d5f656e21e78e15f4","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":59421},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"e44dd56f-8486-47bf-a51e-4af1727643f5","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"那你打算，这些数据怎么展示呢？\" — \"So how do you plan to display these metrics?\"\n\nThey're asking about the presentation layer for metrics. Let me think about what's the right answer for THEIR project stage.\n\nContext: solo developer, local dev project (Data Agent Harness), MySQL/Postgres/Qdrant/ES/Neo4j already in Docker, FastAPI backend, Next.js frontend. No Prometheus/Grafana deployed. The metrics plan was: prometheus-client + /metrics endpoint.\n\nDisplay options:\n\n**Option A: Prometheus + Grafana (standard stack)**\n- Standard, powerful, industry standard\n- Cost: two more services to run (Docker containers), dashboard configuration effort\n- For a solo dev pre-launch project: heavy-ish, but Grafana dashboards are the \"real\" answer for operational monitoring\n- Grafana has nice visualizations out of the box, alerting built in\n\n**Option B: 自建管理页 in the existing Next.js admin**\n- They don't have an admin console yet (the frontend is the chat insight-agent)\n- Would mean building charts from scratch — pointless duplication\n- Could add a lightweight /api/metrics/summary endpoint + simple page\n\n**Option C: textfile/简单页面 (the /metrics endpoint itself)**\n- Prometheus text format is human-readable-ish but not great\n- Zero work but poor UX\n\nWhat's actually optimal for this project right now?\n\nHonest engineering judgment: the metrics program has two different consumers:\n1. **机器/报警**（Prometheus 抓取 + alert rules）— this doesn't need custom display at all; alerts go to 通知渠道 (email/webhook/飞书)\n2. **人看趋势**（dashboard）— Grafana is the fastest path to good dashboards; building custom charts in Next.js is wasted effort\n\nBut also — there's a subtlety. For a data-agent product, part of \"metrics display\" could be PRODUCT-facing (user-facing analytics: \"你的助手这周处理了多少查询\") vs OPERATIONS-facing (dev monitoring). The user's question follows my framing of operational metrics (p95, error rates, token costs). So ops-facing.\n\nMy recommendation:\n- **第一阶段（埋点本身）**: prometheus-client, /metrics endpoint — data starts accumulating. Actually wait — important consideration: Prometheus pulls and stores its own TSDB. If you only add prometheus-client without a Prometheus server, the /metrics endpoint only shows CURRENT values (counters since process start), no history. So history requires Prometheus (or pushing to somewhere).\n- **第二阶段（存储+展示）**: Prometheus + Grafana as two Docker containers in the existing docker-compose. Grafana provisioned with a dashboard JSON. For a solo dev this is ~half a day setup, standard, and scales to production later.\n- **报警**: Grafana alert rules → webhook (飞书/邮件).\n\nAlternative lightweight path if they don't want two more containers: **Postgres-backed aggregation** — since harness events are already persisted per turn in the execution trace, they could run a nightly/hourly aggregation job writing to a metrics table, and view via simple SQL/charts. But that reinvents Prometheus poorly for real-time; fine for daily reports only. Hmm — actually there's an even simpler intermediate: their events are already in Postgres (execution traces per turn). Wait — actually are they? save_execution_trace saves events JSON per turn in conversation repo. Aggregating from that is possible but ugly (JSON blobs). Better to have proper metrics.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — what would I genuinely recommend for this project?\n\nThe pragmatic sequence:\n1. **埋点先行，不急着展示** — add prometheus-client instrumentation; /metrics endpoint exposes current values. This is where the value density is.\n2. **Prometheus + Grafana docker-compose 加两个服务** — standard scrape + dashboards. Grafana dashboard JSON I'd provision with: run duration p50/p95, run status distribution, tool call rate/error rate by tool, token usage, iteration distribution, memory formation status.\n3. **报警规则** — a few key ones: tool failure rate, deadline-triggered runs, run failure rate, embedding latency.\n4. **产品侧展示（可选、以后）** — if the product later needs user-facing usage stats, that's a separate feature fed from the same metrics/DB, built into the product UI — but that's NOT ops monitoring and shouldn't be mixed.\n\nAlso mention what I would NOT do: build custom chart pages in the Next.js frontend for ops metrics — duplicating Grafana, wasted effort; ops dashboards are for the developer, not end users, so they don't belong in the product UI.\n\nShow what the Grafana dashboard would contain concretely (panels list) so the answer is tangible. Also mention /metrics is enough to start — you can eyeball current values with curl before any Grafana.\n\nStructure:\n1. 原则: 运维指标不进产品 UI —— 展示分两层\n2. 方案: prometheus-client → /metrics（马上有数据）→ docker-compose 加 prometheus + grafana（历史+图表+报警）\n3. Grafana 具体面板清单（concrete, tied to their SDD metrics)\n4. 报警: 2-3 rules examples\n5. 不做的: 自建前端监控页\n6. 落地顺序 + effort estimate\n\nKeep it concise. This is a plan/discussion answer, no implementation yet. End with offer to start with phase 1.","startTime":1791428023744,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023744},{"id":"d44f746b-d2c3-4aa3-a2b1-def81efb804b","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"先说一个原则：**这些是运维指标，不是产品功能，所以不进产品 UI**。给“你”（开发者/运维）看的监控和给最终用户看的界面是两回事，混在一起会把产品页面做脏。展示分三层，按落地顺序：\n\n## 第一层：/metrics 端点（埋点当天就有）\n\n`prometheus-client` 暴露的文本端点本身就是可读的：\n\n```\n# HELP harness_tool_call_total ...\nharness_tool_call_total{tool=\"query_data\",status=\"failed\"} 3\nharness_context_build_duration_bucket{le=\"0.5\"} 41\n```\n\n埋完点 `curl localhost:8000/metrics` 就能看当前值，验证埋点对不对。这一步**不需要任何展示设施**。\n\n## 第二层：Grafana 面板（历史趋势，主战场）\n\ndocker-compose 加两个容器（prometheus 抓取存历史 + grafana 出图），加起来半天工作量，面板我直接用 JSON provision 好，对应 SDD 规划的指标：\n\n| 面板 | 图型 | 回答的问题 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Run 耗时 p50/p95 | 时序曲线 | 性能是变好还是变坏 |\n| Run 终态分布 | 饼图 | failed/timeout/cancelled 占比 |\n| 工具调用率 & 失败率 | 按工具分组的时序 | 哪个工具最不稳 |\n| Token 消耗 | 按 run/按天 | 成本曲线 |\n| Iteration 分布 | 直方图 | Planner 几轮收敛，有没有异常多轮 |\n| Context 构建耗时 / 记忆形成状态 | 时序 | 检索层和记忆层健康度 |\n\n## 第三层：报警（不需要\"看\"，主动找你）\n\nGrafana alert rules → webhook 到飞书/邮件，规则就几条：\n- 工具失败率 5 分钟窗口 > 10%\n- 出现 run 触发 deadline\n- embedding 调用 p99 > 10s（防再出现那次挂死）\n\n## 不做的\n\n**不在 Next.js 里自建监控图表页**——那是把 Grafana 重写一遍，纯浪费；产品侧以后如果要做“用量统计”给用户看，那是另一个功能（从聚合表出数），和运维监控分开。\n\n落地顺序：**先埋点（第一层）→ 跑几天攒数据 → 再上 Prometheus+Grafana（第二层）**。没有历史数据的空面板没意义，所以埋点才是第一步。要开始埋的话说一声。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789628361311},{"id":"0b57c574-c2f9-4126-8977-183916a666c0","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"这个先记录一下先不做，我们目前分析问题，有这些执行过去已经是够用了。接下来我其实更想补充上的是 @filter_metric.py    logger.info(\"指标过滤 LLM 原始返回：%r\", selected_metric_ids) .这些logger方便我更快速的定位到问题在，代码在哪里","payload":{"query":"这个先记录一下先不做，我们目前分析问题，有这些执行过去已经是够用了。接下来我其实更想补充上的是 @filter_metric.py    logger.info(\"指标过滤 LLM 原始返回：%r\", selected_metric_ids) .这些logger方便我更快速的定位到问题在，代码在哪里","rawMessage":"这个先记录一下先不做，我们目前分析问题，有这些执行过去已经是够用了。接下来我其实更想补充上的是$[filter_metric.py](file:app/agent/nodes/filter_metric.py)   logger.info(\"指标过滤 LLM 原始返回：%r\", selected_metric_ids) .这些logger方便我更快速的定位到问题在，代码在哪里","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/nodes/filter_metric.py","name":"app/agent/nodes/filter_metric.py","type":"FILE"},{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"c527814e-b703-4c0e-ae9d-37e5e2c4cc13",