uld be huge and noisy (states contain full candidate lists — hundreds of rows).\n- What to log? For entry: the \"input\" keys the node actually uses (question, keywords, etc.). For exit: summary of returned dict (truncated).\n\nOptions:\nA. **Decorator with explicit field selection**: `@log_node(\"过滤指标\", inputs=[\"input_text\", \"metric_infos\"], outputs=[\"metric_selection\"])` — declarative, per-node specify which state keys matter, decorator logs `key=len or truncated repr` at entry and exit. Elegant, one implementation, per-node config = one line each.\n\nB. **Manual logger.info in each node** — matches existing style but ~15 nodes × 2 logs = repetitive; user explicitly asked for module-level consistency though.\n\nC. **Log full state entry/exit** — too noisy (candidates lists are big), and would blow log files.\n\nOption A is the elegant one. But hold on — let me reconsider. The nodes have different signatures? All graph nodes are `async def node(state: AgentState, runtime: Runtime[AgentContext])`. Two harness-side entry points too? The user said \"按照模块来进行\" — modules = the pipeline nodes (analysis chain). Should it also cover harness controller/services? The context of the conversation: \"我们目前分析问题\" — the analysis pipeline nodes. Keep scope to app/agent/nodes/*.py pipeline nodes. Plus maybe the harness bridge later.\n\nLet me design the decorator:\n\n```python\n# app/agent/nodes/logging.py or app/agent/node_logging.py\n\"\"\"节点级出入口日志：记录每个节点收到什么、返回什么，便于按模块定位问题。\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nfrom collections.abc import Awaitable, Callable\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n_MAX_LOG_CHARS = 500  # hmm, or use repr with truncation\n\ndef _summarize(value):\n    \"\"\"把长列表/长文本压缩成可读摘要，避免日志被候选列表淹没。\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, str):\n        return value if len(value) <= 200 else f\"<{len(value)} 字符> {value[:200]!r}...\"\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return f\"<{len(value)} 项> 首项={value[0]!r}\" if value else \"[]\"\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return f\"<{len(value)} 键> keys={list(value.keys())}\"\n    return repr(value)\n\ndef log_node(step: str, inputs: tuple[str, ...] = (), outputs: tuple[str, ...] = ()):\n    \"\"\"装饰图节点：进入时记录选定的 state 输入，结束时记录返回的 state 更新。\"\"\"\n    def decorator(func):\n        @functools.wraps(func)\n        async def wrapper(state, runtime):\n            logger.info(\"节点[%s]开始：%s\", step, {k: _summarize(state.get(k)) for k in inputs})\n            result = await func(state, runtime)\n            logger.info(\"节点[%s]结束：%s\", step, {k: _summarize(result.get(k)) for k in outputs})\n            return result\n        return wrapper\n    return decorator\n```\n\nWait — but many nodes already HAVE logging (filter_table logs selection, extract_keywords logs raw, retrieve_columns logs both, generate_sql logs call+return...). Adding decorator logs would duplicate those existing logs. Options: remove the now-redundant manual logs and standardize on the decorator? That's a bigger refactor touching many files — risk of losing the \"LLM 原始返回\" logs which the user explicitly values. Hmm.\n\nThe user said: \"我们应该按照模块来进行，那个是开始的函数，那个是结束的函数，开始的函数都有什么参数，结束后的都返回什么\" — they want entry/exit coverage per module. The existing LLM raw logs are complementary (mid-function detail), not redundant with entry/exit... partially overlapping though (e.g. filter_table's \"表字段过滤选择：%s\" IS the exit log).\n\nTwo paths:\n- **Path 1 (decorator everywhere + prune overlapping manual logs)**: consistent, but bigger diff, prunes logs user likes.\n- **Path 2 (add decorator only where entry/exit missing, keep existing)**: inconsistent — some nodes double-log.\n\nHmm. Actually, let me think about what's genuinely best and matches the user's taste (\"优雅\", \"不做没必要的抽离，只做公共函数的抽离\"):\n\nA single shared decorator IS the \"公共函数\" they'd accept. And to avoid double-logging, prune the manual logs that the decorator now covers (exit logs like \"表字段过滤选择\"), while KEEPING mid-function detail logs (LLM 原始返回 — those are NOT entry/exit). That gives:\n- Entry log (decorator): module received what\n- Exit log (decorator): module returned what\n- LLM raw logs (manual, keep): mid-call detail\n\nThat's clean layering: 节点边界 = decorator；节点内部的 LLM 原始返回 = 手写。The user explicitly wants both (they cited the LLM raw log as the exemplar AND asked for entry/exit).\n\nBut wait — decorator with per-node inputs/outputs config: the config for each node requires knowing which state keys each node reads/writes. I know most from the audit:\n- route_question: inputs=[input_text], outputs=[routing/analysis_mode...] — need to check return keys\n- extract_keywords: inputs=[input_text], outputs=[keywords] (returns AgentState? line 70 returns AgentState — need to check what keys)\n- retrieve_columns: inputs=[input_text, keywords], outputs=[column_recall_terms, column_candidates]\n- retrieve_tables: no LLM but has entry/exit? inputs=[keywords...], outputs=[table_candidates]\n- retrieve_metrics: inputs=[input_text, keywords], outputs=[metrics_recall_terms, metrics_candidates]\n- filter_metric: inputs=[input_text, metric_infos], outputs=[metric_selection]\n- filter_table: inputs=[input_text, table_infos], outputs=[table_selection]\n- retrieve_dimension_values: inputs=[input_text, keywords], outputs=[dimension_value_recall_terms, dimension_value_candidates]\n- merge_retrieved_info: inputs=[...candidates], outputs=[extra_context]\n- reconcile_filtered_context: inputs, outputs\n- generate_sql: inputs=[input_text, extra_context], outputs=[display_sql / sql...]\n- execute_sql: inputs=[sql...], outputs=[sql_result...]\n- enrich_query_result: inputs/outputs\n- plan_analysis: inputs=[input_text, analysis_goals], outputs=[analysis_plan]\n- execute_analysis: inputs=[analysis_plan...], outputs=[analysis_task_results...]\n- generate_report_plan: outputs=[report_plan]\n- render_report: outputs=[report...]\n- daily_chat: inputs=[input_text, messages], outputs=[output_text]\n\nI don't know all exact keys — I'd need to read each node's return statement. That's the remaining audit work. Files I've read: I know returns for filter_metric (metric_selection), filter_table (table_selection), retrieve_metrics (metrics_recall_terms, metrics_candidates), retrieve_columns (column_recall_terms, column_candidates), daily_chat (output_text, llm_output), extract_keywords (partial — returns AgentState? saw only up to line 99; return likely {\"keywords\": ...}), route_question (result dict written to writer; return unknown), plan_analysis (analysis_plan, output_text), generate_sql (partial).\n\nThis is getting big. Alternative lighter approach that still fully answers the ask WITHOUT touching every node's internals: a **generic decorator that logs the whole state diff**? No — noisy.\n\nHmm wait — actually, reconsider: maybe simpler and MORE aligned with \"优雅\": the decorator logs:\n- Entry: ALL state keys the node declares as inputs — still needs config.\n\nOR: entry logs a compact signature: question/keywords etc. — config needed regardless.\n\nOR — radically simpler: decorator logs `state.keys()` + sizes at entry, and return dict keys + sizes at exit? \"收到 8 个","startTime":1791428023744,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023744}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789628927901},{"id":"5fe3fd77-3c36-47c9-a493-15b9a98d020a","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"能理解我的意思吗，可以先给我方案","payload":{"query":"能理解我的意思吗，可以先给我方案","rawMessage":"能理解我的意思吗，可以先给我方案","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"interrupt","clientRequestId":"42700c3d-143f-401a-b9b6-692cc48bcfab","requestedAt":1789628926170,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact