raps execution; tool.completed/tool.failed emitted by runtime after tool returns? I have enough).\n\nPlan:\n1. Create tasks for doc chapters (ch2, ch3, ch4, part2) — actually keep it light: one task per chapter + part 2 later. Create 3 tasks (ch2, ch3, ch4)? Part 2 module summaries are \"second stage\" — can add later. I'll create tasks: 撰写第2章主干, 撰写第3章, 撰写第4章. Mark ch2 in_progress.\n\nHmm, the task system reminder said tasks exist from prior work (all completed). Creating 3 new tasks is reasonable.\n\n2. Launch 4 Explore agents in parallel (single message, multiple Agent calls).\n3. When results come back, write chapter 2.\n4. Reply to user with reading route + what I did.\n\nActually the response flow: I should first give the reading route in my reply, and launch agents in the same turn. The agents run, then I continue writing. Since agent results arrive as tool results, I'll then write the doc and finish the reply.\n\nLet me write the agent prompts carefully — they must return raw structured data with file:line.\n\nOne more thing: the user's reading route should mention reading alongside the doc and how we collaborate: \"你按路线读，读到哪一章发现文档与代码不符，直接标出来我来改\" — good collaboration model.\n\nAlso mention: 用一次真实 run 的「全部事件」tab 作为对照材料 (trace 已落库，可回放).\n\nNow compose the reply structure:\n1. 主线阅读路线 (7 steps, files + focus, mapped to doc sections)\n2. 阅读方法 3 条 (对照状态图; grep _emit 索引; 真实 run 全部事件对照)\n3. 分工: 你读, 我写 — 我现在开始写第 2 章\n4. Launch agents.\n\nThen after agents return, write ch2 into doc, update tasks, and summarize.\n\nAgent prompts (must be self-contained):\n\nAgent A (Explore, medium):\n\"Research task (read-only, no code changes). File: /Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/api/routers/harness.py. Extract for documentation, each with exact file:line:\n1. The POST endpoint that starts a harness run: exact route path, HTTP method, request model name + its fields, response model/type.\n2. How the run is initialized before calling LoopController.start: S