ter.custom()`. `context_engine/` and `planning_agent/` contain zero event-emission code (grep for `emit|event_writer|HarnessEvent` returns nothing in both).\n\n## 1. Shared writer API — app/agent/streaming/writer.py\n\nFile: /Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/streaming/writer.py\n\n`HarnessEventWriter` (L75-87): holds `run_ref`, `sink` (a `HarnessEventSink`; production sink is `QueueEventSink` L62-72, which appends to a list and `queue.put_nowait(event)` — non-blocking, same event loop as SSE), and a per-run `ContextVar[dict]` `self._context` (L85-87) used as the bound-context fallback.\n\n`emit()` (L89-121):\n- Signature: `emit(event_type, *, source=None, phase=None, iteration=None, action_id=None, payload=None) -> HarnessEvent`.\n- ContextVar fallback (L100-108): `context = self._context.get()`; `effective_source = source or context.get(\"source\") or \"harness\"` (L101); `effective_phase = phase or context.get(\"phase\") or \"start_run\"` (L102); `effective_iteration = iteration if not None else context.get(\"iteration\", 0)` (L103-105); `effective_action_id = action_id if not None else context.get(\"action_id\")` (L106-108).\n- Builds `HarnessEvent` (contract: /Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/streaming/contracts.py L13-24 — fields `event_id, event_type, run_ref, phase, iteration, action_id, source, timestamp, payload`), `event_id=str(uuid4())`, `timestamp=now(UTC)` (L109-119).\n- Payload is run through `_sanitize()` (L118; sanitizer defined L41-59: depth > 3 → `str(value)[:500]`, strings truncated to 2000, dicts capped at 64 keys, lists at 32 items, and `_DROP_KEYS` fields dropped — L18-37 drops `rows, sql_result, display_rows, display_sql_result, sql, query, python_code, code, analysis_plan, analysis_task_results, analysis_evidence, calculation_result, result, output, messages, prompt, reasoning, content`).\n- Publishes via `self.sink.publish(event)` (L120).\n\n`custom()` (L123-137):\n- Purpose (docstring L124): normalizes LangGraph `custom` stream events into the frontend-stable `tool.progress` type.\n- `custom_type = str(value.pop(\"type\", \"progress\"))` (L126) — the incoming `type` key is popped and forced into `payload[\"custom_type\"]`; the event_type is always the literal `\"tool.progress\"` (L131). `node = str(value.get(\"node\", \"tool\"))` (L127); `source = f\"{context.get('source', 'tool')}:{node}\"` (L129) — so source is `\"<bound source>:<node>\"`, e.g. `query_data:filter_table`.\n- Delegates to `emit(\"tool.progress\", source=source, payload={\"custom_type\": custom_type, **value})` (L130-137). No phase/iteration/action_id args — those come only from the ContextVar binding (or defaults: phase `\"start_run\"`, iteration 0, action_id None) unless the caller is inside `bind()`.\n\n`bind()` (L139-162): contextmanager that merges `source/phase/iteration/action_id` into the ContextVar dict, sets token, resets in `finally`.\n\n`NullHarnessEventWriter` (L165-169) + `_NullEventSink` (L172-174): no-op sink for non-streaming runs.\n\n`format_sse` (L182-185): SSE frame `id/event/data` from `event.model_dump(mode=\"json\")`.\n\n## 2. loop_controller module\n\nFile: /Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/loop_controller/controller.py\n\nWriter API used by every event below: `self._emit(...)` → L1138-1163, which resolves `writer = self.event_writer or NullHarnessEventWriter(run_ref=run_ref)` (L1149) and calls `writer.emit(event_type, phase=phase.value, iteration=iteration, action_id=action_id, payload=payload)` (L1151-1157), swallowing and logging exceptions (L1158-1163). It never uses `.custom()` and never touches the sink directly. The `phase=` argument is a `LoopPhase` enum serialized to its string value (enum: /Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/state_result_store/contracts.py L23-33).\n\n| Event | file:line (emit call / string) | Method | phase | payload | Fires when |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `context.started` | L847-852 (str @849) | `_build_context` | current `LoopPhase` from state (normally `build_context`) | none (empty `{}`) | Unconditionally at the top of `_build_context`, before `context_request_factory.create` (L854) and `context_builder.build` (L859). |\n| `context.failed` | L862-868 (str @864) | `_build_context` | same phase | `{\"error_code\": \"context_build_failed\"}` | Bare `except Exception` (L860) around request creation + build; comment L861: context is the only phase that can be `started` without a terminal event, so this pairs the lifecycle. Exception is re-raised (L869). |\n| `context.memory_retrieved` | L886-902 (str @888) | `_build_context` | same phase | `{\"selected_count\": memory_count, \"source_counts\": {semantic, episodic, perceptual}}` | After successful build; counted from `compiled_context.trace.decisions` where `decision.selected` (L873-884): `memory_count` = sum of SEMANTIC+EPISODIC+PERCEPTUAL selected counts. |\n| `context.knowledge_retrieved` | L903-912 (str @905) | `_build_context` | same phase | `{\"selected_count\": knowledge_count, \"evidence_count\": len(sections.external_evidence)}` | Same success path, immediately after memory_retrieved; `knowledge_count = selected_by_kind[ContextSourceKind.RAG.value]` (L885). |\n| `context.context_compiled` | L914-920 (str @916) | `_build_context` | same phase | snapshot dict from `_context_snapshot` (L944-984): `build_id`, `token_count`, `resolved_asset_ids`, `model_messages` (`[{role, text}]`), `sections` (`conversation_summary, known_facts, prior_work, attachments, external_evidence, unresolved_references`), `trace` (`candidate_count, selected_count, final_token_count, summary_updated, reference_resolution{asset_ids, historical_asset_ids, needs_working_context, unresolved_references}`) | Always on the success path, after the two retrieval events, before `context.completed`. |\n| `context.completed` | L921-926 (str @923) | `_build_context` | same phase | none | End of successful `_build_context`, right before the structured `logger.info` (L927-941). |\n| `planner.started` | L745-751 (str @747) | `_plan_action` | `plan` | `{\"action_seq\": action_seq}` where `action_seq = harness.action_seq + 1` (L744) | Start of every planner invocation, before `self.planning_agent.plan(...)` (L753). |\n| `planner.completed` | L786-800 (str @788) | `_plan_action` | `plan` | `{\"action_seq\": action.action_seq, \"action_type\": action.action_type.value, \"tool_name\": action.tool_call.tool_name or None}` | `plan()` returned without raising. (Adjacent, not requested: `planner.failed` emitted at L762-772 with `{action_seq, error_code: exc.error.code, retryable}` for `PlannerFailure`, and L775-784 with `{action_seq, error_code: \"planner_unexpected_error\"}` for any other `Exception`; both re-raise.) |\n| `planner.retrying` | L618-627 (str @620) | `_handle_planner_failure` | `plan` | `{\"retry_count\": harness.planner_retry_count (already incremented), \"error_code\": failure.error.code}` | Condition L612: `failure.error.retryable and retry_count < self.max_planner_retries`; state re-saved as RUNNING/PLAN first (L614-617), returns True (retry). If not retryable or retries exhausted, returns False with no event. |\n| `action.committed` | L826-841 (str @828) | `_commit_action` | `validate_action` | `{\"action_seq\": action.action_seq, \"action_type\": action.action_type.value, \"commit_status\": commit.status}`; `action_id=action.tool_call.action_id or None` (L831-835) | After `action_committer.commit` (L807-820) passes the guards: `commit.status in {\"committed\", \"idempotent\"}` (L821) and `commit.action_seq == action.action_seq` (L823), and after `state[\"harness\"][\"action_seq\"]` is updated (L825). |\n\nAdjacent, same module (not in the requested list, same `_emit` API): `tool.retrying` at L690-701 (str @692), phase `execute_tool`, payload `{\"tool_name\", \"attempt\": retry_count + 2, \"error_code\": result.error_code}`, fired in `_execute_tool`'s retry loop when