alization_service.finalize(...) → ledger stages (history_saved → checkpoint_saved → released → formation_submitted → completed)\n3. `self._emit_terminal(...)` — AFTER finalize returns (i.e., after all ledger stages, after run persisted as terminal)\n4. return LoopRunResult\n\nThen in the API layer `_sse_response.run_operation` (harness.py lines 487-500), after `operation()` returns, it emits \"run.result\" with the serialized loop_result payload. So ordering: ledger stages → run.completed (terminal event, in controller._emit_terminal) → run.result (SSE final envelope event, in the router). Both emitted after the ledger reaches \"completed\" and after the run state was saved as terminal in the checkpoint_saved stage.\n\nLet me verify the router prefix and the HarnessReconcileRequest model, plus check `_serialize_result`. Also let me confirm where \"run.completed\" events go through writer — HarnessEventWriter and event sink. Not strictly needed, but the router prefix is needed for \"which API endpoint exposes reconcile\".\n\nAlso I should double check the memory formation submit: `formation_run_id` — and that \"completed\" stage increments attempts. Yes, in advance() line 136-137.\n\nAlso confirm what `_require_finalizable` does — already read.\n\nAlso let me quickly check the `HarnessEventWriter`/`emit` — not needed deeply.\n\nLet me read the top of harness.py (router prefix) and the HarnessReconcileRequest definition.","startTime":1791428023747,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023747},{"id":"call_81a942a52ca549299f1c2824","type":"TOOL","toolName":"grep_content","params":{"-A":"6","-n":"true","output_mode":"content","path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/api/routers/harness.py","pattern":"router = APIRouter|class HarnessReconcileRequest|def _serialize_result"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Found 3 matches\n\n/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/api/routers/harness.py:\n  Line 88: router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/harnes