E_ORDER = (\"prepared\", \"history_saved\", \"checkpoint_saved\", \"released\", \"formation_submitted\", \"completed\")\n```\n`stage_rank()` at lines 38-43 rejects unknown stages.\n\nStages as implemented in `PostgresFinalizationService._drive` (app/agent/finalization/service.py@LINE[85..144]):\n\n- `prepared` — ledger row created & content locked by `PostgresFinalizationLedger.prepare()` (finalization_repository.py@LINE[57..92]); called from `PostgresFinalizationService.finalize()` service.py@LINE[63..68]. Digest computed by `_digest` (service.py@LINE[229..235], SHA-256 of canonical FinalizationInput JSON).\n- `history_saved` — `await self._save_history(value)` then `ledger.advance(stage=\"history_saved\")`. `_save_history` service.py@LINE[146..161] calls `ConversationRepository.finish_turn(...)` writing assistant message + turn output; `_final_output` (service.py@LINE[163..182]) resolves structured output from artifact store by reference, or returns (\"text\", {\"message\": final_answer}).\n- `checkpoint_saved` — `state[\"harness\"] = transition_harness_state(state[\"harness\"], status=terminal_status, phase=LoopPhase.FINALIZATION, terminal_intent=...)`; `run_store.save(...)`; then advance to \"checkpoint_saved\". service.py@LINE[98..108]. This is the actual terminal-state commit of the run.\n- `released` — `conversation_repository.release_active_run(conversation_id, user_id, run_id, status)`; raises RuntimeError if conversation missing (\"会话不存在，无法释放 active_run\") service.py@LINE[109..120]. Releases the conversation's active_run slot.\n- `formation_submitted` — `_submit_formation(value)` service.py@LINE[184..206]: only if memory_formation_service configured AND terminal_status is COMPLETED; submits `TurnMemoryInput` to MemoryFormationService, returns formation_run_id (None otherwise); advance stores formation_run_id in ledger. service.py@LINE[121..128].\n- `completed` — pure ledger advance, marks ledger complete; `advance()` increments `attempts` when stage == \"completed\" (finalization_repository.py@LINE[136..137]). service.py@LINE[129..132].\n\nGuard for each stage: `self._before(model, stage)` = `stage_rank(model.stage) < stage_rank(stage)` (service.py@LINE[224..227]) — makes stages skippable if already passed (idempotent resume).\n\n**2. Failure semantics**\n\n- Any exception inside `_drive`'s try block is re-raised as `FinalizationFailure(value.run_ref, model.stage) from exc` — service.py@LINE[133..134]. `FinalizationFailure` defined app/agent/finalization/errors.py@LINE[8..14], carrying `run_ref` and `stage`.\n- Ledger state left behind: stays at the last successfully advanced stage (the stage whose op completed); the failing stage is NOT recorded in the ledger (stage only advances after the op succeeds). Run state left behind: run remains `running` + `phase=finalization` + `terminal_intent=<target>` (set by controller._finalize before calling finalize, controller.py@LINE[1017..1024]); the run status is NOT flipped to terminal because `checkpoint_saved` didn't happen or happened earlier. So a failure after checkpoint_saved leaves status=terminal, phase=finalization; failure before leaves running/finalization with terminal_intent.\n- In the controller, `_run_guarded` re-raises FinalizationFailure without degrading to FAILED (controller.py@LINE[228..231]) — comment: degrading would fabricate a terminal state the user never saw.\n- In the API, `_http_error` maps FinalizationFailure → HTTP 503 with the message (harness.py@LINE[375..377]).\n- Also, `_finish_unhandled_start_failure` (harness.py@LINE[389..466]) checks `PostgresFinalizationLedger.get(...)`: if a ledger row exists, it does NOT fabricate a FAILED terminal (lines 412..420).\n- Ledger content conflicts: `FinalizationLedgerError` and `FinalizationDigestConflict` (finalization_repository.py@LINE[20..25]) raised in `prepare` when a second finalize attempt for the same run uses different content (digest mismatch) — lines 80..92.\n- `last_error` JSONB column exists on the ledger (models/harness.py@LINE[268..269]) and `advance()` accepts a `last_error` param (repository@LINE[113..114, 134..135]) but `_drive` never passes it; last_error is written to the run's harness state by the controller for non-COMPLETED terminal statuses (FinalizationInput.error_message, controller.py@LINE[1039..1043]).\n\n**3. reconcile()**\n\n- `PostgresFinalizationService.reconcile(run_id, user_id)` service.py@LINE[70..83]: loads ledger row via `ledger.get` (raises FinalizationLedgerError if none); rebuilds `FinalizationInput.model_validate(model.input_payload)` from the locked JSON; `ledger.mark_reconcile_attempt` increments `attempts` (repository@LINE[141..154]); reloads run state via `run_store.load(value.run_ref)`; then `_drive(...)` replays from current stage.\n- Exposed at HTTP `POST /harness/run/reconcile` — app/api/routers/harness.py@LINE[833..852] (`reconcile_harness`, router prefix \"/harness\" at line 88; request model HarnessReconcileRequest {run_id, user_id} at lines 117..121). It constructs a fresh PostgresFinalizationService with ledger/run_store/conversation repo/memory formation/artifact store and returns `result.model_dump(mode=\"json\")`. Errors mapped via `_http_error` (503 for FinalizationFailure).\n\n**4. Event ordering vs ledger stages**\n\n- Inside `_drive`, ledger stages run first with NO events emitted.\n- After `finalize()` returns (i.e., after the ledger reaches \"completed\" and the run row has been saved in terminal status at checkpoint_saved), `controller._finalize` calls `self._emit_terminal(command.run_ref, finalization)` — controller.py@LINE[1049..1057]; `_emit_terminal` (controller.py@LINE[1108..1136]) maps COMPLETED→\"run.completed\", FAILED→\"run.failed\", TIMEOUT→\"run.timeout\", CANCELLED→\"run.cancelled\" and emits with phase=finalization, payload {status, final_answer, final_output_type, final_output_ref, error_code}. Docstring line 1113: \"只在终态已成功持久化后发布一次本次控制器实例的终态事件\" — events strictly AFTER ledger completion.\n- `_emit` (controller.py@LINE[1138..1163]) swallows writer exceptions (event failure doesn't change persisted result).\n- Then \"run.result\" is emitted by the API layer after the whole operation returns: `_sse_response.run_operation` harness.py@LINE[487..500] emits \"run.result\" with payload {\"loop_result\": _serialize_result(result)} (model_dump of LoopResult). So ordering: ledger stages → run.completed → run.result. Both after terminal persistence.\n\n**5. LoopResult shape on success & harness state at terminal time**\n\n- `LoopResult = LoopRunResult | LoopPausedResult | LoopResumeAcceptedResult` (contracts.py@LINE[146]).\n- Normal COMPLETED path returns `LoopRunResult` (contracts.py@LINE[89..107]): fields run_ref: HarnessRunRef, status: HarnessStatus, phase: LoopPhase (must be FINALIZATION), iteration: int, finalization_result: FinalizationResult, last_error: RunError|None. Validators: phase must be finalization; run_refs equal; statuses equal.\n- Constructed in controller._finalize at lines 1050..1057.\n- `FinalizationResult` (contracts.py@LINE[66..86]): run_ref, status, final_answer, final_output_type (default \"text\"), final_output_ref, iteration, last_error; validator requires terminal status ∈ {COMPLETED, FAILED, CANCELLED, TIMEOUT}. Built in service._drive at service.py@LINE[135..144] (iteration/last_error read from HarnessStateSnapshot of the post-checkpoint state).\n- HarnessControlState fields (state_result_store/state.py@LINE[13..46]) — relevant terminal-time fields:\n  - `final_answer` written by controller._finalize BEFORE finalize: state[\"harness\"][\"final_answer\"] = final_answer (controller.py@LINE[1017]).\n  - controller._finalize transitions state to status=RUNNING, phase=FINALIZATION, terminal_intent=terminal_status.value and saves it (controller.py@LINE[1018..1024]) — this is the \"recoverable\" pre-finalize fieldset.\n  - Inside the service checkpoint_saved stage: transition_harness_state(status=terminal_status, phase=FINALIZATION, terminal_intent=...) — writes `status` (terminal), keeps `phase=finalization`, `terminal_intent`, and bumps `state_version` (state.py@LINE[177..186]); run_store.save persists.\n  - `transition_harness_state` only writes status/phase/terminal_intent/state_version (+ clears pending_confirmation when going from WAITING_CONFIRMATION→RUNNING). There is NO `finished_at` in harness state — timestamps on harness state are only `started_at` and `deadline_at` (state.py@LINE[28..29]). `finished_at` exists only on `ToolResult` (contracts.py@LINE[387..388]), and turn `completed_at` is set by ConversationRepository.finish_turn (repositories/conversation_repository.py@LINE[291]) during the history_saved ledger stage.\n  - Terminal-state invariants validated by HarnessStateSnapshot.validate_combination (contracts.py@LINE[285..316]): terminal status requires phase=finalization, terminal_intent == status.value, pending_confirmation must be None.\n  - `last_error`: for non-COMPLETED terminal statuses the controller passes error_message into FinalizationInput from state[\"harness\"][\"last_error\"].message (controller.py@LINE[1039..1043]); last_error in harness state is set earlier by _set_interruption_state etc. For COMPLETED, error_message is \"\".\n\n**6. HarnessFinalizationModel / harness_finalizations table**\n\n- app/models/harness.py@LINE[227..277]. `__tablename__ = \"harness_finalizations\"` (line 234). Index idx_harness_finalizations_user_stage on (user_id, stage) (line 236). Comment \"Data Agent Harness 收口账本\" (line 237).\n- Columns:\n  - run_id: String(128), PK, FK→harness_runs.run_id ON DELETE CASCADE (lines 241..245) — one finalization per run\n  - user_id: String(128), not null (247)\n  - conversation_id: String(128), not null (249)\n  - turn_id: String(128), not null (251)\n  - finalization_digest: String(64), not null (253) — SHA-256 digest; same-run re-finalization must match\n  - terminal_status: String(32), not null (255) — completed/failed/cancelled/timeout\n  - stage: String(32), not null (257) — prepared/history_saved/checkpoint_saved/released/formation_submitted/completed\n  - final_answer: Text, not null (259)\n  - error_message: Text, not null, default \"\" (261)\n  - input_payload: JSONB, not null, default {} (263) — full FinalizationInput JSON for reconcile\n  - formation_run_id: String(64), nullable (265)\n  - attempts: Integer, not null, default 0 (267) — reconcile replays (+1 per completed stage advance)\n  - last_error: JSONB, nullable (269)\n  - created_at: DateTime, not null, default utcnow (271..273)\n  - updated_at: DateTime, not null, default utcnow, onupdate (275..277)\n\nAlso the callsites of the normal COMPLETED path: `_run` loop, when action_type is FINAL_ANSWER and action committed → `_finalize(...)` without terminal_status → default COMPLETED (controller.py@LINE[422..428]); also without action_committer at lines 378..384. And resume rejection path → CANCELLED (174..180), timeout (198..204), cancelled (213..221), unexpected exception → FAILED (240..246).\n\nDigest: `_digest` service.py@LINE[229..235] sha256 of json.dumps(value.model_dump(mode=\"json\"), ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True).\n\nWhere's finalize called from resume for rejected confirmation: CANCELLED.\n\nNow compose the final answer with file:line references. Use absolute paths. The user asked \"Return raw structured data with file:line. Your final message IS the return value.\" — respond in English (query is English).","startTime":1791428023747,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023747},{"id":"308e6422-b5e1-44ac-b8aa-4ac301ea2b86","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"# Finalization Pipeline Research — Data Agent Harness\n\n## 1. Fixed stage order of the finalization ledger\n\nStage order is defined in `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/repositories/finalization_repository.py@LINE[28..35]`:\n\n```python\n_STAGE_ORDER = (\n    \"prepared\", \"history_saved\", \"checkpoint_saved\",\n    \"released\", \"formation_submitted\", \"completed\",\n)\n```\n`stage_rank()` at `finalization_repository.py@LINE[38..43]` rejects unknown stages.\n\nExecution lives in `PostgresFinalizationService._drive()` — `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/finalization/service.py@LINE[85..144]`. Each stage runs only if `self._before(model, stage)` (`service.py@LINE[224..227]`, i.e. `stage_rank(model.stage) < stage_rank(stage)`), then `ledger.advance(...)` moves the row forward exactly +1 (enforced in `advance()`, `finalization_repository.py@LINE[127..130]`).\n\n| # | Stage | What it does | Implementing method | file:line |\n|---|-------|--------------|---------------------|-----------|\n| 0 | `prepared` | Ledger row created; finalization content locked (digest + full `input_payload` JSON) | `PostgresFinalizationLedger.prepare()` ← `finalize()` | `finalization_repository.py@LINE[57..92]`; called `service.py@LINE[63..68]` |\n| 1 | `history_saved` | Writes assistant message + turn output via `ConversationRepository.finish_turn(...)`; resolves structured output by reference via `ArtifactStore.read()` or falls back to `(\"text\", {\"message\": final_answer})`; raises `RuntimeError` if save fails | `_save_history()` + `_final_output()` | `service.py@LINE[93..97, 146..161, 163..182]` |\n| 2 | `checkpoint_saved` | Commits terminal run state: `transition_harness_state(status=terminal_status, phase=FINALIZATION, terminal_intent=...)` then `run_store.save(...)` — the actual terminal-state persistence of the run | inline in `_drive` | `service.py@LINE[98..108]` |\n| 3 | `released` | `ConversationRepository.release_active_run(conversation_id, user_id, run_id, status)`; raises `RuntimeError(\"会话不存在，无法释放 active_run\")` if not released | inline in `_drive` | `service.py@LINE[109..120]` |\n| 4 | `formation_submitted` | `_submit_formation()`: only if `memory_formation_service` configured AND `terminal_status is HarnessStatus.COMPLETED`; submits `TurnMemoryInput` to `MemoryFormationService`, stores returned `formation_run_id` in ledger (else `None`) | `_submit_formation()` | `service.py@LINE[121..128, 184..206]` |\n| 5 | `completed` | Pure ledger advance to terminal ledger stage; `advance()` increments `attempts` when `stage == \"completed\"` | inline in `_drive` | `service.py@LINE[129..132]`; `finalization_repository.py@LINE[136..137]` |\n\nDigest locking: `_digest()` = SHA-256 of `json.dumps(FinalizationInput.model_dump(mode=\"json\"), ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True)` — `service.py@LINE[229..235]`.\n\n## 2. Failure of a stage\n\n- Any exception inside `_drive`'s try-block is re-raised as `FinalizationFailure(value.run_ref, model.stage) from exc` — `service.py@LINE[133..134]`. `FinalizationFailure` is defined at `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/finalization/errors.py@LINE[8..14]` carrying `run_ref` and `stage`.\n- Ledger left behind: stays at the last successfully advanced stage (stage only advances AFTER its operation succeeds — the failing stage is never recorded). Run left behind: `running` + `phase=finalization` + `terminal_intent=<target>` (written by the controller before calling finalize, `controller.py@LINE[1017..1024]`); if failure occurred after `checkpoint_saved`, run is already terminal. No downgrade/second terminal commit is attempted: `controller.py@LINE[1030..1031]` comment.\n- Controller explicitly re-raises `FinalizationFailure` instead of converting to FAILED: `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/loop_controller/controller.py@LINE[228..231]`.\n- API maps it to HTTP 503: `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/api/routers/harness.py@LINE[375..377]`.\n- The unhandled-failure cleanup path refuses to fabricate a FAILED terminal if a ledger row exists (result ownership is locked): `harness.py@LINE[412..420]`.\n- Content conflicts: `FinalizationLedgerError` / `FinalizationDigestConflict` (`finalization_repository.py@LINE[20..25]`) raised in `prepare()` on IntegrityError → re-read → digest mismatch (`finalization_repository.py@LINE[80..92]`).\n- Note: `HarnessFinalizationModel.last_error` column and `advance(last_error=...)` param exist (`models/harness.py@LINE[268..269]`, `finalization_repository.py@LINE[113, 134..135]`) but `_drive` never passes it.\n\n## 3. reconcile()\n\n- `PostgresFinalizationService.reconcile(*, run_id, user_id)` — `service.py@LINE[70..83]`: `ledger.get()` (raises `FinalizationLedgerError` if no row) → rebuilds `FinalizationInput.model_validate(model.input_payload)` from the locked JSON → `ledger.mark_reconcile_attempt()` increments `attempts` (`finalization_repository.py@LINE[141..154]`) → `run_store.load(value.run_ref)` → `_drive(...)` replays from current stage. Never returns to Planner or tools (input comes from `input_payload`).\n- HTTP exposure: `POST /harness/run/reconcile` — `reconcile_harness()`, `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/api/routers/harness.py@LINE[833..852]` (router prefix `\"/harness\"` at `harness.py@LINE[88]`; request model `HarnessReconcizeRequest{run_id, user_id}` at `harness.py@LINE[117..121]`). Builds a fresh `PostgresFinalizationService` and returns `result.model_dump(mode=\"json\")`.\n\n## 4. Event ordering vs ledger stages\n\nEvents are emitted AFTER finalize completes — never inside it:\n1. Ledger stages run to `completed` (run already persisted terminal at `checkpoint_saved`).\n2. `controller._finalize` then calls `self._emit_terminal(...)` — `controller.py@LINE[1049]`; `_emit_terminal` at `controller.py@LINE[1108..1136]` maps `COMPLETED→\"run.completed\"`, `FAILED→\"run.failed\"`, `TIMEOUT→\"run.timeout\"`, `CANCELLED→\"run.cancelled\"` with `phase=finalization` and payload `{status, final_answer, final_output_type, final_output_ref, error_code}`. Docstring `controller.py@LINE[1113]`: “只在终态已成功持久化后发布一次…终态事件”.\n3. `_emit` (`controller.py@LINE[1138..1163]`) swallows writer exceptions — event failure does not alter the persisted result.\n4. `\"run.result\"` is emitted by the API SSE layer after the whole `operation()` returns: `harness.py@LINE[487..500]`, payload `{\"loop_result\": _serialize_result(result)}` (`_serialize_result` = `LoopResult.model_dump`, `harness.py@LINE[344..346]`).\n\nOrder: ledger stages → `run.completed` → `run.result`.\n\n## 5. Success result shape and terminal-time `state[\"harness\"]` fields\n\n- `LoopResult = LoopRunResult | LoopPausedResult | LoopResumeAcceptedResult` — `app/agent/loop_controller/contracts.py@LINE[146]`. Normal COMPLETED path returns `LoopRunResult` (`contracts.py@LINE[89..107]`, constructed `controller.py@LINE[1050..1057]`): fields `run_ref: HarnessRunRef`, `status: HarnessStatus`, `phase: LoopPhase` (must be `FINALIZATION`), `iteration: int`, `finalization_result: FinalizationResult`, `last_error: RunError | None`; validators require equal run_ref/status between the two results.\n- `FinalizationResult` (`contracts.py@LINE[66..86]`, built `service.py@LINE[135..144]`): `run_ref`, `status`, `final_answer`, `final_output_type` (default `\"text\"`), `final_output_ref`, `iteration`, `last_error` — status must be terminal (`contracts.py@LINE[77..86]`).\n- Terminal-time writes to `state[\"harness\"]` (schema: `HarnessControlState`, `/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/state_result_store/state.py@LINE[13..46]`):\n  - `final_answer = final_answer` — `controller.py@LINE[1017]` (before finalize).\n  - Transition #1 (pre-finalize, saved): `status=running`, `phase=finalization`, `terminal_intent=<target>`, `state_version+1` — `controller.py@LINE[1018..1024]`.\n  - Transition #2 (inside `checkpoint_saved` stage): `status=<terminal>` (e.g. `completed`), `phase=finalization`, `terminal_intent`, `state_version+1`; `pending_confirmation` cleared only on WAITING_CONFIRMATION→RUNNING — `service.py@LINE[98..105]`, `state.py@LINE[177..186]`.\n  - There is NO `finished_at` in harness state; only `started_at` / `deadline_at` exist (`state.py@LINE[28..29]`). `finished_at` belongs to `ToolResult` only (`state_result_store/contracts.py@LINE[387..388]`); turn timestamps are DB-side (`completed_at` set by `finish_turn`, `app/repositories/conversation_repository.py@LINE[291]`).\n  - Invariants enforced by `HarnessStateSnapshot.validate_combination` (`state_result_store/contracts.py@LINE[285..316]`): terminal requires `phase=finalization`, `terminal_intent == status.value`, `pending_confirmation is None`.\n  - `last_error`: for non-COMPLETED statuses the controller copies `state[\"harness\"][\"last_error\"].message` into `FinalizationInput.error_message` (`controller.py@LINE[1039..1043]`); empty string for COMPLETED.\n- Normal COMPLETED callsite: planner emits `FINAL_ANSWER` → action committed → `_finalize(...)` with default `terminal_status=COMPLETED` — `controller.py@LINE[422..428]` (no-committer variant `controller.py@LINE[378..384]`). Other paths: CANCELLED on rejected confirmation (`controller.py@LINE[173..180]`), TIMEOUT on deadline (`controller.py@LINE[198..204]`), CANCELLED on client disconnect via shielded task (`controller.py@LINE[205..227]`), FAILED on unexpected exceptions (`controller.py@LINE[240..246]`).\n\n## 6. HarnessFinalizationModel / `harness_finalizations` table\n\n`/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/models/harness.py@LINE[227..277]`; `__tablename__ = \"harness_finalizations\"` @LINE[234]; index `idx_harness_finalizations_user_stage (user_id, stage)` @LINE[236].\n\nColumns:\n- `run_id` String(128) PK, FK→`harness_runs.run_id` ON DELETE CASCADE — one finalization per run @LINE[241..245]\n- `user_id` String(128) NOT NULL @LINE[247]\n- `conversation_id` String(128) NOT NULL @LINE[249]\n- `turn_id` String(128) NOT NULL @LINE[251]\n- `finalization_digest` String(64) NOT NULL — re-finalization must match @LINE[253]\n- `terminal_status` String(32) NOT NULL (completed/failed/cancelled/timeout) @LINE[255]\n- `stage` String(32) NOT NULL (the 6 stages above) @LINE[257]\n- `final_answer` Text NOT NULL @LINE[259]\n- `error_message` Text NOT NULL default \"\" @LINE[261]\n- `input_payload` JSONB NOT NULL default {} — full `FinalizationInput` for reconcile rebuild @LINE[263]\n- `formation_run_id` String(64) NULL — memory formation audit ID @LINE[265]\n- `attempts` Integer NOT NULL default 0 — reconcile replays (+1 per `completed` advance and per `mark_reconcile_attempt`) @LINE[267]\n- `last_error` JSONB NULL @LINE[269]\n- `created_at` / `updated_at` DateTime NOT NULL @LINE[271..277]"}]}]}]},{"id":"6aab9d421ca25a5d6904f614","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":209788},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"6a37e39c-7a52-4167-9172-8df0b216bf6b","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Excellent. All four research agents returned rich data. Now I have everything to write §2. Let me synthesize:\n\n**§2.1 触发入口:**\n- Router prefix `/harness` (harness.py:88)\n- `POST /harness/run` (non-stream, harness.py:595-596) and `POST /harness/run/stream` (harness.py:652-653) — frontend uses stream\n- Request model `HarnessRunRequest` (harness.py:92-103): input_text (1..20000), user_id (default settings.app.default_user_id), conversation_id (optional), asset_ids (max 32)\n- conversation_id defaults to uuid4; asset_ids dedup\n- run_ref built at harness.py:659-665: user_id, conversation_id, thread_id=conversation_id, turn_id=uuid4, run_id=uuid4\n- StartRunCommand at harness.py:699-704\n- active_run mutex: ConversationRepository.start_turn locks conversation row with_for_update, raises ValueError \"当前会话已有未完成的 Harness 运行\" if active_run_id not in (None, run_id) — conversation_repository.py:156-175 (check 174-175), set at 211; called from router harness.py:689-696\n- deadline_at computed in controller _new_state (controller.py:1087-1094) from run_timeout_seconds (settings.harness.* passed at harness.py:317-320)\n- _require_runtime precheck harness.py:124-135\n- SSE: queue + QueueEventSink (harness.py:671-672, writer.py:62-72), writer HarnessEventWriter (673), _sse_response (469-584): heartbeat settings.harness.sse_heartbeat_seconds (481-485), run_operation awaits operation() then emits run.result (490-500), on failure stream.failed (516-524), finally saves trace (526-542) and done marker (543); controller task create_task (545); body() iterator with wait_for queue.get timeout heartbeat → \": heartbeat\" SSE comment (551-556), done marker break, format_sse frames (560), client disconnect cancels task + shield (561-569)\n\n**§2.2 事件序列** (normal completion):\n1. run.started — controller.py:123-128, phase=start_run, iteration=0, no payload\n2. context.started — 847-852\n3. context.memory_retrieved — 886-902, payload selected_count + source_counts{semantic,episodic,perceptual}\n4. context.knowledge_retrieved — 903-912, payload selected_count + evidence_count\n5. context.context_compiled — 914-920, payload snapshot (build_id, token_count, resolved_asset_ids, model_messages, sections, trace)\n6. context.completed — 921-926\n7. planner.started — 745-751, payload {action_seq}\n8. planner.completed — 786-800, payload {action_seq, action_type, tool_name}\n9. action.committed — 826-841, payload {action_seq, action_type, commit_status}, action_id\n10. tool.started — runtime.py:72-79, payload {tool_name, attempt}, source=spec.name\n11. tool.progress — via writer.custom (writer.py:123-137), payload {custom_type, ...}, source=\"tool:node\"\n12. tool.completed / tool.failed — runtime.py:197-263 (_publish_result at 209-223), payload {tool_name, status, duration_ms, result_ref, error_code, row_count}\n13. (loop) repeat 2-9 with iteration+1\n14. final pass planner.completed action_type=final_answer → _finalize\n15. run.completed — _emit_terminal controller.py:1108-1136 (via 1049), phase=finalization, iteration=finalization.iteration, payload {status, final_answer, final_output_type, final_output_ref, error_code}\n16. run.result — router layer harness.py:490-500, payload {loop_result}\n\nOrder: ledger stages → run.completed → run.result.\n\nAlso note: tool.retrying (690-701) on the happy path CAN fire when idempotent tool has retryable TEMPORARY_ERROR within max_tool_retries — that's still part of \"normal\" path (transient). Mention it as optional branch. payload {tool_name, attempt: retry_count+2, error_code}, phase=execute_tool.\n\nAlso planner.retrying (618-627) — also fires on happy path when planner has retryable failure. payload {retry_count, error_code}, phase=plan.\n\nFrontend consumption for each event (from previous work): I know the frontend maps: run.started → 开始执行; context.* → 构建上下文 group; planner.* → 任务划分; action.committed → 提交动作; tool.started/progress/completed/failed → 执行工具; confirmation.* → 等待确认; run.completed/failed/timeout/cancelled → 终态; run.result → 最终回答. iteration drives round grouping. I can describe per-event consumption in the table.\n\n**§2.3 状态变化:**\n- transitions in _run: 336-338 BUILD_CONTEXT, 343-345 PLAN, 373-375 VALIDATE_ACTION, 451-453 EXECUTE_TOOL, 463-465 HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT, 507-509 RECORD_OBSERVATION, 521-523 BUILD_CONTEXT (下一轮), 528-530 PLAN\n- _finalize: 1018-1023 RUNNING/FINALIZATION + terminal_intent=\"completed\" (only transition carrying terminal_intent), save 1024\n- checkpoint_saved stage: transition #2 status=completed (service.py:98-108, state.py:177-186)\n- state fields per round: iteration += 1 at 510; action_seq updated at 825 (in _commit_action); planner_retry_count reset 369; last_error cleared 370-372; observations appended 482\n- state_version +1 per transition (state.py:182)\n- _save_running_state call sites: 339, 346, 376, 454, 466, 511, 524, 531 — persists whole HarnessGraphState via run_store.save\n\n**§2.4 涉及模块:**\n- 路由层 harness.py\n- LoopController (start/_run/_build_context/_plan_action/_commit_action/_execute_tool)\n- ContextEngine — note: context_engine/ has ZERO event emission; all context.* events emitted by controller._build_context (important as-built fact! SDD might suggest otherwise)\n- PlanningAgent — also zero event emission; planner.* emitted by controller._plan_action\n- ActionCommitter — commit guards: status committed/idempotent (821), action_seq match (823)\n- ToolRuntime — runtime.py: tool.started 72-79, bind 80-85, execution wait_for 86-88, _publish_result 197-263\n- FinalizationService — service.py\n- 前端 execution-panel\n\nKey as-built deviation note: 事件全部由 controller/runtime 层发出，ContextEngine 与 PlanningAgent 模块内部零事件代码 —— 这与\"节点自报事件\"的直觉相反，值得在文档里显式写出（保持模块纯净，事件集中在编排层）。\n\n**§2.5 收口方式:**\n- _finalize flow (controller.py:1006-1057): transition RUNNING/FINALIZATION + terminal_intent (1018-1023), save (1024), finalization_service.finalize(FinalizationInput) (1032-1048), _emit_terminal (1049), return LoopRunResult (1050-1057)\n- FinalizationInput: final_answer copied at 1017; error_message from last_error for non-COMPLETED (1039-1043)\n- Ledger six stages (finalization_repository.py:28-35): prepared → history_saved → checkpoint_saved → released → formation_submitted → completed\n  - prepared: ledger row created, digest lock (SHA-256 of FinalizationInput), finalization_repository.py:57-92, service.py:63-68\n  - history_saved: finish_turn writes assistant message + turn output; _final_output resolves RenderedReport artifact ref or fallback text (service.py:93-97, 146-182); RuntimeError if save fails\n  - checkpoint_saved: transition to terminal status + run_store.save (service.py:98-108)\n  - released: release_active_run (service.py:109-120; repo 330-361); RuntimeError if conversation missing\n  - formation_submitted: only if memory service configured AND COMPLETED; TurnMemoryInput → formation_run_id in ledger (121-128, 184-206)\n  - completed: pure advance; attempts incremented (129-132; repo 136-137)\n- each stage only runs if rank(current) < rank(stage) (224-227); advance moves +1 exactly (repo 127-130)\n- failure: wrapped FinalizationFailure(run_ref, stage) (133-134); ledger stays at last successful stage; run stays running/finalization + terminal_intent; controller re-raises (228-231); API maps 503 (harness.py:375-377); reconcile: POST /harness/run/reconcile (harness.py:833-852) → service.reconcile (service.py:70-83) rebuilds FinalizationInput from locked input_payload and _drive replays from current stage\n- event ordering: ledger → run.completed → run.result (router 487-500)\n- no finished_at in harness state; terminal invariant: terminal requires phase=finalization, terminal_intent==status, pending_confirmation None (contracts.py:285-316)\n\n**§2.6 前端表现:**\n- 三个 tab: 进度（状态板单节点+第 N 轮指示）/ 步骤返回（按 event.iteration 分轮 → 步骤分组）/ 全部事件（全量列表）\n- 状态推导: statusFromEventType 类型后缀约定; itemStatus 族内配对（同族后续 terminal 事件按 sequence 判定成功）; statusForEvents 顺序遍历最后事件定轮状态; interrupted = run.cancelled/timeout/failed 存在 → partial\n- 轮次: event.iteration 顶层字段，buildRoundGroups 分轮，第 N 轮 = iteration+1\n- run.result → 聊天气泡最终回答\n- SSE 帧 id/event/data; 历史回放 execution-trace API → toHistoricalStreamEvent\n\nNow write §2 into the doc. The template sections have HTML comments — I should replace them with real content. Keep the comment style? No — replace comments with actual content (comments were placeholders for the user; now I write). Keep structure and add 疑点清单 entries where genuine uncertainty remains.\n\nGenuine 疑点 for §2: \n- tool.retrying / planner.retrying appear on \"normal\" path when transient failures occur — document as normal-path optional branches (not really a 疑点).\n- The non-stream POST /run exists but frontend uses /run/stream — note.\n- _final_output fallback when artifact missing — behavior note.\n- last_error column on ledger model exists but _drive never passes it (agent D noted) — that's a potential dead field; list in 疑点清单 as observation.\n\nAlso §2.2's event table should include: event name, 发出位置, phase, iteration 来源, payload 关键字段, 前端消费. That's a wide table — maybe split into two tables or keep concise columns: 事件 | 发出位置 | phase | payload 关键字段 | 前端消费. And note iteration semantics once above the table (iteration read live from state[\"harness\"][\"iteration\"]; round N events carry iteration=N).\n\nAlso worth n