he event skeleton. Two complementary views.\n\nActually — maybe cleaner: make the numbered steps the backbone of §2 (the \"主线步骤表\"), with each step mapping to: functions involved, key parameters, events emitted, state changes. Then 2.1/2.2/2.3 content folds into it? That's a bigger restructure. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about what serves the user best:\n\nOption A: Add a new subsection §2.2 \"主线步骤链\" (numbered function-level steps) before the event table; event table stays as §2.3. Steps cover: ① 预检 ② 身份生成 ③ start_turn ④ _build_controller 装配（依赖树） ⑤ SSE 管道 ⑥ start: _new_state 状态初始化 + create + run.started ⑦ _run: build_context（含五个事件） ⑧ plan_action ⑨ commit_action ⑩ execute_tool ⑪ 记录观察+iteration ⑫ 循环回 ⑦ ⑬ _finalize + ledger 六 stage ⑭ run.completed + run.result。\n\nEach step: 函数（file:line）→ 作用一句 → 关键参数/返回 → 发出事件。That's a compact \"函数级地图\". For the loop steps (⑦-⑫), the detail already exists in the event table; the step table can be leaner with cross-references.\n\nOption B: Full annotation of every function with parameters — too much, rots fast, duplicates signatures. I should push back on this part: 函数签名和参数细节以代码为准，文档里只写\"关键参数\"（那些语义不明显的，比如 thread_id=conversation_id 的设计、confirmation_dispatcher=None 的意义），不逐参数罗列。\n\nI should agree with the diagnosis, refine the proposal (steps yes; exhaustive annotation no — keep 参数说明 selective), and then DO it — the user asked \"你感觉呢\", expecting my judgment, and given the established mode (I write docs), I should just implement.\n\nAlso note: their two questions also revealed something else — the questions were about *things the doc didn't make obvious*: _build_controller's role (装配) and start_turn's role (会话层生命周期). The step chain fixes exactly this.\n\nAlso worth noting: the same step-chain treatment will later benefit chapters 3/4 (resume flow steps, abnormal paths) — but those are diffs; for now do §2.\n\nStructure of the new content — I'll rewrite §2.1 into a numbered step chain. Let me design the steps with real file:line:\n\n**步骤链（请求 →