hat's stored in the artifact and what payload ends up as the turn output payload?\n\nAlso build_report/tool.py:62: `return self._output(state, rendered[\"rendered_report\"])` — hmm, rendered dict has \"rendered_report\" key. And tool.py:191 `rendered_report=report`. Need to see how the final turn output payload for output_type=\"rendered_report\" is assembled — in conversation_repository.finish_turn? No — the payload comes from FinalizationInput final_output_ref → artifact content, or from loop_result.\n\nLet me check the _final_output in finalization service and what the artifact stores for build_report. And check what the frontend receives as payload from history API (turn output payload).\n\nActually the crash happened when viewing a session — could be real-time or history. ReportView renders when meta.rendered_report exists, i.e., outputType === \"rendered_report\" and payload cast. If payload = {\"report\": {...RenderedReport...}} then report.sections undefined → crash. OR payload = actual report but an OLD turn stored with a different schema (before sections existed), or failure path stored empty payload {} → sections undefined.\n\nNote agent_service.py:171: `\"rendered_report\": {}` — that's the old AgentService path (旧图 API), empty dict default. If an old-style turn has output_type rendered_report with empty payload {}, ReportView crashes too.\n\nThe robust fix has two layers:\n1. **Root cause layer**: verify what the harness path stores as turn output payload for rendered_report, ensure it's the report object itself (with sections). If mismatch, fix backend to store the right shape OR frontend to unwrap.\n2. **Defense layer**: ReportView must not crash on malformed/legacy payloads — guard `const sections = report.sections ?? []`, and maybe hide the report block entirely if sections missing. Also limitations guard (`report.limitations.length` → `(report.limitations ?? []).length`).\n\nLet me check the backend payload shape: finalization/service.py _final_output + how build_report ToolResult result_ref artifact content looks. Read service.py:146-182 and build_report tool _output.","startTime":1791428023748,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023748},{"id":"a7774344-789a-416e-a799-e9fd92c38448","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"前端把 turn 的 payload 直接 `as RenderedReport`（chat-session-view.tsx:205-207）。现在核对后端到底往这个 payload 里放了什么——查收口时的 `_final_output` 和 build_report 的产物结构："},{"id":"call_ec221c1c4f8e4ebfba07c5d8","type":"TOOL","toolName":"read_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/agent/finalization/service.py","limit":"45","offset":"146"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"<file>\n   146→    async def _save_history(self, value: FinalizationInput) -> None:\n   147→        \"\"\"保存受控 assistant message 和 turn output。\"\"\"\n   148→        output_type, output_payload = await self._final_output(value)\n   149→        saved = await self.conversation_repository.finish_turn(\n   150→            conversation_id=value.run_ref.conversation_id,\n   151→            user_id=value.run_ref.user_id,\n   152→            turn_id=value.run_ref.turn_id,\n   153→            execution_mode=\"harness\",\n   154→            status=value.terminal_status.value,\n   155→            assistant_content=value.final_answer,\n   156→            output_type=output_type,\n   157→            output_payload=output_payload,\n   158→            error_message=value.error_message,\n   159→        )\n   160→        if not saved:\n   161→            raise RuntimeError(\"Harness 最终答案未能写入会话历史\")\n   162→\n   163→    async def _final_output(\n   164→        self, value: FinalizationInput\n   165→    ) -> tuple[str, dict[str, object]]:\n   166→        \"\"\"没有结构化输出引用时只保存文字结果。\"\"\"\n   167→        if value.final_output_ref is None:\n   168→            return \"text\", {\"message\": value.final_answer}\n   169→        if self.artifact_store is None:\n   170→            raise RuntimeError(\"结构化输出需要配置 ArtifactStore 才能收口\")\n   