ccess ✓\n5. 模型输出 (result) → success ✓\n\nvs BEFORE: 173+ spinners. Massive improvement. The one spinner: actually hmm, it WILL look odd next to 4 green items. But it's honest-ish (that progress marker never got a terminal). itemStatus's concluded check would fix it if status weren't explicit... \n\nYou know what — minimal targeted fix: in compactAllEvents merge, when accumulating tool.progress buckets, DON'T carry explicit running status from a lone first event? No — hacky.\n\nCleaner targeted fix at display: in itemStatus, extend the concluded check to explicit running:\n\n```ts\nfunction itemStatus(event: DebugEvent, siblings: DebugEvent[]): RunStatus | undefined {\n  if (event.status && event.status !== \"running\") return event.status;\n  if (event.type === \"error\" || ...) return \"failed\";\n  const derived = statusFromEventType(event.type) ?? (event.status === \"running\" ? \"running\" : undefined);\n  if (derived === \"running\") { ...concluded check... }\n  return derived;\n}\n```\n\nHmm — this makes explicit-running events participate in the concluded check while preserving derived-undefined cases... wait no: for analysis_task_phase with explicit running: derived = undefined; `?? (event.status === \"running\" ? \"running\" : undefined)` → \"running\" → concluded check: family = \"analysis_task_phase\".split(\".\")[0] = \"analysis_task_phase\" → looks for \"analysis_task_phase.completed/failed/resolved\" — never exists → stays \"running\". No regression. For context.* progress with explicit running → family context → context.completed → success. Good. For tool.progress initial → tool.completed → success. \n\nHmm wait, but what about task-scoped analysis_task_phase events — they SHOULD show running while later phases run? Actually currentEvents already collapses old phases (keeps latest running per baseScope for analysis_task_phase). So the displayed one is the latest phase — running is correct until task result. Task result event: type \"analysis_task_resu