sk tools like SQL query path — simple_data): tool.started/tool.completed under node execute_sql etc. — hmm, the tool events are per tool execution. For the timeline, maybe a generic \"执行数据查询\" step driven by tool.started/completed.\n   - 生成报告: report_plan_result → rendered_report (or run.completed)\n   \n   Simpler generic approach: derive the stage list from the SAME mainStep grouping the panel uses? That could get noisy. Better: a fixed stage pipeline with dynamic presence:\n   \n   Stages (each with start/complete event predicates):\n   1. 理解问题：context.started → context.completed (any context.*)\n   2. 划分任务：planner.* exists OR analysis_plan exists → complete when planner.completed or analysis_plan(status success)\n   3. 执行分析任务：tasks exist → task list card; complete when all tasks terminal\n   4. 执行数据查询（simple_data path）: tool.* events where node not in LLM-ish nodes? Hmm — tricky. Maybe: tool.started/completed for tool_name/source that isn't analyze_data? Actually analyze_data IS a tool too. Hmm.\n   5. 生成报告：report_plan_result or rendered_report or run.completed with rendered_report type.\n   \n   Wait — but actually let me think about what runs in the main line: BUILD_CONTEXT → plan (planner) → loop: analyze_data tool (which internally runs plan_analysis/generate_sql/execute_sql/execute_analysis/generate_report) → finalize. For simple_data/chat route: different tools (query_data? chat?).\n   \n   The timeline stages must work across routes. Rather than hardcoding stages by event types, maybe simpler and more robust: **stage list = the mainStep groups** (构建上下文/任务划分/提交动作/执行工具/等待用户确认/运行结果) — the same grouping the panel's step view uses, but rendered as a compact vertical mini-timeline with only: label + status icon + elapsed. Plus, inside 执行工具 group: if tasks exist render task checklist; thinking stream attaches to the current running node.\n   \n   Hmm — but that's basically a mini version of the panel's ProgressView. Reuse! The panel already has ProgressView (进度 tab): steps with status + latest message. I could extract/reuse its logic.\n   \n   Actually — let me design ChatRunProgress independently but reuse exported helpers from execution-panel: `buildTasks`, `DebugEvent`, `progressKind`... I'd need to export them. execution-panel.tsx currently exports: StreamEvent, DebugEvent, appendExecutionEvent, ExecutionPanel. I can export a few internals (buildTasks, eventOrder?) or better: create the component in the same file? The file is already 770 lines. A new file importing shared helpers is cleaner. Let me export `buildTasks` and `progressKind` and type `TaskSummary` from execution-panel.tsx... hmm, exporting internals creates coupling but avoids duplication (优雅 = 不复制逻辑). Alternatively move shared helpers to a new `execution-events.ts` module — bigger refactor. \n\n   Minimal coupling approach: export from execution-panel.tsx: `buildTasks`, `progressKind`, and types `TaskSummary`, `DebugEvent` (already exported). ChatRunProgress imports those. Reasonable.\n\n2. **Thinking stream (方案 B)**: from events, collect tool.progress items with progressKind reasoning (custom_type reasoning_chunk) — per node (source), chunks carry `chunk` + `chunk_index` + `accumulated_chars`. Group by node (source = \"analyze_data:plan_analysis\"), order by first appearance; label per node: map node suffix → friendly label (plan_analysis → 生成分析计划, generate_sql → 生成 SQL, execute_analysis → 执行分析, generate_report_plan → 生成报告, fallback = payload.step). Stream display: show the LATEST node's reasoning while running (or all sections, collapsed except current). Each section: header (label + 用时/片段数 no—no counts... header with label + status), body = combined text.\n   \n   Simpler: for each reasoning node in order, one collapsible section; the currently-streaming one (no reasoning_result yet) auto-expanded with live text + spinner; completed ones collapsed with \"已思考\". The live text: concat chunks in chunk_index order (or arrival order — arrival order is fine and matches panel's combined_text).\n   \n   Performance: chunks arrive per token-ish; each append re-renders. debugEvents updates already re-render the panel; chat will too. Throttle not needed initially — chunk rate = LLM stream rate (~tens/sec worst case). React can handle; the panel already does. Fine.\n\n   Auto-scroll: ref + scrollTop = scrollHeight on update while expanded. Use max-h-40 overflow-y-auto.\n\n3. **Task checklist (方案 C)**: reuse buildTasks(events) → TaskSummary[] (task_id, question, status, node, phase, events). Render each task: status icon + question (truncated) + current phase label (from summary.phase or latest event). tasks complete when terminal().\n\n4. **Summary chip (after done)**: when !running: compute total steps count + elapsed = last event receivedAt - first event receivedAt (debugEvents have receivedAt). Render one muted line: 「已完成 · 用时 52 秒」— maybe with 查看执行过程 entry already existing separately (the bubble has executionLabel button when meta exists — but during run meta?.turn_id — hmm the placeholder message has no meta; the executed trace button appears after history refetch replaces the message). Keep chip simple: status + elapsed. On failure: 「执行失败 · 用时 X 秒」+ error message line.\n\nWhere to render: inside AssistantMessageBubble for the LAST assistant message when it's the local placeholder... But the bubble is inside assistant-ui MessagePrimitive; ChatRunProgress needs debugEvents + isRunning — passed via context. There's already an `ExecutionProcessContext` (useContext(ExecutionProcessContext)) providing executionProcess {open, activeTurnId, toggle}. I can extend that context value or add a new context (RunProgressContext) providing {events, running}. Cleaner: new small context in chat-session-view: `RunProgressContext = createContext<{events: DebugEvent[]; running: boolean} | null>`. Provider wraps the thread; AssistantMessageBubble consumes for the last assistant message while running.\n\nWhen to show vs hide:\n- Show full tim