ext + (no chip yet, meta attached at :1088 update — YES updateAssistantMessage attaches responseMeta :910-912). So at run.completed, message gets text + meta immediately, chip can show, isRunning might still be true briefly. Good — condition on message.status not on isRunning.\n\nSo bubble render rule:\n- isUser → normal.\n- assistant message:\n  - if threadIsRunning && message.status?.type === \"running\" && it's the last message → ChatRunProgress running UI (inside bubble).\n  - else → text (+cursor logic unchanged) + below: chip if meta && meta.elapsed_seconds != null && meta has terminal-ish status. \n\nHmm — should the chip show for daily_chat quick answers (elapsed 1-2s)? A 1-second answer with a chip is noise. Gate: show chip only when elapsed >= some threshold (e.g. >= 5s) OR response_type != chat? For daily chat the run is fast; chip unnecessary. Decision: show chip when response_type !== \"chat\" && elapsed_seconds >= 1. Hmm — simple_data queries take a few seconds; chip「已完成 · 用时 6 秒」 is fine. For chat (1-2s) skip. Gate: meta.execution_mode !== \"daily_chat\" && elapsed > 0. Actually — daily chat turns: does buildConversationMeta get execution_mode daily_chat? turn?.execution_mode — for live completion, turn param = {turn_id, status} — no execution_mode → isDailyChat false → chip would show for chat answers with elapsed 2s. Hmm. Use response_type: \"chat\" skip; \"analysis\"/\"simple_data\"/\"clarification\"/\"failure\" show? failure chip = 「执行失败 · 用时 X」 good. Let me gate: response_type === \"chat\" → no chip. Others → chip.\n\nWait — for the running UI also: daily chat route — does it go through harness with context/planner events? The chat node probably skips context/planner (直接 final_answer) — events would be just run.started → run.completed within 1-2s. Running UI shows... a brief flash of timeline「理解问题」? With only run.* events, my stage derivation yields NO stages (only run.started/run.completed) → ChatRunProgress running UI would render empty — must 