nitizer ✓).\n\nNote: sections label — payload.step of chunks = \"生成分析计划\" ✓. Different nodes have different steps → good labels.\n\nRendering:\n```tsx\n{sections.map((section, index) => {\n  const isCurrent = !section.done && index === sections.length - 1;\n  return (\n    <details key={section.key} open={isCurrent}>\n      <summary> {icon} {section.label} {section.done ? \"已完成\" : \"思考中\"} </summary>\n      <div ref>...{section.text}...</div>\n    </details>\n  );\n})}\n```\nLive text: dark mini-console look (bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 text-[11px] font-mono? or light gray box). Match app aesthetic: rounded bg-slate-50 border, text-slate-600, text-xs leading-5, max-h-40 overflow-auto. Auto-scroll: ref + useEffect on text.\n\nOnly auto-open the current section; done sections collapsed (`open` attribute only set for current — React details with open prop — uncontrolled afterwards; fine).\n\nEdge: multiple LLM nodes stream sequentially; when section 1 done and section 2 starts, section 1 collapses (open=false) — React re-render sets open={false}... hmm — controlled `open` prop on <details> makes it controlled-ish: React sets the attribute each render; user toggling won't stick (React re-renders on events → open forced). For done sections open={false} always → user can't expand! Because every SSE chunk re-renders. Hmm — need uncontrolled behavior: use `open` only as INITIAL default via key trick, or track manually. Simplest: keep done sections as `open={undefined}`... React details: passing open={false} forces closed. Passing undefined → uncontrolled. But when a section transitions current→done, we want it to collapse: with uncontrolled it stays open. Trick: set `key={section.key + (section.done ? \":done\" : \":live\")}` → remount on done transition with defaultOpen=false. details without open attr = closed default. And current section: `open` attr present (controlled open true) — during streaming re-renders keep it open ✓ (user collapse during streaming gets overridd