sponseMeta attached (metadata.custom.conversation)? During resume running, responseMeta not yet attached (attached only at terminal updateAssistantMessage calls since responseMeta variable set before update). Wait — in resume, at :1301 updateAssistantMessage with responseMeta set. During running, no meta. And in the initial send: during typewriter, meta NOT attached either (attached at :1088 final update... wait — updateAssistantMessage reads responseMeta variable at call time (:910) — during drainTypewriter (:930) responseMeta is... set at run.completed :1079 BEFORE drainTypewriter :1086! So during typewriter drain, updates DO carry responseMeta. Hmm so meta-presence doesn't distinguish typewriter from resume-running.\n\nOK — use the placeholder-text set approach. It's honest: the two states where the assistant message is a placeholder. \n\nHmm, wait — actually there's yet another wrinkle: during RESUME, is threadIsRunning true? setIsRunning(true) at :1203 ✓. And message.status running ✓, last message ✓ → showStreamingCursor true ✓ → timeline shows over the placeholder text ✓. Good — resume shows the CONTINUED timeline (events include pre-pause history — stages remain ✓ thinking sections continue ✓). \n\nNow — one more: `getDisplayMessageText` (:639) — check it handles content array. Assume similar to getMessageText. Fine.\n\nChip during resume-pause: meta.status waiting_confirmation → amber chip 「已暂停，等待你的确认」 ✓ (from confirmation paths :1293-1301).\n\nAlso — legacy execution button suppression: when chip shows with toggle. Let me now also confirm getDisplayMessageText (:639 uses it) — fine.\n\n**Now write the code.**\n\nFiles:\n1. `frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx` — export RunStatus, TaskSummary, StatusIcon, buildTasks, progressKind.\n2. New `frontend/components/insight-agent/chat-run-progress.tsx` — ChatRunTimeline + ChatRunSummaryChip.\n3. `frontend/components/insight-agent/chat-session-view.tsx` — RunProgressContext provider + bubble integration (placeholder swap + chip replacing legacy button when shown).\n\nLet me write chat-run-progress.tsx carefully.\n\n```tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport {\n  AlertCircle,\n  CheckCircle2,\n  ChevronRight,\n  Circle,\n  Loader2,\n  XCircle,\n} from \"lucide-react\";\nimport { buildTasks, progressKind, StatusIcon, type DebugEvent, type RunStatus, type TaskSummary } from \"./execution-panel\";\n\n/** 聊天气泡内的运行进度：从同一份 SSE 事件派生思考流、阶段时间线与任务清单，不落库。 */\n\ninterface RunStage {\n  key: string;\n  label: string;\n  status: RunStatus;\n  detail?: string;\n  tasks?: TaskSummary[];\n}\n\nfunction hasEvent(events: DebugEvent[], pred: (e: DebugEvent) => boolean) { return events.some(pred); }\n\nfunction deriveRunStages(events: DebugEvent[], tasks: TaskSummary[]): RunStage[] {\n  const stages: RunStage[] = [];\n  const failed = events.some((e) => e.type === \"run.failed\" || e.type === \"run.timeout\" || e.type === \"run.cancelled\" || e.type === \"stream.failed\");\n\n  const pushStage = (stage: RunStage) => {\n    if (failed) stage.status = \"failed\";  // hmm — mark ALL stages failed? No — only the last active one. \n    stages.push(stage);\n  };\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm, failure marking: if run failed, the in-flight stage failed; completed earlier stages stay success. Approach: derive stages with natural status first; then if failed, find the LAST stage with status \"running\" → set failed. If none running, leave as-is.\n\nStage statuses:\n1. understand — present if any context.* or question_route:\n   - status: context.failed → \"failed\"; context.completed → \"success\"; else \"running\".\n2. plan — present if planner.* or analysis_plan:\n   - planner.failed → failed; analysis_plan failed → failed; planner.completed or analysis_plan success → success; else running. detail: tasks.length ? `${tasks.length} 个任务` : undefined.\n3. execute — present if action.committed || any tool.* (type startsWith \"tool.\") || tasks.length:\n   - tasks.length ? label \"执行分析任务\" : label \"执行数据查询\"\n   - tasks: with tasks: done = tasks.filter(terminal).length; allDone = done === tasks.length; anyFailed = tasks.some(failed); status = allDone ? (anyFailed ? \"partial\" : \"success\") : \"running\"; detail = allDone ? undefined : `已完成 ${doneCount}/${tasks.length}`. hmm if partial show detail undefined ok.\n   - without tasks: tool.failed → failed; tool.completed → success; tool.started/progress → running; action.committed only → running.\n4. report — present if report_plan_result or rendered_report:\n   - rendered_report or run.completed → success; else running.\n\nWait — the execute stage with tasks: what about non-task tools ALSO running (analyze_data IS the tool that runs tasks internally)? For analysis route: tool events are analyze_data (source analyze_data) with tasks inside. Both representations coexist — stage label 执行分析任务 with task checklist ✓ (tool.started for analyze_data + tasks). Good.\n\nFor simple_data route: tool query_data etc., no tasks → 执行数据查询 ✓.\n\nHmm — what about tool.progress thinking sections in simple_data route (LLM generating SQL inside query tool)? Thinking sections render above timeline regardless of stage ✓.\n\nterminal helper:\n```ts\nfunction taskTerminal(status: RunStatus) { return status === \"success\" || status === \"partial\" || status === \"failed\"; }\n```\n\nThinking sections:\n\n```tsx\ninterface ThinkingSection { key: string; label: string; text: string; done: boolean; }\n\nfunction deriveThinkingSections(events: DebugEvent[]): ThinkingSection[] {\n  const sections = new Map<string, ThinkingSection>();\n  for (const event of events) {\n    if (event.type !== \"tool.progress\" || progressKind(event) !== \"reasoning\") continue;\n    const key = event.node;\n    const section = sections.get(key) ?? {\n      key,\n      label: typeof event.payload.step === \"string\" && event.payload.step.trim() ? event.payload.step : key,\n      text: \"\",\n      done: false,\n    };\n    if (event.payload.custom_type === \"reasoning_result\") section.done = true;\n    else if (typeof event.payload.chunk === \"string\") section.text += event.payload.chunk;\n    sections.set(key, section);\n  }\n  return Array.from(sections.values());\n}\n```\n\nHmm — wait: chunk events order — iteration order of events array = arrival order ✓ text concatenates in arrival order ✓.\n\nEdge: a node whose reasoning stream failed midway (timeout) — section never done → stays \"思考中\" forever after run end... After failure the whole message becomes failure text; timeline gone. OK.\n\nThinkingBody with autoscroll:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ThinkingBody({ text, live }: { text: string; live: boolean }) {\n  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (live && ref.current) ref.current.scrollTop = ref.current.scrollHeight;\n  }, [text, live]);\n  return (\n    <div ref={ref} className=\"mt-1 max-h-40 overflow-y-auto rounded-lg bg-slate-50 px-3 py-2 text-xs leading-5 whitespace-pre-wrap text-slate-600\">\n      {text || \"…\"}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nSections render:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ThinkingSections({ sections }: { sections: ThinkingSection[] }) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"space-y-1.5\">\n      {sections.map((section, index) => {\n        const live = !section.done && index === sections.length - 1;\n        return (\n          <details key={section.key + (section.done ? \":done\" : \":live\")} open={live ? true : undefined} className=\"group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white\">\n            <summary className=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2\">\n              <ChevronRight className=\"size-3.5 text-slate-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-90\" />\n              {live ? <Loader2 className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin text-blue-500\" /> : <CheckCircle2 className=\"size-3.5 text-emerald-500\" />}\n              <span className=\"text-[11px] font-bold text-slate-600\">{section.label}</span>\n              <span className=\"text-[10px] text-slate-400\">{live ? \"思考中\" : \"已完成\"}</span>\n            </summary>\n            <div className=\"px-3 pb-2\">\n              <ThinkingBody text={section.text} live={live} />\n            </div>\n          </details>\n        );\n      })}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nHmm — label wording: 「思考中」/「已完成」— maybe 「深度思考中」/「思考完成」. Keep 思考中/已完成. Hmm — for llm-only... no, sections are reasoning only. OK.\n\nWait — the label: sections keyed by node; label from payload.step of the reasoning events — \"生成分析计划\" ✓, for generate_sql \"生成 SQL\" ✓, generate_report_plan \"生成报告规划\" or similar ✓. \n\nTask list:\n\n```tsx\nfunction TaskChecklist({ tasks }: { tasks: TaskSummary[] }) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-1.5 space-y-1 rounded-lg border border-slate-100 bg-slate-50/60 px-2.5 py-2\">\n      {tasks.map((task) => (\n        <div key={task.task_id} className=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n          <span className=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><TaskDot status={task.status} /></span>\n          <div className=\"min-w-0\">\n            <div className=\"truncate text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-600\">{task.question || task.task_id}</div>\n            <div className=\"text-[10px] text-slate-400\">{taskStatusText(task)}</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction TaskDot({ status }: { status: RunStatus }) {\n  if (status === \"success\") return <CheckCircle2 className=\"size-3.5 text-emerald-500\" />;\n  if (status === \"failed\" || status === \"partial\") return <XCircle className=\"size-3.5 text-rose-500\" />;\n  if (status === \"running\") return <Loader2 className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin text-blue-500\" />;\n  return <Circle className=\"size-3.5 text-slate-300\" />;\n}\n\nfunction taskStatusText(task: TaskSummary) {\n  if (task.status === \"running\") return task.phase || \"执行中\";\n  if (task.status === \"success\") return \"已完成\";\n  if (task.status === \"failed\") return task.error || \"执行失败\";\n  if (task.status === \"partial\") return task.error || \"部分完成\";\n  return \"等待执行\";\n}\n```\n\nTimeline stages render:\n\n```tsx\nfunction StageRow({ stage }: { stage: RunStage }) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n      <span className=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><StatusIcon status={stage.status} /></span>\n      <div className=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n        <div className=\"text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700\">\n          {stage.label}\n          {stage.detail && <span className=\"ml-1.5 text-[10px] font-normal text-slate-400\">{stage.detail}</span>}\n        </div>\n        {stage.tasks && stage.tasks.length > 0 && <TaskChecklist tasks={stage.tasks} />}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nMain ChatRunTimeline:\n\n```tsx\nexport function ChatRunTimeline({ events }: { events: DebugEvent[] }) {\n  const tasks = useMemo(() => buildTasks(events), [events]);\n  const stages = useMemo(() => deriveRunStages(events, tasks), [events, tasks]);\n  const sections = useMemo(() => deriveThinkingSections(events), [events]);\n  const [startMs] = useState(() => Date.now());   // hmm — better first event receivedAt\n  const [, setTick] = useState(0);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const timer = setInterval(() => setTick((value) => value + 1), 1000);\n    return () => clearInterval(timer);\n  }, []);\n  const elapsedSeconds = ...;\n  ...\n  return (\n    <div className=\"space-y-2.5\">\n      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] font-bold text-blue-600\">\n        <Loader2 className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin\" />\n        正在执行 · {elapsedSeconds}s\n      </div>\n      {sections.length > 0 && <ThinkingSections sections={sections} />}\n      {stages.length > 0 && <div className=\"space-y-1.5\">{stages.map((s) => <StageRow key={s.key} stage={s} />)}</div>}\n      {sections.length === 0 && stages.length === 0 && <div className=\"text-xs text-slate-400\">正在思考…</div>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nElapsed: start = events[0]?.receivedAt ? Date.parse : mount time. \n```ts\nconst first = events[0] ? Date.parse(events[0].receivedAt) : NaN;\nconst startedAtMs = Number.isFinite(first) ? first : startRef\nconst elapsedSeconds = Math.max(1, Math.round((Date.now() - startedAtMs) / 1000));\n```\nNeed Date.now() each render — tick forces re-render ✓. Store mount time via useRef initial. Fine.\n\nElapsed display — hmm `Math.max(1,...)`... 0 fine too. Keep Math.max(0,...).\n\nNote timer interval runs only while component mounted = while a placeholder running ✓ (unmounts on completion → timer cleared ✓).\n\nMemo deps: `events` array identity changes every append ✓ recompute fine.\n\n**Chip**:\n\n```tsx\nexport function ChatRunSummaryChip({\n  status,\n  elapsedSeconds,\n  traceLabel,\n  onOpenTrace,\n}: {\n  status?: string;\n  elapsedSeconds?: number;\n  traceLabel?: string;\n  onOpenTrace?: () => void;\n}) {\n  const waiting = status === \"waiting_confirmation\";\n  const failed = status === \"failed\" || status === \"timeout\" || status === \"cancelled\" || status === \"stream_failed\";\n  const tone = waiting\n    ? \"border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 text-amber-700\"\n    : failed\n      ? \"border-rose-100 bg-rose-50 text-rose-600\"\n      : \"border-slate-200 bg-white text-slate-500\";\n  const icon = waiting\n    ? <AlertCircle className=\"size-3.5\" />\n    : failed\n      ? <XCircle className=\"size-3.5\" />\n      : <CheckCircle2 className=\"size-3.5 text-emerald-500\" />;\n  const text = waiting\n    ? \"已暂停，等待你的确认\"\n    : failed\n      ? \"执行失败\"\n      : \"已完成\";\n  return (\n    <button  // or div when no onOpenTrace\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={onOpenTrace}\n      disabled={!onOpenTrace}\n      className={`mt-1 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md border px-2.5 py-1.5 text-[11px] font-semibold ${tone} ${onOpenTrace ? \"cursor-pointer transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:text-blue-700\" : \"cursor-default\"}`}\n    >\n      {icon}\n      <span>{text}{typeof elapsedSeconds === \"number\" && elapsedSeconds > 0 ? ` · 用时 ${formatElapsed(elapsedSeconds)}` : \"\"}</span>\n      {onOpenTrace && traceLabel && (\n        <span className=\"inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 text-blue-600\">· {traceLabel}<ChevronRight className=\"size-3\" /></span>\n      )}\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction formatElapsed(seconds: number) {\n  if (seconds < 60) return `${Math.round(seconds)} 秒`;\n  const minutes = Math.floor(seconds / 60);\n  const rest = Math.round(seconds % 60);\n  return rest ? `${minutes} 分 ${rest} 秒` : `${minutes} 分钟`;\n}\n```\n\nHmm — disabled button styling... use a div when no onOpenTrace? Simpler: always a <button type=\"button\"> but without onClick when no handler; disabled attr greys it (opacity default?) — avoid disabled; just omit onClick. Accessibility nitpick aside, fine. Actually make it a <div> when no trace? Conditional element type is awkward. Use span role none... Keep button without disabled and without onClick when no handler — clickable no-op. Meh. Alternatively wrap: if onOpenTrace → button else div. I'll do `{onOpenTrace ? <button ...> : <div ...>}` sharing className var. Slightly verbose but correct.\n\nHmm wait — simplified: since bubble already computes canViewExecution, chip nearly always has toggle when it matters. For messages without trace (daily chat) chip hidden anyway (response_type chat → null in bubble gate). failure/waiting chips: toggle available? canViewExecution requires response_type analysis/simple_data/harness — failure meta response_type = \"failure\"?? outputResponseType(\"failure\")... hmm :1100 buildConversationMeta(failedMessage, \"failure\", ...) → response_type = outputResponseType(\"failure\") — unknown mapping, probably \"chat\" or fallback. Whatever — pass onOpenTrace only when canViewExecution && traceTurnId; chip renders text-only otherwise ✓.\n\nNow **bubble integration** in chat-session-view.tsx:\n\n```tsx\nconst RunProgressContext = createContext<DebugEvent[]>([]);\n```\nProvider: wrap inside ExecutionProcessContext.Provider (or outside — needs to cover AssistantChatThread): \n```tsx\n<ExecutionProcessContext.Provider value={...}>\n  <RunProgressContext.Provider value={debugEvents}>\n    ...existing tree...\n  </RunProgressContext.Provider>\n</ExecutionProcessContext.Provider>\n```\n\nIn AssistantMessageBubble:\n```tsx\nconst liveEvents = useContext(RunProgressContext);\n...\nconst placeholderText = displayText.trim();\nconst isLivePlaceholder = showStreamingCursor && (placeholderText === \"\" || placeholderText === \"正在根据你的确认继续处理...\");\n```\nBubble content:\n```tsx\n<div className={bubbleCls}>\n  {isLivePlaceholder ? <ChatRunTimeline events={liveEvents} /> : <>{displayText}{showStreamingCursor && cursor}</>}\n</div>\n```\n(keep cursor when text typing ✓)\n\nChip + legacy button merge:\n```tsx\nconst metaElapsed = typeof meta?.elapsed_seconds === \"number\" ? meta.elapsed_seconds : 0;\nconst showSummaryChip = !!meta && meta.response_type !== \"chat\" && metaElapsed > 0 && !isLivePlaceholder;\nconst traceToggle = canViewExecution && traceTurnId && executionProcess ? () => executionProcess.toggle(traceTurnId) : undefined;\n```\nRender:\n```tsx\n{showSummaryChip ? (\n  <ChatRunSummaryChip status={meta?.status} elapsedSeconds={metaElapsed} traceLabel={executionLabel || undefined} onOpenTrace={traceToggle} />\n) : (\n  executionProcess && executionLabel && traceTurnId && ( existing button )\n)}\n```\nPosition: where the legacy button was (after time span, before rendered_report) ✓. Note: existing button has mt-4; chip has own margin — align: keep mt-1? The button previously `mt-4`. For chip: mt-2 fine.\n\nHmm — one ordering detail: `meta?.query_result` renders before button; keep order: query_result → chip/button → rendered_report. Existing order: time span → query_result → button → rendered_report. I'll place chip in the button slot ✓.\n\nAlso waiting chip: waiting_confirmation messages have response_type \"clarification\" — meta.response_type !== \"chat\" ✓ elapsed > 0 (they set elapsed override ✓) → chip shows 「已暂停，等待你的确认」 ✓. \n\nDaily chat: response_type \"chat\" → chip hidden ✓, legacy button hidden (canViewExecution false) ✓.\n\nOne more check — conversationMeta(message): extracts meta from message metadata (:637). For live placeholder it's undefined ✓ chip path guarded by !isLivePlaceholder anyway.\n\n**Export changes in execution-panel.tsx**: \n- `type RunStatus` → export\n- `type TaskSummary` → export\n- `StatusIcon` → export\n- `buildTasks` → export\n- `progressKind` → export\n\nCheck StatusIcon signature: `({ status }: { status: RunStatus | undefined })` ✓ good — StageRow uses it.\n\nRunStatus usage in new file for local helpers ✓.\n\nPotential circular import? chat-run-progress imports from execution-panel; chat-session-view imports both — no cycle ✓.\n\n**One concern — buildTasks on every SSE append**: buildTasks iterates all events (169+) per chunk append — O(n) per append, O(n²) cumulative — same as the panel already does (buildTasks called in ExecutionPanel every render). Fine.\n\n**Another check — details `open={live ? true : undefined}`**: TS: open?: boolean — passing undefined ok.\n\nWait — there's an issue with the remount key trick: `key={section.key + (section.done ? \":done\" : \":live\")}` — when done flips, remount closed ✓. But DURING live, every chunk re-render... key stable (\":live\") ✓ no remount, open stays forced true ✓. After done, key \":done\", open undefined → uncontrolled, user can expand/collapse freely; re-renders (later events, e.g. new nodes streaming) don't force it ✓.\n\nHmm — but wait: `open={undefined}` + React — does React treat details as uncontrolled when open omitted? Yes — attribute omitted → browser default (closed), user toggles natively, React won't touch it. ✓\n\n**deriveRunStages detail** — \"已完成 X/Y\" while running. Also during running show CURRENT task phase in detail? The checklist already shows per-task phase ✓ detail keeps counts.\n\nEdge — multiple rounds (iteration loops): tasks from round 1 all done, round 2 tasks pending — buildTasks merges all analysis_plan tasks (each taskId once) ✓ counts include pending ✓.\n\nNow — also the \"等待你确认\" stage handling: skipped as reasoned (message swaps immediately). OK.\n\nFailure marking: after deriving stages, if runFailed: find last stage with status \"running\" → \"failed\". Also stages after it (none since it's last running). And if the last stage is report running → failed ✓.\n\nHmm — one more subtle: stream.failed reconciliation path — events include stream.failed ✓ runFailed true ✓.\n\nAlso — context.failed event exists (added in task #13) → understand stage failed ✓ (before generic failure marking).\n\nLet me also double check `statusOf`/status derivation for stage statuses I compute manually — I compute directly from event presence, not via statusForEvents (which needs RunStatus fallback semantics) — simpler and predictable ✓.\n\nAlright — also need `useMemo` import in chat-run-progress. And \"use client\".\n\nTypeScript details:\n- TaskSummary fields: task_id, status, question?, resolved_question?, purpose?, depends_on, node?, phase?, error?, events. ✓\n- DebugEvent.payload: Record<string, unknown> ✓.\n\nNow also — hmm, `buildTasks` groups tasks from analysis_plan events; for routes without analysis_plan → [] ✓.\n\nWrite the files now. Also add module-level doc comments per style.\n\nOne more integration point — the `ChatRunTimeline` shows in the white bubble; bubble has padding px-4 py-3 — timeline inside gets cramped but OK. Bubble width: assistant `w-full min-w-0` with inner max-w-[70%]... the bubble div has `${!isUser ? \"max-w-[70%]\" : \"\"}` — timeline constrained to 70% width — thinking text readable. Fine. Hmm — actually for the live placeholder maybe wider is nicer, but keep consistent.\n\nAlso — the timeline replaces the empty text; the bubble keeps whitespace-pre-wrap (no effect on divs).\n\nNow write everything. After that: tsc, lint skip, commit.\n\nWait — one more thing about `ChatRunSummaryChip` when `meta.status === \"completed\"` BUT outputType rendered_report → chip + big report below — fine.\n\nAnd `elapsed_seconds` for live completed flow: buildConversationMeta override = (Date.now()-startedAt)/1000 ✓.\n\nAlso — history messages: meta from :313 `buildConversationMeta(message.content, output.output_type, payload, turn)` — turn includes status + started_at/completed_at → elapsed ✓ status ✓. Do history turns include failed status? conversation_turns have status column; failed turns presumably persisted with status failed — chip renders 执行失败 for history too ✓.\n\nEdge: old messages before this feature — meta still has elapsed → chips appear retroactively. That's FINE/desirable.\n\nLet me write the new file now.","startTime":1791428023748,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023748},{"id":"da28dba3-5127-42ed-8656-e4e759b71cef","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"流程全部摸清了（含确认暂停/恢复路径）。开始实现 — 先建任务跟踪："},{"id":"call_b9512cd312674f738c6eb529","type":"TOOL","toolName":"create_task","params":{"activeForm":"实现聊天内运行进度组件","description":"新建 chat-run-progress.tsx：从 debugEvents 派生思考流分节（reasoning_chunk 按节点聚合）、阶段时间线（context/planner/execute/report）、任务清单（复用 buildTasks）；完成后由 meta.elapsed_seconds 渲染摘要 chip。execution-panel 导出 buildTasks/progressKind/StatusIcon/TaskSummary/RunStatus。","subject":"聊天内运行进度：思考流+时间线+任务清单组件"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Task #20 created successfully: 聊天内运行进度：思考流+时间线+任务清单组件","metadata":{"taskId":"20","task":{"id":"20","subject":"聊天内运行进度：思考流+时间线+任务清单组件","description":"新建 chat-run-progress.tsx：从 debugEvents 派生思考流分节（reasoning_chunk 按节点聚合）、阶段时间线（context/planner/execute/report）、任务清单（复用 buildTasks）；完成后由 meta.elapsed_seconds 渲染摘要 chip。execution-panel 导出 buildTasks/progressKind/StatusIcon/TaskSummary/RunStatus。","activeForm":"实现聊天内运行进度组件","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},"taskSnapshot":{"$blob":"sha256:5946eebc54915e4f00bd35df4635b0b9d78b195fd7162517a85464add4c979e6","version":1,"encoding":"json","byteLength":637