tokens each? v3: batch 6? Actually text-embedding-v3 via compatible-mode: max 6 texts per call? The comment says 兼容接口单次请求最多 6 条文本)\n- ES also has dense_vector fields for dimension values (task #11 rebuilt ES+Qdrant) — dimension change affects ES mapping too\n- Memory encoder uses active_model naming\n\n**Target: qwen3.7-text-embedding**\n- Custom dimensions 256~2560 → can set dimensions=1024 → SAME vector_size → no collection rebuild needed IF we keep 1024!\n- Max input 131072 tokens (vs v3's 8192)\n- Price 0.5元/M tokens (v3 is 0.0007元/1k = 0.7元/M — so slightly cheaper)\n- Better MTEB (~20% over v4, v4 > v3)\n- Same OpenAI-compatible endpoint (compatible-mode) — provider dashscope unchanged\n- Batch size limit: unknown for this model — v3/v4 compatible-mode limit is 10 texts per batch (DashScope text-embedding-v3/v4: batch ≤ 10; the OpenAI compat endpoint... the comment says 6). For qwen3.7-text-embedding, batch limit unknown from fetched page. Keep batch_size 6 to be safe? Or test. The config comment says 兼容接口单次请求最多 6 条 — that was v3's constraint (v3: 6 texts? v4: 10?). Safe: keep 6 initially.\n\nSo the answer: **能切，而且可以无痛切** — because qwen3.7-text-embedding supports custom dimensions including 1024, matching the current qdrant.vector_size=1024. BUT — vector space changes even at same dimension! Switching embedding models changes the vector SPACE (different model = different distribution), so existing stored vectors (embedded with v3) mixed with new query vectors (qwen3.7) = garbage similarity. The verify_dimension check only validates DIMENSION, not model identity — it would pass with 1024 dims while recall quality silently degrades!\n\nSo: same dimension = no infrastructure rebuild needed, but MUST re-embed all stored vectors (rebuild collections content): metadata tables/columns/metrics vectors, dimension values (ES + Qdrant), memory collections. That's exactly tasks #10-#12 they did before. Alternatively recreate collections fresh.\n\nWait — ES: dimension values use ES dense_vector with dims 1024? ES mapping has fixed dims — same 1024 → no mapping change needed, but the stored vectors must be re-embedded too (they're v3 vectors). Task #11 covered ES rebuild.\n\nMemory collections: agent_memory_* were emptied in task #12 before... they may have data now. Need re-embed or clear.\n\n**What to change:**\n1. `.env`: `DASHSCOPE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3.7-text-embedding` (config.yaml default is text-embedding-v3; env overrides)\n2. dimensions stays 1024 (config.yaml `dimensions: 1024` — passed as `dimensions` param to OpenAIEmbeddings → DashScope compatible API supports dimensions parameter for this model ✓ 256~2560)\n3. Rebuild vectors: re-run the rebuild flows (tasks #10-12 equivalents):\n   - 重建元数据向量（tables/columns/metrics）— the vector services have rebuild endpoints/CLI?\n   - 重建维度值索引（ES + Qdrant）\n   - 记忆 collection 清空/重编码\n4. Startup verify_dimension will pass (1024=1024) — but it can't catch \"model mismatch\". Note: worth mentioning that dimension check won't protect against forgetting the re-embed; must actually rebuild.\n\nAlso worth checking: does the model name need exact string `qwen3.7-text-embedding`? Yes per doc. Region: 华北2（北京）or Singapore; their base_url is dashscope.aliyuncs.com (Beijing region) ✓ compatible.\n\nRate limit: TPM 1,000,000 (Beijing) — fine for their batch rebuilds.\n\nCost: their metadata volume is small (tables/columns/metrics/dimension values) — negligible cost.\n\nAlso `qwen3.7-text-embedding-flash` exists (cheaper/faster variant) — could mention as alternative.\n\nShould I check where memory encoder names by active_model — switching model changes encoder name → memory collections keyed by encoder? \"用于记忆编码器命名等场景\" — active_model used in memory encoder naming; the memory collections are named *_v1 fixed in config. If encoder name changes, memory formation might write to same collection with new vectors — mixed space. Recommend clearing memory collections on switch.\n\nAlso batch_size: v3 limit 6? For qwen3.7 — unknown; DashScope text-embedding series compatible-mode batch limit is 10 for v3/v4 actually... the comment says 6 (they may have hit limits). Keep 6; if API rejects adjust. Actually — let me not assert; recommend keep 6 then test.\n\nSo my answer structure:\n1. 结论：能切，当前架构就是为这种切换设计的（provider 不变，只换模型名），而且 qwen3.7 支持自定义维度 → 保持 1024 维就不需要动 Qdrant/ES 的 collection 结构\n2. 但必须重建向量内容（不能只改配置就跑）：向量空间变了，维度相同也不兼容 —— 启动自检只校验维度，校验不出模型不一致\n3. 具体步骤：.env 加 DASHSCOPE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3.7-text-embedding → 重启前先清/重建：元数据向量（3 个 collection）、维度值（ES+Qdrant）、记忆 collections\n4. 模型规格要点：131k 输入、0.5元/M、batch 限制保持 6 试水、flash 变体存在\n\nOffer: 要我现在帮你切换吗（改 .env + 走一遍重建流程）？They asked \"我现在能切换这个向量模型吗\" — a question. Answer it, offer to execute. Don't just do it — switching affects running services and requires rebuilding indexes; confirm first.\n\nKeep it concise.","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"0e074b78-c672-4f7c-9c6d-46444bf5936b","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"能切，而且你这套架构就是为这种切换准备的——但有一个关键前提要先说清楚。\n\n## 结论\n\n**架构层面无痛**：当前就是走百炼 OpenAI 兼容接口（`provider: dashscope`，`base_url` 指向 `dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1`），换模型只是换一个名字：\n\n```bash\n# .env 加一行（config.yaml 默认值是 text-embedding-v3，环境变量覆盖）\nDASHSCOPE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3.7-text-embedding\n```\n\n`qwen3.7-text-embedding` 支持 **256~2560 维自定义维度**，所以把 `dimensions` 保持 1024 不变，Qdrant collection（`vector_size: 1024`）和 ES 的 dense_vector mapping 都**不用重建结构**。规格也全面优于现在的 v3：131072 输入长度（v3 只有 8k）、检索效果比 v4 还高约 20%、0.5 元/百万 tokens 还更便宜。\n\n## 但必须重建向量内容，不能只改配置\n\n**维度相同 ≠ 向量空间相同**。库里存的向量是 v3 编码的，新查询用 qwen3.7 编码，相似度计算完全是错的。而你的启动自检（`verify_dimension`，main.py:44）只校验维度一致——1024=1024 会静默通过，召回质量悄悄劣化，这种静默劣化比启动报错更危险。\n\n所以要切就得走一遍你之前做过的全套重建（就是任务 #10-#12 那轮）：\n\n1. 清空并重建元数据向量：`meta_tables/columns/metrics_semantic` 三个 collection\n2. 重建维度值索引：ES + Qdrant 双份\n3. 清空记忆 collections（`agent_memory_*_v1`，记忆编码器标识也随 `active_model` 变了）\n\n## 两个小注意点\n\n- `batch_size: 6` 先保持——这是 v3 时代的兼容接口单批上限，qwen3.7 的上限文档页没写明，先用 6 试水，报错再调\n- 还有更便宜的 `qwen3.7-text-embedding-flash` 变体，如果只想试水可以先切 flash\n\n要我现在动手吗？步骤是：改 `.env` → 清空 4+6 个 collection 和 ES 索引 → 跑元数据向量重建 → 维度值重建 → 重启后端看维度自检。确认了我就开始。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789699707081},{"id":"023754df-8fb7-4e7a-b233-7df304a262a6","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"就是一次切换向量模型，就要删除现有的向量数据库，重新再来一遍吗？","payload":{"query":"就是一次切换向量模型，就要删除现有的向量数据库，重新再来一遍吗？","rawMessage":"就是一次切换向量模型，就要删除现有的向量数据库，重新再来一遍吗？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"cb5c3aa2-a9aa-40a8-91f7-7eef94796988","requestedAt":1789699934319,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"023754df-8fb7-4e7a-b233-7df304a262a6"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789699934344},{"id":"199b058e-5cae-4caa-a281-65969e7bde2e","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"023754df-8fb7-4e7a-b233-7df304a262a6","reportedId":"26d709db-8389-4726-993d-9b7242029efc","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":75.23,"contextUsed":192597,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":799,"totalDuration":60382},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aaca75f2dd493057d75cac3","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":59583},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"bc51b9fb-5f88-4ba0-bc30-e473a46c3e9c","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user is asking: \"就是一次切换向量模型，就要删除现有的向量数据库，重新再来一遍吗？\" — \"So switching the vector model once means deleting the existing vector database and doing it all over again?\"\n\nThis is a conceptual question about why model switching requires re-embedding. They may be reluctant about the cost/inconvenience. I should:\n\n1. Explain clearly WHY: vectors are coordinates in a model-specific semantic space; comparing vectors from different models is meaningless (like comparing temperature in Celsius to distance in kilometers — same numbers, different meaning). Dimension matching is necessary but not sufficient.\n\n2. Clarify what \"重来一遍\" actually means in their case — it's NOT rebuilding infrastructure:\n   - Collection structure/mapping: unchanged (dimension 1024 same)\n   - The data sources of truth are NOT the vector DB: metadata (tables/columns/metrics) lives in PostgreSQL (meta_build_test repository), dimension values live in business DB, memory is generated content\n   - Re-embedding = re-running the embedding pipeline over source data — their rebuild flows already exist (they did it in tasks #10-12, took one round)\n   - Volume: it's their own metadata — tables/columns/metrics/dimension values are maybe thousands of rows, not millions. Cheap and fast (a few minutes, few cents at 0.5元/M tokens)\n\n3. Alternatives that avoid rebuild (be honest):\n   - No real way around it for stored vectors — any embedding model change invalidates stored vectors. This is industry-standard (even Pinecone/Weaviate docs say re-embed on model change).\n   - What CAN persist: nothing vector-based. Non-vector data (ES keyword index for dimension values — the ES part might be keyword-based? Actually ES holds dense_vector too for dimension values — task #11 \"重建维度值索引（ES + Qdrant）\" suggests ES has vector fields; but ES also may have keyword/text fields which don't need rebuilding... careful. If ES index is hybrid (text + vector), only vector field needs reindexing. Actually for dimension value search they use ES + Qdrant hybrid RRF — ES likely has both text and dense vector. If switching model, the ES dense_vector values also need re-embedding but text fields stay. The rebuild script handles it.)\n   - Dual-collection migration strategy (for zero-downtime production): build new collections alongside, dual-write, switch alias, drop old. For their dev stage — overkill. But worth mentioning as the production-grade answer: don't delete in place, rebuild into new collections and cut over. With same dimension, you can even write into NEW collections named v2, verify, then switch config. Their config has collection names in config.yaml so they could add new names, rebuild, flip config.\n   - Also: avoid frequent switching — pick once, stick with it. Memory collections are the most painful (generated content re-encoding... actually memory items' text can be re-embedded too — the memory module stores original text + vector? If original text is stored, re-embedding is mechanical, not regeneration.)\n\n4. Practical cost estimate: their data volume — metadata (hundreds-thousands of rows), dimension values (maybe thousands-tens of thousands). At 0.5元/M tokens with short texts (~50 tokens each), 10k items ≈ 500k tokens ≈ 0.25元. Trivial. Time: minutes with batching.\n\n5. Also mention: because it's disruptive, batch future switches (e.g., when v4→qwen3.7 or when they next change, do all collections in one pass). And note the startup self-check protects dimension but not model identity — optionally could store model name marker per collection (Qdrant payload/config) to detect mismatch — a small hardening idea, offer it.\n\nTone: direct answer first — \"是的，向量内容必须重编码，但不是'推倒重来'\" — clarify the distinction between 结构重建 (not needed) and 内容重嵌 (needed, cheap, scripted).\n\nKeep it concise, no need for tools. Maybe a small table of what changes/what doesn't. Don't over-engineer the answer. End with offer to execute the switch with the non-destructive path (new collections + flip) if they want.\n\nActually let me reconsider the non-destructive path feasibility with their setup: config.yaml collection names are static (tables_collection: meta_tables_semantic etc.). Rebuild services write to settings.qdrant.collections. A zero-downtime swap = change names to *_qwen37, run rebuild (writes new collections), then... but the query path reads the configured names — flip config once rebuild done. This works with same dimension and is genuinely safer (old vectors kept until verified). For memory collections: 6 more. ES: reindex to new index + alias flip, or just rebuild in place (ES rebuild script presumably deletes+recreates).\n\nFor their dev environment: in-place is fine. Present both briefly.\n\nAlso answer the implicit \"每次都要这样吗\" — yes, every embedding model change requires re-embedding stored vectors; there's no way around it (vectors have no cross-model meaning). Mitigation: (1) source-of-truth data is in PG, rebuild is mechanical; (2) keep model stable; (3) if you switch often, use collection-version naming + alias pattern to make swaps routine.\n\nOne more precision: \"删除现有的向量数据库\" — not the DATABASE (Qdrant server stays), just collections' contents; and source data in PG untouched. So \"重新再来一遍\" = re-run embedding pipeline, not re-enter data.","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"5b2c0d49-3020-480f-923e-9e185a67955f","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"是的——**向量内容必须重编码，这一点绕不开**；但“删除数据库重来”是个误解，实际代价比你想象的小很多。拆开说：\n\n## 为什么绕不开\n\n向量不是数据本身，是某个模型语义空间里的**坐标**。v3 把“销售额”编码成 `[0.12, -0.33, ...]`，qwen3.7 编码同一个词会得到完全不同分布的另一组数——两组坐标虽然都是 1024 个数字，但不在同一个空间里，算余弦相似度就是噪声。这跟维度无关，哪怕维度一样也不行。\n\n所以行业里任何 embedding 模型更换（Pinecone/Weaviate 官方文档也一样）都要求重嵌全部存量向量，没有捷径。\n\n## 但“重来一遍”的真实成本很小\n\n关键：**向量库里没有源头数据，源头都在 PostgreSQL 和业务库里**。\n\n| 东西 | 切换时 |\n|---|---|\n| Qdrant 服务、collection 结构（1024 维）| 不动 |\n| ES mapping | 不动 |\n| 元数据源数据（tables/columns/metrics，在 PG）| 不动 |\n| 维度值源数据（在业务库）| 不动 |\n| 记忆原文 | 不动 |\n| 向量内容（Qdrant 4 个 + ES 向量字段 + 记忆 6 个）| **全部重嵌** |\n\n重嵌不是手工活，是重跑一遍你已有的流水线——就是任务 #10~#12 那轮做过的：元数据重建脚本按 PG 里的活跃行批量编码写回。你这点数据量（元数据 + 维度值撑死几千条，每条约几十 token），按 0.5 元/百万 tokens 算**几分钱、几分钟**的事。记忆那 6 个 collection 直接清空即可，让记忆模块自然重新积累。\n\n## 真正要注意的是：别频繁切\n\n频繁换 embedding 模型才是灾难，不是换一次。所以建议：\n\n1. **一次选好，稳定用下去**——qwen3.7-text-embedding 比 v3/v4 都强，切这次是值得的\n2. 如果以后还想有切换余地，可以把 collection 命名带上模型版本（如 `meta_tables_qwen37`），重建新 collection → 验证 → 翻转 config 里的名字 → 删旧——旧向量全程保留，随时可回滚。开发阶段没必要，生产化之后值得\n3. 一个可选的加固：启动自检目前只校验维度（1024=1024 会静默通过），可以在每个 collection 里存一个模型名标记，启动时校验“向量是不是当前模型编的”，防止忘了重建导致静默劣化\n\n要切的话流程就是：改 `.env` 一行 → 重跑元数据向量重建 + 维度值重建（ES+Qdrant）→ 清空记忆 collections → 重启验证。上一轮整套做下来也就一轮对话的功夫。要开始吗？"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789699995099},{"id":"89ad8def-c6e4-4154-8829-9c763efb3b6a","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"我主要是千问有免费模型，可以用，可能就会频繁切换，这是不是不太好","payload":{"query":"我主要是千问有免费模型，可以用，可能就会频繁切换，这是不是不太好","rawMessage":"我主要是千问有免费模型，可以用，可能就会频繁切换，这是不是不太好","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"},{"id":"624504","name":"image.png","content":"https://comate.baidu.com/api/aidevops/autocomate/rest/autowork/v1/file/stream/624504?authorization=NjFjYWEwODUtMGY0Ni00YTYyLTg1NjEtN2Y0MmJlYWJlNzYx","type":"IMAGE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"7deea211-b0f8-43cb-a279-ddab9902a125","requestedAt":1789700186831,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"89ad8def-c6e4-4154-8829-9c763efb3b6a"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789700186987},{"id":"1dc26980-1b2f-416d-973b-a938c8143d32","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"89ad8def-c6e4-4154-8829-9c763efb3b6a","reportedId":"44204d33-753e-4a14-8c93-aedffc9674a0","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":77.15,"contextUsed":197502,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":1161,"totalDuration":63263},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aaca85cb58a630c138dd525","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":62102},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"b09ec9f3-86d1-4780-b8c7-0e8204c692e9","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user shows their Bailian console free quota page:\n- qwen3.7-text-embedding-flash: 剩 1M / 共 1M tokens, expires 2026/11/30 (73 days left)\n- qwen3.7-text-rerank: 剩 1M / 共 1M, expires 2026/11/30 (73 days)\n- qwen3.7-text-embedding: 剩 1M / 共 1M, expires 2026/10/13 (25 days left!)\n\nThey say: \"我主要是千问有免费模型，可以用，可能就会频繁切换，这是不是不太好\" — \"Mainly because Qwen has free models I can use, and I might switch frequently — is that not good?\"\n\nTheir concern: free quotas (1M tokens each, expiring) tempt them to switch embedding models frequently to chase free quota. Is that bad?\n\nKey points to make:\n\n1. **Yes, frequent switching is bad** — each switch = full re-embed + recall quality jumps around + evaluation becomes impossible (can't compare recall quality across changes). Vector store should be stable infrastructure, not a place to chase free tokens.\n\n2. **But the math says they don't need to chase free quota**: 1M tokens free, but their actual usage is tiny. Let me estimate their real consumption:\n   - Metadata rebuild: tables+columns+metrics+dimension values — say ~5k texts × ~50 tokens ≈ 250k tokens one-time per rebuild\n   - Query-time embedding: each user question embeds 1 query (~20-50 tokens) + maybe dimension value terms. Even 100 questions/day ≈ 5k tokens/day → 150k/month\n   - Memory encoding: small\n   So monthly steady-state is maybe a few hundred thousand tokens at most = **well under 1元/month** at 0.5元/M. The free 1M is basically several months to a year+ of runtime. The REAL cost is not tokens, it's the rebuild chore + quality instability.\n\n3. **Expiry matters more than quota**: qwen3.7-text-embedding free tier expires 2026/10/13 — 25 days away! If they switch to it on free quota and it expires, they either pay (0.5元/M — trivial) or get cut off (用完即停 toggle). The flash variant expires 11/30. So \"free\" is actually a ticking constraint — worse for stability than paying ~0.5元/M.\n\nActually wait — current date: 2026-09-17 per env. So qwen3.7-text-embedding expires 10/13 (25 days), flash 11/30 (73 days). Right.\n\n4. **Recommendation**:\n   - Don't treat embedding model as a free-quota rotation item. Pick one (qwen3.7-text-embedding is the best; flash is the cheap tier), pay the trivial cost after free quota runs out, and freeze it.\n   - If they want to experiment with models, do it in an eval harness, not in production config. Or use the collection-versioning pattern so experimentation never touches the stable store.\n   - If cost is truly the concern: their entire monthly embedding spend at paid rate is ~0.x 元 — the free quota chase saves them less than a coffee per year, while each switch costs a rebuild + recall regression risk + the 25-day expiry cliff.\n   - Also: 1M free is enough for the one-time switch + months of queries. Use it, then pay pennies.\n\n5. Offer a concrete stability mechanism (optional): \n   - Freeze the model in .env with a comment\n   - Add the collection model-marker hardening so accidental switches fail fast at startup (protects against the \"forgot to rebuild\" silent degradation)\n   \n6. Also worth noting: rerank model (qwen3.7-text-rerank) — separate topic, they have free quota there too; rerank does NOT require re-embedding (it's cross-encoder scoring at query time) — switching rerank IS free and safe! That's a useful distinction: rerank can be switched freely (no index to rebuild), embedding cannot. If they want to \"use free models\", the rerank slot is the safe place to experiment. That's a genuinely useful insight for them.\n\nWait — do they even use a rerank model currently? I haven't seen rerank in the config (config.py showed ElasticsearchConfig, metadata_recall...). Not sure. Don't assert; phrase conditionally: \"如果以后要接 rerank\" — the project currently may not have rerank integrated. Mention it as the safe slot IF they add one.\n\nStructure the answer:\n- 直接回答：对，频繁切换 embedding 模型是坏事，但你的场景其实不需要频繁切换\n- 算账：你的真实用量 vs 免费额度 vs 付费价格 → 免费额度能覆盖很久，付费也只是几毛钱\n- 到期时间陷阱：qwen3.7-text-embedding 免费额度 25 天后到期（10/13）→ \"免费\"反而是稳定性陷阱\n- 建议策略：embedding 一次选定冻结（推荐 qwen3.7-text-embedding 或 flash），额度用完就付，每月几毛钱\n- 可以随便换的位置：rerank（查询时打分，不需要重建向量库）——想蹭免费额度在这个位置蹭\n- 可选加固：collection 模型标记，防误切\n\nKeep it tight. No tools needed — all info in hand. Maybe use a tiny cost table.\n\nCost estimate details:\n- 0.5元/M (qwen3.7-text-embedding paid)\n- Their rebuild: metadata ~5k texts... honestly I don't know exact counts; keep rough: \"撑死几十万 token，几分钱\"\n- Query: every question embeds the question text only (metadata recall embeds query; dimension values pre-embedded). ~50 tokens/question. 1000 questions/month = 50k tokens = 0.025元. Memory encoding small.\nSo monthly ≈ 毛毛雨. State: \"一年也到不了一杯奶茶钱\".\n\nAlso the free quota already includes the rebuild: rebuild once (~0.3M tokens) + months of queries fits in 1M.\n\nOne nuance: \"用完即停\" toggle visible in screenshot — if enabled, service stops when quota exhausted. Recommend NOT enabling it for the model they rely on... actually the toggle \"用完即停\" presumably means when free quota exhausted, stop instead of falling to paid billing. If they keep it off (未开启 status shown), after free quota exhausts it falls through to paid billing automatically — that's actually GOOD for stability: no cliff, just starts costing pennies. So advise: keep 用完即停 off → free quota acts as a credit buffer, then seamlessly paid at 0.5元/M. That reframes \"free expiring\" from cliff to cushion. \n\nSo final strategy:\n1. 切到 qwen3.7-text-embedding（或 flash），保持用完即停关闭 → 免费额度用完后自动转付费，每月几毛钱，无断崖\n2. 冻结不轻易动\n3. 想体验新模型 → rerank 位/评测环境，不动生产 embedding\n4. 可选：collection 模型标记加固\n\nThat's the answer. Concise.","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"7bef2e60-3def-4737-a3bf-d48a3839e53e","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"对，频繁切换确实不好——但先把账算清楚，你会发现**你根本不需要频繁切换**。\n\n## 你的真实用量 vs 免费额度\n\n| 项目 | 消耗 |\n|---|---|\n| 一次性重建（元数据 + 维度值，几千条短文本）| 约 0.2~0.3M tokens |\n| 查询时编码（每个问题 ~50 token）| 1000 个问题/月 ≈ 0.05M |\n| 记忆编码 | 很小 |\n\n**你的系统一个月稳态消耗也就几十万 token，免费额度 1M 够用大半年**。额度用完转付费是 0.5 元/百万 tokens——一个月几毛钱，一年不到一杯奶茶钱。为了省几毛钱频繁重建向量库，是花大成本省小钱。\n\n## 截图里真正的陷阱：到期时间\n\n注意 `qwen3.7-text-embedding` 免费额度 **2026/10/13 到期，只剩 25 天**。如果你把它当“免费模型”用，25 天后就面临“续费还是再切一次”的选择——免费额度反而成了强迫你切换的计时炸弹。\n\n解法就在你截图里：**「用完即停」开关保持关闭**。这样免费额度只是个抵扣券，用完自动转付费（0.5 元/M），没有断崖，服务不中断。免费部分白拿，到期无痛过渡。\n\n## 建议的姿势\n\n1. **embedding 一次选定，冻结**：推荐 `qwen3.7-text-embedding`（比 flash 效果好，付费后也就几毛钱）。切这一次值得，之后把它当基础设施，不再动\n2. **想白嫖新模型，去不影响向量库的位置**：你截图里还有个 `qwen3.7-text-rerank`（1M 免费）——rerank 是查询时对召回结果重排序的打分模型，**不产生存储向量，切换零成本**，随便换。这才是适合追免费额度的位置（不过项目目前还没接 rerank，要接的话是个独立的增量功能）\n3. **可选加固**：给每个 Qdrant collection 存一个“编码模型名”标记，启动时校验——防止哪天误切了模型配置，静默劣化一个月才发现\n\n所以回答你的问题：不是“不能切”，是“不值得常切”。切这一次（v3 → qwen3.7），开着用完即停转付费，然后冻结。要现在开始切吗？"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789700250788},{"id":"43f8020a-c4e7-4622-8d59-e4ff3590e730","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"这4个你推荐用哪个，我还有硅基流动的20元没有使用呢","payload":{"query":"这4个你推荐用哪个，我还有硅基流动的20元没有使用呢","rawMessage":"这4个你推荐用哪个，我还有硅基流动的20元没有使用呢","model":{"displ