)\n\nRename plan: `provider: dashscope` → `provider: openai_compatible`? Or keep the semantic \"remote OpenAI-compatible\". The llm section uses `provider: openai-compatible` (kebab). For embedding, I'd use the same style for consistency: `openai-compatible`. Two code changes:\n- embedding_client.py:45: `if self.config.provider == \"openai-compatible\":`\n- config.py:162: `return self.model_name if self.provider == \"openai-compatible\" else self.model`\n\nHmm, but wait — is this scope creep? The switch is \"change embedding provider service\". Renaming the provider value makes the config truthful and matches the llm section's naming convention. It's 3 lines total (config.yaml + 2 py lines). The user values 优雅/不做无用兼容. The value \"dashscope\" pointing to siliconflow would be actively wrong. I'll do the rename — it's minimal and coherent. Kebab-case \"openai-compatible\" to match llm section.\n\nAlso EmbeddingConfig docstring at :144 says \"provider 决定走云端兼容接口还是本地推理服务\" — already generic, good. Maybe update comment to name the two values? config.yaml comment currently says \"切回本地推理服务时改为 provider: local\" — fine.\n\nWait, also check: are there tests referencing provider \"dashscope\"? Let me grep tests dir. Actually the grep above covered app/ only. Let me grep whole repo for `\"dashscope\"` in tests. Quick check.\n\nAlso active_model \"用于记忆编码器命名等场景\" — where is active_model used? Memory encoder naming. If memory collections don't exist yet, no issue. After switch active_model = \"Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B\". Fine.\n\nNow the full execution plan:\n\n1. Grep tests for dashscope provider references (quick).\n2. Edit config.yaml embedding section (SiliconFlow active + Bailian commented).\n3. Edit .env: add SILICONFLOW_API_KEY.\n4. Edit embedding_client.py:45 + config.py:162 (provider rename).\n5. Quick smoke: run a tiny python snippet to init settings + embedding client and embed 1 text (validates OmegaConf env resolution + code path) — actually the rebuild scripts will do this anyway. But a 5-second check before deleting collections is worth it. Use `uv run python -c \"...\"` with asyncio to call aembed_query and print len. This validates everything before destructive step.\n6. Delete meta_dimension_values_semantic collection.\n7. Run build_meta_vectors (recreates 3 meta collections, rebuilds).\n8. Run build_dimension_value_indexes (recreates ES index + alias switch, rebuilds Qdrant dim values).\n9. Restart backend: kill 95334/95336 tree, start `uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload` in background, wait for startup, check log for \"Embedding 客户端已初始化：provider=openai-compatible model=Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B dimensions=1024\" and no verify_dimension error, hit /health or similar.\n10. Verify Qdrant counts.\n11. Commit (config.yaml + embedding_client.py + config.py). .env gitignored.\n\nAbout restarting the user's uvicorn: it's their terminal process. I'll kill it and relaunch in background via my Bash run_in_background with output saved. I must tell the user clearly. Alternatively — I could ask... no, we're executing an approved plan \"改配置 → 重建 → 自检，一轮搞定\". 自检 = startup check. Proceed.\n\nHmm wait, one consideration on `--reload`: if I start uvicorn from my Bash tool with run_in_background, it persists after my session? Background tasks in this harness keep running (output saved to file). It's the same behavior as nohup-ish. Fine. I'll note to the user that the backend now runs in background and they can Ctrl-C… they can't Ctrl-C a background task from their terminal. Hmm — that could annoy the user later (\"how do I stop it?\"). I'll tell them: `kill <pid>` or I can stop it next time. Alternatively, leave restart to the user with a one-liner instruction. \n\nLet me reconsider: the \"don't ask questions\" instruction is about not stalling the workflow. Telling the user \"重启后端完成自检\" isn't a question. But leaving the task 90% done forces a manual step. The spirit of \"一轮搞定\" → I'll restart it myself in background and clearly report. If they