ted","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\n6x30字: 78.1s dim=1024\n6x150字: 89.1s dim=1024\n6x600字: 30.8s dim=1024\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"5n4rox","output":"6x30字: 78.1s dim=1024\n6x150字: 89.1s dim=1024\n6x600字: 30.8s dim=1024\n","exitCode":0,"inBackground":false}}}]},{"id":"6aacafdf2333250053159f10","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":92794},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"dc2de688-0172-4a30-8fe2-12239f7f6c83","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Wow — SiliconFlow's Qwen3-Embedding-8B is SLOW: even 6 short texts took 78s! And 6x600字 took only 30.8s?? That's inverted — suggesting server-side variance/queueing rather than input-size-bound. This is slow-tier/free-tier style latency variance (the user has ¥20 credit — standard tier, but 8B embedding may be queued).\n\n78-89s for 6 texts is terrible. The rebuild would need 655/6 ≈ 110 batches × ~80s ≈ 2.4 hours! That's unusable — and at runtime, metadata recall embeds query terms (max 8 terms, concurrent 4) — 78s per query embed would make the agent feel dead. This is a real product problem, not just rebuild pain.\n\nWait — let me reconsider. Maybe the first requests include cold-start. The three calls: 78s, 89s, 31s. Highly variable. Let me re-test short texts a few times to see if latency improves (warm) — maybe it was a temporary queue.\n\nAlso important: the user's earlier choice context — they wanted to use their ¥20 SiliconFlow credit, and worried about频繁切换 free quotas. I recommended 8B. But if 8B on SiliconFlow is this slow at query time, the agent's retrieval latency will be unacceptable. Maybe 0.6B (1024 dims, matches!) would be much faster. Recall the 4 models: 8B@4096, 4B@2560, 0.6B@1024. Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B native dim is 1024 — same as current vector_size, no structural change either!\n\nLet me first check whether the slowness is transient. Run