tency for 6 short texts. So realistic per-batch latency ≈ 20-25s, and the 0.3s is response caching for identical texts.\n\nFor the rebuild: 110 batches × ~22s ≈ 40 minutes. Tolerable with resume + a bigger timeout (60s). But for RUNTIME: query embedding — 1 short query text per call ≈ maybe 5-10s? Let me check single-query latency since that's what the agent does per retrieval term (metadata recall does up to 8 terms with concurrency 4). A single text query embed taking multiple seconds on every user question is noticeable but might be acceptable... but 22s for 6 texts suggests single text ≈ 4-8s. Hmm.\n\nWait, actually — aembed_query also might hit different batching. Let me measure single-query latency (this is the runtime-critical path). Also measure 0.6B for comparison — it's the same native dim 1024, much smaller model, likely 10x faster, MTEB 70.58 is for 8B but 0.6B still scores decently (64-ish). If single-query latency on 8B is <2s, keep 8B with timeout 60-90s and grind through the rebuild. If it's 5s+, consider 0.6B.\n\nLet me test: single text on 8B, then single text on 0.6B, a few runs each with distinct texts (avoid cache).","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"14a00226-4d40-4c44-838d-692f7148abc1","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"稳定后约 22s/批（6 条），最后一次 0.3s 是服务端对相同输入的缓存。重建 655 点约 110 批 ≈ 40 分钟，可以靠续建磨过去；但关键在**运行时查询延迟**——每次召回都要现场向量化。测一下单条查询的真实延迟，并和 0.6B 对比："},{"id":"call_6ac8bd4bdebf4ecaa4e7c4a0","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"uv run python -c \"\nimport time, asyncio\nfrom langchain_openai import OpenAIEmbeddings\nfrom app.core.config import settings\n\ndef mk(model):\n    return OpenAIEmbeddings(\n        model=model, dimensions=1024, api_key=settings.embedding.api_key,\n        base_url=settings.embedding.base_url, request_timeout=120,\n        max_retries=0, chunk_size=6, check_embedding_ctx_length=False,\n    )\n\nqueries = [\n    '家具品类的销售额达成情况怎么样',\n    '圣保罗州客户订单的延迟率',\n    '信用卡支付方式占比多少',\n    ' delayed 订单的同比变化',\n]\n\nasync def bench(model):\n    client = mk(model)\n    lat = []\n    for q in queries:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        await client.aembed_query(q)\n        lat.append(time.perf_counter() - t0)\n    print(model, '->', ' / '.join(f'{x:.2f}s' for x in lat))\n\nasync def main():\n    await bench('Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B')\n    await bench('Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B')\n\nasyncio.run(main())\n\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Benchmark single-query latency 8B vs 0.6B"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nQwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B -> 5.74s / 0.20s / 2.28s / 1.34s\nQwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B -> 0.31s / 0.10s / 0.21s / 0.10s\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"6fc3ud","output":"Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B -> 5.74s / 0.20s / 2.28s / 1.34s\nQwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B -> 0.31s / 0.10s / 0.21s / 0.10s\n","exitCode":0,"inBackground":false}}}]},{"id":"6aacb060b7e22404df6e4e77","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":57713},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"4465e5e9-37df-4125-b8e6-e4492e593ed4","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Now we have the real picture:\n\n- **8B**: single query 1.3-5.7s (after cold start), batch of 6 ≈ 22s. First call cold ~5.7s.\n- **0.6B**: single query 0.1-0.3s. 20-50x faster.\n\nRuntime impact of 8B:\n- metadata_recall: up to 8 recall terms, max 4 concurrent → 2 waves × ~2-5s = 5-10s added latency per retrieval step. Plus dimension value semantic search, memory lookups. Each user question would feel noticeably slower.\n- Question understanding/routing also embeds the question (context recall).\n\nThis is a serious runtime regression. The user cares about UX (they've been polishing the frontend progress UX all session). An extra 5-10s before any visible progress on every query is bad.\n\nQuality tradeoff: MTEB multilingual — 8B: 70.58, 4B: ~69+, 0.6B: ~64.3. For this domain (e-commerce table/column/metric/dimension-value retrieval with Chinese business terms), 0.6B is usually plenty, especially combined with ES keyword search + RRF fusion (the architecture already fuses lexical + semantic, which cushions embedding quality differences).\n\nWhat about 4B? dims 2560 native, MRL to 1024. Latency probably between. Let me quickly benchmark 4B single-query too — if it's ~0.5s it could be the sweet spot (better quality than 0.6B, still fast). Actually let me benchmark 4B before deciding.\n\nAlso should verify quality difference matters at all here. Hard to evaluate quality without a test set. The pragmatic approach: benchmark 4B; then present the tradeoff to the user? But instruction: don't ask questions, proceed. Hmm — but this is a real decision point affecting product quality. The user approved \"切到 8B\" based on my recommendation ($0.04/M, top MTEB). The new fact is: SiliconFlow's serving latency for 8B is 10-50x worse than 0.6B. That fact was not known at approval time.\n\nThe user's own earlier concern was about cost/quota churn, not latency. But they also spent the whole session polishing UX snappiness (progress UI). I think the right move:\n\n1. Benchmark 4B.\n2. Decide: if 4B single-query ≲0.5s → recommend 4B@1024 (MRL) — quality close to 8B, speed close to 0.6B. If 4B is also slow (e.g. 2s+), then it's 8B (slow) vs 0.6B (fast).\n\nActually wait — let me reconsider whether query latency of ~2s (8B) is truly a problem. The agent pipeline: user question → context recall embeds question + recall terms (concurrent 4). With 8B: cold call 5.7s, warm 1.3-2.3s. Per retrieval round ≈ 2-6s extra. For a data-analysis agent whose LLM thinking takes 30s+, an extra 2-5s is noticeable but not fatal. BUT the 22s per 6-text batch hits the *rebuild* and any bulk paths (dimension value indexing is offline; memory encoding batches — memory writes would batch texts too, 22s per write batch could time out the 30s limit and break memory writes at runtime!).\n\nTimeout config is 30s — bulk-ish runtime paths (memory episodic encoding of a batch) would exceed it intermittently. We already saw APITimeoutError twice during rebuild. That means runtime memory writes with >1-2 texts risk timeouts → memory module would be flaky.\n\nOptions:\nA. Keep 8B, raise timeout_seconds to 60-90. Rebuild ~40min (grind with resume). Runtime: query embeds 1.3-5.7s each, memory writes slower but under 60s timeout. Quality best.\nB. Switch to 0.6B (native 1024): everything fast (0.1-0.3s), rebuild minutes, zero timeout risk. Quality lowest of the three but adequate with ES+RRF fusion.\nC. 4B @1024 (MRL): benchmark needed.\n\nThe honest engineering answer: SiliconFlow's 8B embedding serving is slow enough to hurt. The 4B might be the sweet spot. Let me benchmark 4B single query + batch of 6, then decide and report transparently to the user. Since the user already approved \"切换到 SiliconFlow\"（the provider switch is approved; the specific model choice within SiliconFlow was my recommendation), switching the model *within the same provider* to fix a measured performance problem is within the spirit of the approval — but I should transparently report the data and decision. If 4B is fast (≤0.5s), I'd switch to 4B: quality 69.35 vs 70.58 (basically identical), speed close to 0.6B. That's clearly the right call. If 4B is slow too, then I face 8B vs 0.6B — bigger quality gap (70.58 vs 64.3) — then maybe keep 8B with timeout 90 and grind rebuild? Hmm, but runtime query latency 2-6s per call × multiple calls per turn is a real UX regression.\n\nLet me get 4B data first.","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"86ec7191-9b91-4894-bafa-531c0db2b2f2","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"8B 单条查询 1.3–5.7s（对比 0.6B 的 0.1–0.3s），而且批处理 22s/批已经把运行时 30s 硬超时打爆了（两次重建失败都是这个原因，记忆写入这类批量路径运行时也会踩）。测一下中间档 4B："},{"id":"call_644237a1b0674b0dab75352a","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"uv run python -