376e","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Confirmed the full picture:\n\n1. **Model level**: Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-4B is a text-only embedding model. The multimodal sibling in their SiliconFlow screenshot was Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B (image+text). Audio/video have no SiliconFlow Qwen embedding offering in that list.\n\n2. **Code level**: \n   - The embedding client (`EmbeddingClientManager`) only exposes text embedding (`aembed_query(text: str)` / `aembed_documents(texts)` via OpenAIEmbeddings/HuggingFaceEndpointEmbeddings) — text-only.\n   - The only memory encoder implemented is `TextMemoryEncoder` (`app/agent/memory/encoders/text.py`, `encoders/__init__.py` exports only TextMemoryEncoder; factory wires TextMemoryEncoder only).\n   - The Qdrant memory repository has plumbing for perceptual collections by modality (text/image/audio/video) with `modality` payload index and asset_id — i.e., the storage layer reserved slots for multimodal, but no encoder exists to generate vectors for image/audio/video. Also those collections don't exist yet (never written to).\n\nSo the answer: 是 — the current embedding pipeline is text-only, at both the model level (Qwen3-Embedding series are text-only) and the code level (only TextMemoryEncoder exists). The perceptual image/audio/video collections are reserved scaffolding (collection routing + payload schema) but nothing generates their vectors today. If multimodal memory is needed later: either a multimodal embedding model (e.g., Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B, 4096 dims — note dim mismatch with our 1024 vector_size; would need a separate collection with own vector_size since MRL... does VL-Embedding support MRL down to 1024? Qwen3-VL-Embedding docs — not sure; would need separate collection config anyway) or caption-then-embed (image → VL model caption → text embedding, reuses current 4B pipeline, keeps one vector space).\n\nAlso worth noting: in the business metadata retrieval pipeline (tables/columns/metrics/dimension values), everything embedded is text by design (business names, descriptions, enum values) — multimodal isn't relevant there.\n\nShould I check SiliconFlow for whether Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B supports image input via their API? From the user's screenshot earlier: \"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B 4096维32K\" — it's in their model list. I know Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B supports text+image (screenshot interleaved) embedding. I don't need to web-search for this answer; the question is about *our* setup (\"这个是只支持文本的向量生成吗?\"). \"这个\" most likely = the embedding model we just switched to / our embedding setup. Answer directly with the two levels + the reserved collections fact + the two future options. Keep it concise.\n\nNo task tracking needed for a Q&A. Don't create tasks.","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"5bbc764f-f010-4511-9da4-3e3a2442f38b","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"是的，**当前整条链路只支持文本**，可以从两层看：\n\n**模型层**：刚切换的 `Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-4B` 是纯文本 embedding 模型（Qwen3-Embedding 全系列 0.6B/4B/8B 都只收文本）。硅基流动截图里那个 `Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B` 才是图文多模态版本，但我们没选它。\n\n**代码层**：向量生成入口只有一个 —— [`app/clients/embedding_client.py`](/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/clients/embedding_client.py) 的 `aembed_query(text: str)` / `aembed_documents(texts)`，底层 `OpenAIEmbeddings` 只发文本。业务侧所有向量化对象也都是文本：表/字段/指标的名称与描述、维度值枚举、召回词、记忆内容。\n\n有一个**预留但未启用**的口子：记忆模块的仓储层已经为多模态留了位置 —— [`qdrant_memory_repository.py:58-63`](/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/app/repositories/memory/qdrant_memory_repository.py#L58-63) 给 PERCEPTUAL 记忆按模态路由到 4 个独立 collection（`perceptual_text/image/audio/video`），payload 里也有 `modality`、`asset_id` 索引字段。但编码器目前只实现了 `TextMemoryEncoder`（`app/agent/memory/encoders/` 下唯一导出），image/audio/video 的向量今天没有任何代码会生成，那几个 collection 也从未被创建过。这是“存储层预留插槽、编码层未实现”的状态。\n\n将来如果要接图片记忆，有两条路：\n\n1. **描述转写**（推荐起步）：图片 → VL 模型生成文字描述 → 走现有 4B 文本 embedding。零结构改动、单一向量空间、文本检索直接可用。\n2. **真多模态 embedding**：换/加 `Qwen3-VL-Embedding-8B`（4096 维），图文同一向量空间，可“以文搜图”。但它维度和现有 1024 不一致，得为图片单独建 collection 配独立 `vector_size`，qdrant 配置和仓储层都要跟着动。\n\n业务元数据检索那条线（表/字段/指标/维度值）不涉及这个问题——它处理的本来就是纯文本。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789703677896},{"id":"7b0d229e-e24d-42cb-b157-d84bf46c0719","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"pdf算是文本吗","payload":{"query":"pdf算是文本吗","rawMessage":"pdf算是文本吗","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"frontend/components/insight-agent/execution-panel.tsx","name":"execution-panel.tsx","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"5feff8e5-a402-4e6f-9ba2-998c51e2da14","requestedAt":1789703744867,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"7b0d229e-e24d-42cb-b157-d84bf46c0719"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"bcc9ce000688653c6d7465fa24c98828a8335cc1","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789703744881},{"id":"eb3667ec-88c1-4458-b30b-ed26f3a02d53","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"7b0d229e-e24d-42cb-b157-d84bf46c0719","reportedId":"c2ca6364-dd34-445d-9c06-0be587acd7cc","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":30.93,"contextUsed":79189,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":794,"totalDuration":42491},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6aacb64152c86817577a3a34","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":15455},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"a45f9e57-6ca1-405e-bd63-fb85dba124be","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"pdf算是文本吗\" — \"Does PDF count as text?\"\n\nContext: We just discussed that the embedding pipeline is text-only. The user is now asking whether PDF counts as text — presumably thinking about whether PDFs could be embedded through this text embedding pipeline (e.g., knowledge base documents, memory).\n\nThe answer needs to be precise:\n\n- A PDF file is not, by itself, text — it's a binary document format that *may contain* a text layer (digital PDF) or may just be scanned images (扫描件).\n- For the embedding pipeline: PDFs must first go through **parsing/extraction** (e.g., PyMuPDF/pdfplumber extracts text layer; OCR for scanned pages) → then the extracted text can be embedded by the 4B model. So the embedding model never \"sees\" the PDF; it sees extracted text.\n- Our current codebase: is there any PDF handling? Let me think — the project is a data analysis agent. There's file upload handling? The conversation summary mentioned \"附件和多模态输入的统一元数据表\" in app/models/memory.py:117 — attachments metadata table. Is there any attachment/PDF processing in the codebase? Let me check quickly — grep for pdf in app/.\n\nActually, I should check whether the project has any PDF-related code to ground the answer in \"our current pipeline\" vs \"in general\". Let me grep.\n\nThe conceptual answer:\n1. 概念上：PDF 是文档容器，不是文本。数字版 PDF 含文本层（可直接抽取）；扫描版是图片（需要 OCR）。\n2. 对 embedding 流水线而言：只要先抽取成文本，就能进现有 4B 流水线。embedding 模型本身永远只吃纯文本字符串。\n3. 项目现状：有没有 PDF 处理代码？查一下。\n\nAlso there's a subtlety: LangChain OpenAIEmbeddings with check_embedding_ctx_length=False sends the raw string — long PDFs would need chunking (RAG-style splitting) before embedding. And SiliconFlow 4B has 32K context — plenty per chunk.\n\nLet me grep for pdf/attachment handling in the codebase to be accurate about project state.","startTime":1791428023749,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023749},{"id":"call_b3745be1cb3a4e83b30b979f","type":"TOOL","toolName":"grep_content","params":{"-i":"true","-n":"true","gl