se / etc) + indeterminate/determinate bar + elapsed\n- Milestone list (ProgressMilestoneRow: icon, label, duration, phases chain, detail)\n- renderMilestones\n\nV3 design (清晰可控):\n- **顶部压缩**: one row: segmented 4-phase mini bar (理解→划分→执行→报告) + current activity text + elapsed. The 4 segments map to milestones: understand/plan/execute(report? tasks+report). Each segment: done (filled blue), running (animated), pending (gray). Under it small text: current headline + elapsed.\n- **主体活动流**: reverse chronological feed of \"activity rows\". What's an activity row? Derive from events: for each meaningful event (planner.started/completed/failed, context.*, analysis_task_*, tool-phase events, report events, run.*) produce a row {icon status, label, time, duration?, expandable detail}. But we already have milestones with phases. Hmm — careful about scope: rebuilding the whole feed logic is big. Simpler robust approach: **activity feed = flattened list of grouped displayEvents** (the ones shown in 工具与事件 tab via nodeGroups/EventDetails) in reverse-chronological order, each row one line with StatusIcon + displayLabel + time, click → expand EventDetails. That's genuinely \"Devin activity feed\" and reuses existing displayLabel/itemStatus machinery. Plus keep the milestone timeline as a compact segmented bar at top.\n\nActually wait — there's already the \"工具与事件\" tab showing nodeGroups with EventDetails. The 进度 tab v3 could become: top = compact segmented progress + current activity; middle = 活动流 (reverse-chron flattened events, one line each, expandable); bottom = task checklist (TaskCard-like). The 工具与事件 tab stays as-is (grouped by node).\n\nBut hmm, \"清晰可控\" — don't overbuild. The activity feed rows: use compactAllEvents displayEvents (already deduped/merged) sorted by eventOrder DESC; each row: StatusIcon + displayLabel(event) + relative time (+duration if derivable) + expandable <details> with EventDetails. Maybe cap display (show all, it's scrollable).\n\nLet me look at the 