       <div className=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n              <div className=\"truncate text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-600\">{task.question || `任务 ${index + 1}`}</div>\n              <div className=\"truncate text-[10px] text-slate-400\">\n                {task.status === \"running\" ? task.phase || \"执行中\"\n                  : task.status === \"success\" ? \"已完成\"\n                  : task.status === \"failed\" ? task.error || \"执行失败\"\n                  : task.status === \"partial\" ? task.error || \"部分完成\"\n                  : \"等待执行\"}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nTaskSummary fields: question, status, phase, error, task_id — verify TaskSummary interface exists with phase/error optional. From buildTasks: sets phase/error conditionally. The interface — let me check it's declared (type TaskSummary). It's exported; buildTasks constructs objects without phase initially — so optional. OK.\n\nActivity feed:\n```tsx\nfunction ProgressActivityFeed({ events }: { events: DebugEvent[] }) {\n  const items = displayEvents(compactAllEvents(events)).slice().reverse();\n  if (!items.length) return null;\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-3.5\">\n      <div className=\"text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400\">执行明细</div>\n      <div className=\"mt-2 space-y-0.5\">\n        {items.map((item) => <EventDetails key={item.key} event={item.event} status={item.status} />)}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nHeader + segments in ProgressView:\n```tsx\n  const segments = milestones.map((milestone) => ({\n    key: milestone.key,\n    status: runCompleted && !interrupted ? \"success\" as RunStatus : milestone.status,\n  }));\n```\nRender:\n```tsx\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n        {headlineIcon}\n        <span className={\"text-sm font-extrabold \" + headlineColor}>{headline.text}</span>\n        <span className=\"ml-auto shrink-0 text-[10px] font-bold text-slate-400\">已执行 {formatDuration(elapsedMs) || \"0 秒\"}</span>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"mt-2.5 flex h-1.5 gap-1\">\n        {segments.length\n          ? segments.map((segment) => (\n              <div key={segment.key} className={\"h-full flex-1 rounded-full \" + segmentColor(segment.status)} />\n            ))\n          : <div className={\"h-full flex-1 animate-pulse rounded-full \" + barTone} />}\n      </div>\n      {milestones.length > 0 && (\n        <div className=\"mt-4 space-y-3 border-t border-slate-100 pt-3.5\">\n          {milestones.map((milestone) => <ProgressMilestoneRow key={milestone.key} milestone={milestone} />)}\n        </div>\n      )}\n      {!milestones.length && <div className=\"py-10 text-center text-xs text-slate-400\">提交问题后显示执行进度</div>}\n      <ProgressActivityFeed events={ordered} />\n      {tasks.length > 0 && <ProgressTaskList tasks={tasks} />}\n    </div>\n  );\n```\n\nsegmentColor helper:\n```ts\nfunction segmentColor(status: RunStatus) {\n  if (status === \"failed\") return \"bg-rose-500\";\n  if (status === \"running\") return \"bg-blue-500 animate-pulse\";\n  if (status === \"success\") return \"bg-blue-400\";\n  if (status === \"partial\") return \"bg-amber-400\";\n  if (status === \"waiting\") return \"bg-amber-400\";\n  return \"bg-slate-200\";\n}\n```\nHmm RunStatus values — need to check the union. StatusIcon handles which? Let me check RunStatus type + StatusIcon quickly. RunStatus used: \"success\"|\"failed\"|\"running\"|\"partial\"|\"pending\"...? grep type RunStatus.\n\nAlso remove now-unused: percent, done, terminalEvents? elapsedMs uses terminalEvents (endMs for non-live) — keep terminalEvents/endMs. percent/done/barTone: barTone reused for empty-segment pulse. percent & done variables removed.\n\nWait — `runCompleted && !interrupted ? success` — if failed, keep milestone statuses (last running marked failed already). Actually simpler: segments 