ilt":true}]},{"id":"6aacd232233325005315d87f","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":17392},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"b2db2cd0-045b-4327-8ba8-cb0fc4fd18a9","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Also — the live thinking section: when live, it auto-expands with max-h-24. But it's now BELOW the stages; during early run (no stages yet) thinking shows directly — fine. \n\nOne more consideration for \"清晰可控\": the plan milestone in deriveRunStages could also show the error detail like the panel (planErrorDetail)? The chat stage detail for plan failure — currently no error shown in bubble. Add: detail on plan stage = error message when failed? Consistent with panel. Small addition:\n\nIn deriveRunStages plan stage:\n```ts\n    stages.push({\n      key: \"plan\",\n      label: \"划分分析任务\",\n      status,\n      detail: status === \"failed\"\n        ? (planErrorMessage(events) ?? (tasks.length ? `${tasks.length} 个任务` : undefined))\n        : tasks.length ? `${tasks.length} 个任务` : undefined,\n    });\n```\nWhere planErrorMessage finds planner.failed/analysis_plan failed error_message/error. Let me add a small helper. Worth it — 失败原因 in bubble matches the panel. \n\n```ts\nfunction planFailureMessage(events: DebugEvent[]): string | undefined {\n  for (const event of events) {\n    if (event.type === \"planner.failed\" || (customEventOf(event, \"analysis_plan\") && event.status === \"failed\")) {\n      const message = [event.payload.error_message, event.payload.error].find(\n        (value): value is string => typeof value === \"string\" && value !== \"\",\n      );\n      if (message) return message;\n    }\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n```\nAnd detail: `status === \"failed\" ? planFailureMessage(events) : tasks.length ? ... : undefined` — hmm keep task count too? When failed, show error instead. OK.\n\nThen tsc + commit + done. Also update the summary chip? Not needed.","startTime":1791428023750,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023750},{"id":"8e292dec-61d1-4d70-b6