st found = events.find((event) => !STREAM_EVENT_TYPES.has(event.type) && progressKind(event) === \"progress\" && eventCategory(event));\n  return found ? eventCategory(found) : null;\n}\n```\n\nWait — progressKind(event) === \"progress\" also excludes tool.progress with custom_type reasoning — good (they're thinking sub-products). But it also includes tool.progress with custom_type analysis_plan → planning ✓.\n\n`CapabilityIcon`:\n\n```tsx\nfunction CapabilityIcon({ category, className }: { category: EventCategory | null; className: string }) {\n  if (!category) return null;\n  const Icon = CATEGORY_ICONS[category];\n  return <Icon className={(category === \"thinking\" ? \"text-violet-500 \" : \"text-slate-400 \") + className} />;\n}\n```\n\nHmm, but thinking color violet; others slate-400. Put tone in the table? One tone map is cleaner:\n\n```tsx\nconst CATEGORY_TONES: Record<EventCategory, string> = {\n  thinking: \"text-violet-500\",\n  planning: \"text-slate-400\",\n  route: \"text-slate-400\",\n  context: \"text-slate-400\",\n  data: \"text-slate-400\",\n  report: \"text-slate-400\",\n  confirm: \"text-slate-400\",\n  run: \"text-slate-400\",\n};\n```\n\nFine — keeps future recoloring one-place. \n\n**3. EventDetails** — add after `{title || event.step}`:\n`<CapabilityIcon category={eventCategory(event)} className=\"ml-1 inline-block size-3.5 shrink-0 align-[-2px]\" />`\n\nNote lucide SVG is inline by default (display inline?). Lucide icons render `<svg>` which is inline by default → inside the bold span works with align tweak.\n\n**4. StepCard** — title span `{group.step}` → prepend:\n`<CapabilityIcon category={groupCategory(group.events) ?? (group.tasks.length ? \"data\" : null)} className=\"mr-1 inline-block size-3.5 shrink-0 align-[-2px]\" />`\n\nAlso node Drawer trigger inside StepCard: `节点：{node.node}` → prepend icon from node.events (DisplayEvent[]) → `groupCategory(node.events.map((item) => item.event))`.\n\n**5. TaskCard trigger** — `{group.taskId}` → 