essKind(event);\nconst type = event.type;\nif (kind === \"reasoning\" || kind === \"llm\"\n  || type === \"reasoning_chunk\" || type === \"reasoning_result\"\n  || type === \"llm_chunk\" || type === \"llm_result\") return \"thinking\";\n```\n\nOr simpler: normalize first: `const rawType = typeof event.payload.custom_type === \"string\" ? event.payload.custom_type : event.type;` then match rawType against the names. That's actually a cleaner universal approach — custom_type IS the original type in harness mode. So:\n\n```ts\nfunction eventCategory(event: DebugEvent): EventCategory | null {\n  const kind = progressKind(event);\n  if (kind === \"reasoning\" || kind === \"llm\") return \"thinking\";\n  const rawType = typeof event.payload.custom_type === \"string\" ? event.payload.custom_type : event.type;\n  if (rawType === \"question_route\") return \"route\";\n  if (rawType === \"analysis_plan\" || rawType === \"report_plan_result\" || rawType.startsWith(\"planner.\")) return \"planning\";\n  if (rawType === \"analysis_task_phase\" || rawType === \"analysis_task_resolved\" || rawType === \"analysis_task_result\") return \"data\";\n  if (rawType === \"rendered_report\") return \"report\";\n  ...context/confirm/run checks remain on event.type...\n}\n```\n\nThis is cleaner AND fixes the old-agent path. Note context./planner./confirmation./run. events in old agent are direct types with no custom_type → rawType = type → same checks work. And harness planner.* events: type startsWith \"planner.\" — rawType = \"planner.completed\" ✓.\n\nKeep customEventOf for context/confirm/run? Just use rawType everywhere except... event.type.startsWith(\"context.\") — with custom_type normalization, harness context events are direct types (context.* not normalized to tool.progress — only custom node events are). So rawType works for all. But careful: bare \"progress\" type → rawType \"progress\" → no match ✓.\n\nAlso `groupCategory`'s filter `progressKind(event) === \"progress\"` still v