":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user is showing a screenshot: a multi-round run. Round 1 (第1轮) succeeded: 开始执行 → 构建上下文 → 任务划分 → 提交动作 → 执行工具. Round 2 (第2轮) is running, showing 构建上下文 → node context_engine running. The user's complaint: \"这里进行了第二轮，有没有好的处理方案？因为到了第二轮聊天内容就没有再更新了，一直到全部任务完成\" — when round 2 starts, the chat bubble (聊天内容) stops updating until all tasks complete.\n\nSo the chat bubble's live progress (ChatRunTimeline in chat-run-progress.tsx) stops updating during round 2. Why?\n\nRecall from the summary: the chat bubble progress derives from the same SSE events via `deriveRunStages` matching question_route, analysis_plan, report_plan_result, rendered_report + `buildTasks`. The bubble shows:\n- timer (正在执行 · 160s)\n- stages (理解问题并召回上下文 ✓ / 划分分析任务 ✓ / 执行数据查询 ✓) — from deriveRunStages\n- thinking sections (生成 SQL 已思考 — collapsed)\n- task list (ProgressTaskList-like, at top per b75447f \"任务清单置顶\")\n\nWait the screenshot shows bubble: 正在执行 · 160s, three green checks (理解问题并召回上下文 / 划分分析任务 / 执行数据查询), and one collapsed section (生成 SQL 已思考). So in round 2, the bubble shows nothing new — the stage list is complete/green, no new activity items appear. The user says \"到了第二轮聊天内容就没有再更新了，一直到全部任务完成\" — i.e., during long task execution rounds (the analysis loop iterating tasks), the bubble sits static with the same three green milestones and no live feedback.\n\nHmm wait — but round 2 in the panel shows 构建上下文 running (context_engine). Interesting: 第2轮 = second iteration of loop_controller. The run structure: iteration 0 = route/context/plan? Actually in this run: round 1 did 开始执行 → 构建上下文 → 任务划分 → 提交动作 → 执行工具; round 2 starts 构建上下文 again?? That's odd — round 2 shows 构建上下文 with context_engine. Wait, actually looking at the panel: 第2轮 running, 构建上下文 step, node context_engine \"开始构建上下文\". Hmm, why would round 2 rebuild context?\n\nActually from the harness architecture: loop_controller iterations. Each iteration: _build_context (context events) → plan/act. So each round re-emits context events? From controller.py `_build_context` — yes, the controller builds context each iteration (with working memory accumulating). So every iteration emits a fresh context.* series + possibly planner.* etc.\n\nSo the UX problem: multi-round runs. The bubble stages (deriveRunStages) were designed for single-round runs: 理解问题 → 划分任务 → 执行数据查询 → 生成报告. In round 2, new context events arrive but the stage matchers don't produce new stages; task events continue per task. The bubble's three stages all show green (已完成) while work continues — no \"what's happening now\" feedback. And thinking sections: collapsed \"生成 SQL 已思考\" — round 2's new thinking (e.g., new SQL generation for another task?) — in this screenshot only one task apparently.\n\nWait — actually let me re-read: \"到了第二轮聊天内容就没有再更新了，一直到全部任务完成\" — chat content stops updating from round 2 until ALL tasks complete. The bubble shows the same content for potentially minutes. The user asks: 有没有好的处理方案?\n\nSo I need to propose a solution (方案 first — the user's standing directive: 方案 first before non-trivial implementation; and this message asks \"有没有好的处理方案\" — explicitly asking for a proposal).\n\nLet me think about why the bubble stops updating in round 2.\n\nBubble components (chat-run-progress.tsx):\n- ChatRunTimeline: timer → deriveRunStages (stages) → ThinkingSections → fallback\n- deriveRunStages: matches question_route / analysis_plan (×3) / report_plan_result / rendered_report via customEventOf. Stages: 理解问题并召回上下文, 划分分析任务, 执行数据查询, 汇总生成报告? and planFailureMessage.\n- ThinkingSections: reasoning/llm streams from compactAllEvents? It shows \"生成 SQL 已思考\" collapsed.\n- Task list at top (b75447f): ProgressTaskList-ish from buildTasks.\n\nWhy does round 2 add nothing?\n1. Stages: derived once per event-name match — e.g. 理解问题并召回上下文 stage keyed on question_route/context events; 划分分析任务 on analysis_plan; 执行数据查询 on task events (analysis_plan tasks count as detail); these all appear in round 1. In round 2, the same event names fire again (context.*, analysis_plan? no—plan only once per run probably; more tasks?). If round 2 executes additional tasks (analysis_task_* with new task_ids), the stage detail might update (task count) but status stays green \"已完成\"... hmm.\n\nWait, actually why is round 2 happening at all in this run? The run \"查询2017年每个月的销售额\" — 1 task presumably. Round 1: plan + execute tool (SQL). Round 2: maybe a follow-up action? Loop controller iterates when... after task execution, it may run additional iterations for report? Actually report stage events (report_plan_result/rendered_report) come at the end. Hmm, round 2 re-running 构建上下文 + context_engine suggests the controller's per-iteration context build. So round 2 might be the \"汇总/报告\" iteration or another action round.\n\nRegardless of semantics, the UX issue: during round 2+ the bubble is static. The root causes:\n\nA. **Stage model is single-pass**: deriveRunStages models the run as a fixed 4-stage narrative; rounds 2+ don't map to any new stage, so nothing new appears. The stages show green even though the run continues.\n\nB. **Thinking sections show per-node streams collapsed** — round 2's new thinking streams (context planning LLM? planner?) may produce new sections... but apparently not, or they're merged/deduped. In the screenshot, only \"生成 SQL 已思考\" from round 1. Round 2's context_engine thinking (LlmContextPlanner uses ainvoke_auto — non-streaming! No events). And loop controller's per-round context build — context events aren't LLM streaming events. So round 2 genuinely produces few stream events visible to the bubble until tasks execute.\n\nWait — but \"一直到全部任务完成\" implies long execution. If round 2 executes tasks (analysis_task_phase events with phases), the task list at top SHOULD update (task phases: task.phase). In the screenshot the bubble has no task list visible? b75447f added 任务清单置顶 — but the screenshot bubble shows stages at top... hmm, the screenshot bubble shows: 正在执行·160s / three