e) — deferred.\n- B3: context planner decision (context.plan event) already exists per iteration? _build_context emits context.plan each call — so round 2 should emit context.plan too → bubble could show \"上下文召回规划\" activity.\n\n**Frontend (render what's already flowing)**:\n- F1: live \"current activity\" line in bubble: derive latest meaningful event (context.*, planner.*, analysis_task_phase, tool.*, report) → \"正在：构建第 2 轮上下文 / 任务 1·生成 SQL / 等待确认\". Always updating → kills the static feeling.\n- F2: round awareness: when iteration > 0 events appear, show round marker in timeline (e.g. stage rows grouped or a \"第 2 轮\" sub-header).\n- F3: stages shouldn't go green-and-silent: 执行数据查询 stage should reflect running task phase (it does have task count detail?).\n\nRecommendation: F1 + B1 (both cheap) — F1 fixes \"no updates\" with existing events; B1 adds a semantic beat at the silent LLM gap (PlanningAgent decision + context rebuild) which no frontend derivation can fill because NO event flows there. Actually wait — is that true? Between round 1's tool completion and round 2's context.started, are there events? action.committed happens before tool execution. After tool.completed → PlanningAgent decides (silent) → _build_context (context.started fires). So the silent gap = PlanningAgent decision time. B1 (controller emits loop/iteration event after deciding) fills exactly that gap. Or emit BEFORE deciding? The decision itself is the silent part; emitting \"正在决策下一步\" before ainvoke would be the honest beat. Controller knows it's about to call PlanningAgent — emit progress there.\n\nLet me verify by reading controller.py around the iteration loop and PlanningAgent call, and chat-run-progress.tsx. Let me do that now.\n\nAlso the user asked \"有没有好的处理方案\" — deliver a 方案 (they'll approve before code, per standing directive; last time they said \"先给我方案\" for icons; this message asks for a proposal — so NO code changes yet, present the plan).\n\nLet me read the two files.","st