c first for my confirmation, then build\"\n\nGiven the pattern from before (方案 first, then 开工), and that they already said 可以开工, I think the right move is: present the concrete spec briefly AND proceed to implement it in the same turn — because they said 开工. But the spec has real decision points (e.g. how much markdown to support, whether reports stay inline). Hmm. The user's phrasing \"要定一下\" = \"let's pin it down\" — they're asking me to make the decisions concrete. I'll define the spec, then implement it, and present the spec at the top of my reply so they can see what was decided and adjust after seeing it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user has been decisive: \"可以开工\" = approved. \"但是具体展示什么，怎么展示要定一下\" = before writing code, define the concrete display contract. I'll write the spec in my response and implement it. If they dislike a detail, it's all in one component, easy to adjust.\n\nLet me define the spec concretely:\n\n## 展示内容与样式规范\n\n### AI 消息块（文档流，从上到下）\n1. **正文**：markdown 渲染，全宽，`text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700`\n2. **查询结果**（single_query 有 query_result 时）：保留 QueryResultView 卡片\n3. **摘要行**（弱化 trace 行）：`查看执行过程 · 用时 X ›` / `已暂停，等待你的确认 · X ›` / `执行失败 ›` —— 一行文字链接替代现在的 chip\n4. **报告**：ReportView 保留（结构化报告独立卡片，不属于 markdown 范畴）\n5. 时间戳：内容下方 10px slate-300\n\n### Markdown 元素映射（react-markdown components 定制）\n- h1/h2/h3: slate-900 粗体，字号收敛（h1 16px, h2 15px, h3 14px）——聊天流里不需要网页级大标题\n- p: text-sm leading-6\n- strong: slate-900 font-semibold\n- em: italic\n- code (inline): slate-100 bg, rounded, px-1.5, font-mono text-[0.85em] —— 截图的 chip\n- pre code block: slate-950 底 slate-100 字, rounded-lg p-3, overflow-x-auto, font-mono text-xs —— 复用 EventDetails pre 风格\n- ul/ol: 缩进 + marker slate-400\n- a: blue-600 underline\n- blockquote: border-l-2 slate-300 pl-3 slate-500\n- table: GFM 表格 → 带边框、表头 slate-50、单元格 px-2 py-1 text-xs；外层 overflow-x-auto\n- hr: slate-200\n- img: rounded, max-w-full\n- 删除线 del\n\n### 用户消息\n- 不变：右侧蓝气泡 max-w-[70%]\n\n### AI 消息布局\n- 去头像、去气泡；`w-full min-w-0`\n- 保留 ChatRunTimeline 占位（执行中）——不变\n- 流式光标保留\n\n### 摘要行（trace line）样式统一\n- 文字 11px slate-400, hover text-blue-600, chevron ›\n- 三态文案: 完成「查看执行过程 · 用时 X」/ 等确认「已暂停，等待你的确认 · X」/ 失败「执行失败 · X」\n- 保留点击切换 ExecutionPanel\n\nNow implementation steps:\n1. `npm install react-markdown remark-gfm`\n2. Create `markdown-content.tsx`\n3. Modify `AssistantMessageBubble`: AI branch → remove avatar + bubble; render MarkdownContent; unify summary chip → trace line (actually ChatRunSummaryChip already exists — restyle it into text-link style; it has waiting/failed/success tones. In the new spec, keep the semantic color hint? The screenshot trace line is muted. But failure should stay visible — rose text. Decision: keep tone colors but drop the border/box: text-only line with icon. That keeps 可控性. So restyle ChatRunSummaryChip from bordered capsule to inline text link with icon, keeping tone colors (amber/rose/slate+emerald icon).)\n4. ChatRunTimeline container tweak (it's fine as-is actually — it renders inside the message block; without bubble it just sits in the flow; the space-y-2.5 container is fine. Maybe minor: no change needed? The bubble previously added px-4 py-3; without it the timeline sits directly in flow — fine. I'll leave ChatRunTimeline unchanged this round unless something looks off. Actually one thing: it was designed to sit inside a white bubble; now on page background (white too — the chat area bg? Let me check the thread viewport bg: the chat area likely bg-slate-50 or white. From screenshot 1: chat area white, bubble bordered. Page bg white → timeline's slate-50 boxes fine.)\n5. tsc + commit.\n\nAlso the empty-state and composer untouched.\n\nWait — one more consideration: `whitespace-pre-wrap` on the old bubble — markdown renderer handles whitespace, remove it.\n\nAlso `displayText` streaming: markdown render during streaming — react-markdown re-parses every chunk; fine for message-length texts.\n\nChatRunSummaryChip is also used... only in AssistantMessageBubble (chat-session-view). Restyle in place (chat-run-progress.tsx).\n\nAlso `showStreamingCursor` — keep.\n\nLet me also double check where `QueryResultView` sits — :708 after timestamp. Keep order: 正文 → 时间戳 → QueryResultView → trace 行 → ReportView? Current order: timestamp, query_result, chip, report. Hmm, better: 正文 → trace 行 (摘要/入口) → QueryResultView → 报告? Actually query result is part of the answer content (single_query), trace line is meta. Spec: 正文 → QueryResultView（回答内容的一部分）→ trace 行（执行过程入口）→ ReportView。时间戳 stays right under 正文. Let me keep current DOM order mostly (timestamp, query_result, chip, report) to minimize diff — it's already reasonable. Actually current: timestamp → query_result → chip → report. Fine, keep.\n\nImplementation. Let me start. First install deps.\n\nThen markdown-content.tsx:\n\n```tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport ReactMarkdown from \"react-markdown\";\nimport remarkGfm from \"remark-gfm\";\n\n/** AI 回复的 markdown 渲染：AST 输出、不放行原始 HTML；样式对齐面板的 slate 体系。 */\nexport function MarkdownContent({ text }: { text: string }) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"min-w-0 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700 [&>*:first-child]:mt-0 [&>*:last-child]:mb-0\">\n      <ReactMarkdown\n        remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}\n        components={{\n          h1: (props) => <h1 className=\"mt-5 mb-2 text-base font-extrabold text-slate-900\" {...props} />,\n          h2: ...\n        }}\n      >\n        {text}\n      </ReactMarkdown>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nType of components props — react-markdown v10 components signature: `components={{ h1: ({node, ...props}) => ... }}`. With TS, using `({node, ...props})` requires care; simpler: `h1: (props) => <h1 className=\"...\" {...props} />` — props includes node? In react-markdown v10, component props include `node` prop — passing it to DOM element causes React warning \"unknown prop node\". Must strip node. Pattern: `h1: ({ node, ...props }) => <h1 {...props} className=\"...\" />`. TS types: Components type from react-markdown. `({ node: _, ...props })` — unused var lint? tsc noUnusedLocals may flag `_`? Destructured unused with underscore — noUnusedLocals flags unused destructured vars? TS ignores leading-underscore for parameters but destructured variables... noUnusedLocals doesn't flag destructuring rest siblings (`...props` omits node — TS has special rule: variables from destructuring with rest sibling are exempt). Yes — TS 4.6+ exempts destructured siblings of rest element from unused checks. Safe.\n\nCode block: react-markdown gives `code` component receiving `className` (language-xxx) and for block code it's wrapped in `pre`. Handle: `pre: ({node, children}) => <pre className=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-100 [&_code]:bg-transparent [&_code]:p-0 [&_code]:text-inherit\">{children}</pre>`, `code: ({node, className, children, ...props}) => inline vs block: in react-markdown v10+, inline code has no className and no newline; the standard check: `const isBlock = /language-/.test(className || \"\")` — not reliable for fenced without language. Alternative: style `code` inline, and override within pre via CSS selector (like above [&_code]). That's the clean trick: code component = inline chip style always; pre overrides descendants back. \n\n```tsx\ncode: ({ node, className, children, ...props }) => (\n  <code className={\"rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em] text-slate-800 \" + (className ?? \"\")} {...props}>{children}</code>\n),\npre: ({ node, children, ...props }) => (\n  <pre className=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-100 [&_code]:rounded-0 [&_code]:bg-transparent [&_code]:p-0 [&_code]:text-inherit\" {...props}>{children}</pre>\n),\n```\n`rounded-0` isn't a tailwind class — use `[&_code]:rounded-none`.\n\ntable: wrap in div overflow-x-auto? react-markdown renders `<table>` directly; component override for table: `<div className=\"overflow-x-auto\"><table .../></div>` — 