ownContent text={displayText} /></div>\n  )}\n  ...\n```\n\nHmm — but cursor also for assistant non-placeholder streaming (text streaming with cursor). Keep cursor inside markdown? Appending cursor span after markdown block: `<MarkdownContent text={displayText} />{showStreamingCursor && <span .../>}` — cursor on its own line then. Better: inline cursor at end of text — with markdown block that's awkward; place cursor as inline-block right after content — will appear below last paragraph. Alternative: pass cursor into MarkdownContent? Append `▍` character to text during streaming? Claude Code style: append \"▍\" char. Simplest robust: when streaming, append `▍` to the markdown text itself: `<MarkdownContent text={displayText + (showStreamingCursor ? \" ▍\" : \"\")} />`. The ▍ renders inline in the last paragraph. \n\nTimestamp span: keep for both, align: user keeps px-1; AI keep.\n\nAvatar: remove for AI. For user: keep user avatar? The screenshot style has no avatars at all; user side stays bubble — keep user avatar for symmetry? 用户说\"ai回复不使用气泡框\" — only AI changes. Keep user avatar + bubble untouched. AI avatar removed.\n\nTrace line: restyle ChatRunSummaryChip in chat-run-progress.tsx: from bordered capsule to text line:\n\nCurrent: `<button className=\"mt-2 inline-flex ... rounded-md border px-2.5 py-1.5 text-[11px] font-semibold ${tone}\">` with tones amber/rose/slate borders.\n\nNew: text-only: `mt-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center gap-1 text-[11px] font-semibold ${textTone}` where textTone: waiting \"text-amber-600\", failed \"text-rose-600\", else \"text-slate-400 hover:text-blue-600\". Keep icons (size-3.5) and chevron. Remove border/bg/padding, adjust mt. The elapsed stays.\n\nAlso the fallback execution button (:717-727) — the bordered button \"查看执行过程\". Should also degrade to same trace-line style for consistency: change to text link style matching. Yes — unify.\n\nReportView wrapper `mt-6 w-full` — keep.\n\nQueryResultView — keep.\n\nOne more: the AI