n\nWhat was the previously working set? We don't have the old lockfile, but package.json said:\n- @assistant-ui/react ^0.14.16 → installed was probably exactly 0.14.16 (if installed when 0.14.16 was latest) — can't be sure, but pinning to 0.14.16 is a reasonable \"known\" floor. However — maybe it was working at some 0.14.2x too. The safest empirical approach: downgrade @assistant-ui/react to 0.14.16 (and its core/store companions), keep everything else, test. If still broken, downgrade react 19.3.0 → 19.2.6.\n\nWait — but before doing shotgun downgrades, let me look at the actual code to find the uncached getSnapshot. Where? node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist — grep for getSnapshot / useSyncExternalStore.\n\nActually, let me think about what in 0.14.29 could loop. Known issue: assistant-ui \"useAuiState\" + zustand v5 — zustand 5 removed the default `useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector` shim? No — zustand v5 uses React.useSyncExternalStore directly with getSnapshot=api.getState (stable reference) and applies selector via useRef comparison... zustand v5 selectors returning new objects cause \"getSnapshot should be cached\" — THIS IS THE KNOWN ZUSTAND V5 ISSUE: in v5, if your selector returns a new object each render, React throws exactly this error (\"The result of getSnapshot should be cached\"). zustand 5.0.14 → 5.0.15 shouldn't change that.\n\nBut our useAuiState selectors return primitives... unless the crash is inside assistant-ui's own components (ThreadPrimitive.Viewport etc.) using a selector that returns fresh object — version 0.14.29 regression.\n\nSecond screenshot showed even the EMPTY thread (before sending) rendering as primitives with nothing — user said \"输入内容后什么也不展示\" — after entering input, nothing displays, jumps to history. So the loop triggers on send → messages array changes → some selector recomputes → loop. On empty thread it renders (screenshot 2 shows empty viewport). So the loop is tied to message rendering — MessagePrimitive/useMessage path — i.e., AssistantMessageBubble with our MarkdownContent? Hmm!\n\nWait — could OUR MarkdownContent cause \"Maximum update depth exceeded\"? That error means setState loops during render — react-markdown doesn't setState. But \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" could also come from a parent loop re-rendering infinitely: e.g., a context Provider whose value changes every render + a consumer that triggers parent state update during render... \n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider: `useExternalStoreRuntime({messages, isRunning, onNew, ...})` — the runtime store: messages prop — the parent of AssistantChatRuntime holds messages state. If getSnapshot of THIS external store returns a fresh array per call → useSyncExternalStore loop! convertMessage: (message) => message as ThreadMessage — fine.\n\nHow does the external store runtime subscribe? useExternalStoreRuntime builds a store from the props: getSnapshot = () => messages (the prop array). If the parent re-creates the messages array every render (e.g., messages = [...something] inline), then getSnapshot returns new reference each call → React throws \"getSnapshot should be cached\" + infinite loop EXACTLY when messages exist/empty transition... But this worked before! The parent's messages building didn't change in our commit... unless — wait, did WE touch anything that changes when messages render? MarkdownContent renders during streaming — but loop trigger on SEND with messages...\n\nHmm hold on, let me look at what invokes navigation \"跳转到历史记录\" — onNew probably does router.push to /sessions/{new id}. Then SessionPage renders ChatSessionView. The loop then crashes the page. Before our change this flow worked.\n\nOK stop guessing — inspect the installed package code. Grep @assistant-ui/react dist for \"getSnapshot\" and look at useExternalStoreRuntime implementation. Also check git: is there a chance the PREVIOUS node_modules had assistant-ui 0.14.16 and the bug was introduced in 0.14.17-0.14.29? Check assistant-ui changelog? Can't easily.\n\nEmpirical plan (fast, decisive):\n1. Inspect dist code of @assistant-ui/react 0.14.29 for getSnapshot usage in useExternalStoreRuntime / useAuiState — 5 min.\n2. Downgrade @assistant-ui/react to 0.14.16 (npm install @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16 --save-exact) — the most likely restoration since ^0.14.16 previously resolved to a specific version that worked. Also pin companions automatically via its deps (^0.2.12 core → will float to 0.2.23 again... need exact pins for core/store too if they're the culprit).\n3. Have user refresh & test.\n\nActually wait — I can't test the browser myself; user must verify. To minimize round-trips, do the code inspection first to identify the exact culprit, then pin precisely.\n\nLet me grep the dist.","startTime":1791428023750,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023750},{"id":"d1737a18-dbd4-406d-9ee9-a9b41627ec05","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"错误证实是客户端无限重渲染循环。版本漂移明确：`@assistant-ui/react 0.14.16 → 0.14.29`、`react 19.2.6 → 19.3.0`、`next 16.2.6 → 16.3.5`。现在看装上的 0.14.29 源码，找出哪个 `getSnapshot` 不稳定："},{"id":"call_f111e295d7bb44f3a1ecefec","type":"TOOL","toolName":"grep_content","params":{"-n":"true","head_limit":"20","output_mode":"content","path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist","pattern":"useSyncExternalStore\\("},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":{"$blob":"sha256:b7067140cb69b0a787cc743332fd138a292a04a623095bd9263099f8cf9dfdaa","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":7735,"compression":"none"},"metadata":{"pattern":"useSyncExternalStore\\(","relevantFiles":[{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/primitives/composer/trigger/TriggerPopoverRootContext.js","startLine":32,"endLine":32},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/primitives/composer/trigger/TriggerPopoverRootContext.js","startLine":40,"endLine":40},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/primitives/composer/trigger/TriggerPopoverRootContext.js","startLine":50,"endLine":50},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/primitives/composer/trigger/TriggerPopoverRootContext.js.map","startLine":1,"endLine":1},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/utils/hooks/useMediaQuery.js","startLine":30,"endLine":30},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/utils/hooks/useMediaQuery.js.map","startLine":1,"endLine":1},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.js.map","startLine":1,"endLine":1},{"path":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.js","startLine":22,"endLine":22}]}}}]},{"id":"6aacec19d0d0586a4a60bc78","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":61809},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"70c5a85f-c97b-43c9-827f-49346d1f1ef9","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Found it! `useRuntimeStateInternal` in the installed @assistant-ui/react 0.14.29:\n\n```ts\nconst slice = useSyncExternalStore(\n  runtime.subscribe,\n  () => selector(runtime.getState()),\n  () => selector(runtime.getState()),\n);\n```\n\nThe getSnapshot passed to useSyncExternalStore is `() => selector(runtime.getState())` — React calls getSnapshot and requires a CACHED result (Object.is stable between calls). If the selector returns a fresh object/array each call → React throws exactly \"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop\". This pattern is inherently unsafe for object-returning selectors — a known assistant-ui issue pattern.\n\nBUT — is this NEW in 0.14.29, or was it in 0.14.16? The compiled code has `t1`/`t2` (react compiler output). The previous working version 0.14.16 probably had `useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector` (which caches selector results) and newer versions switched to this naive pattern — OR they had it all along and the selectors used were primitives.\n\nNow, who returns a fresh object in OUR tree? Our `useAuiState` selectors return primitives (isRunning: bool, messages.at(-1)?.id: string). `useMessage()` — need to check what it uses. But also `ThreadPrimitive.Viewport`, `MessagePrimitive.Root`, `ComposerPrimitive` internals — if ANY of them calls useRuntimeState with an object-returning selector (like `.slice()` — look at sourcesContent: there's `slice`... `t2.slice` hmm) → loop.\n\nRather than auditing the whole package, the decisive fix: **pin back to the version that worked**. The previous working install: we know package.json constraint ^0.14.16 and it worked. What exact version was installed before the rebuild? Unknown, but the bug appeared after float to 0.14.29. Downgrade to 0.14.16 exactly (+ its matching core/store).\n\nCheck dependency relationships: @assistant-ui/react 0.14.16 requires @assistant-ui/core ^0.2.12, @assistant-ui/store ^0.2.14, @assistant-ui/tap ^0.6.1. If I pin react to 0.14.16 but core floats to 0.2.23, the buggy code might live in core or react. The useRuntimeState code is in react package. Let me pin all three exactly: @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16, @assistant-ui/core@0.2.12, @assistant-ui/store@0.2.14, @assistant-ui/tap@0.6.1.\n\nWait — but before pinning, double-check the hypothesis differently: does 0.14.16's dist have the same useRuntimeState code? I can check by downloading/inspecting... `npm view @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16` won't show code. Could `npm pack @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16` and inspect the tarball — cheap and decisive! Let me do that: pack 0.14.16, extract dist/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.js, compare.\n\nActually — even better idea: check if the bug is triggered by OUR selectors or by internal ones. The React error fires when getSnapshot result differs between two calls. For our primitive selectors — stable. So the offending selector is inside assistant-ui internals (e.g., `state.thread.messages.slice(...)` or object construction). If those internal call sites exist in 0.14.29 regardless of our code, then ANY user of 0.14.29 would crash — unlikely such a glaring bug ships... unless the crash needs a specific code path (messages present + our MessagePrimitive usage...). Hmm.\n\nAlternatively the trigger could be in @assistant-ui/store 0.2.22 (useAuiState implementation). Let me grep the store package for useSyncExternalStore too.\n\nAnd — one more important check: React 19.3.0! React tightened the getSnapshot caching check: React 19.x added \"getSnapshot should be cached\" warning→error? In React 19.2 the useSyncExternalStore uncached getSnapshot produced a console WARNING (\"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop\") in dev; React 19.3 may have escalated to THROW (\"Maximum update depth exceeded\" + uncaught). If assistant-ui 0.14.29's uncached-getSnapshot pattern coexisted with react 19.2.6 as a warning... but user says BEFORE our rebuild it worked fine (no warnings?). Maybe warnings existed but benign; now react 19.3.0 + \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" = crash. Actually \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" is the real killer — a genuine re-render loop (setState during render repeatedly), not just the snapshot warning.\n\nHmm — \"Maximum update depth exceeded. The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop.\" — combined into one message? The user pasted them as one string. In React source, when useSyncExternalStore detects unstable getSnapshot during render it logs the warning; the \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" is thrown when a render-loop is detected (nested updates > 50). The two together = selector returns fresh object → forceUpdate loop → depth exceeded → crash.\n\nDecision: downgrade the assistant-ui trio + keep react? Or also downgrade react 19.3.0 → 19.2.6? React 19.3 is very new (today is 2026-09). assistant-ui 0.14.29 peer allows ^18||^19 so it \"supports\" 19.3 nominally.\n\nMost conservative restoration = pin EVERYTHING that floated to the versions that were installed before. But we don't know exact previous versions except from package.json floors... The floors: @assistant-ui/react ^0.14.16 — when was this package.json last edited? The dependency was added when 0.14.16 might have been latest. zustand ^5.0.14 → previous likely 5.0.14. react ^19.2.6 → previous likely 19.2.6. next ^16.2.6 → previous could be 16.2.x (now 16.3.5 — screenshot confirms 16.3.5).\n\nPlan:\n1. `npm pack @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16` → inspect useRuntimeState.js — if it uses useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector (cached) → confirms regression → pin exact trio.\n2. Pin: `npm install --save-exact @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16 @assistant-ui/core@0.2.12 @assistant-ui/store@0.2.14 @assistant-ui/tap@0.6.1` — wait, tap version? Current installed tap? Check. And also consider react 19.2.6 pin: if crash persists after assistant-ui pin, downgrade react/next next.\n\nLet me check installed tap version + run the pack inspection.","startTime":1791428023750,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023750},{"id":"8465000f-03df-4e5f-995f-3e59ae5eaaf7","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"找到嫌疑点了：装上的 0.14.29 里 `useRuntimeStateInternal` 把 `() => selector(runtime.getState())` **直接**传给 `useSyncExternalStore` 当 `getSnapshot`——这个写法只要 selector 返回新对象就会触发 React 的这个错误。现在验证这是不是 0.14.29 的新回归——拉旧版 0.14.16 的包对比同一处代码："},{"id":"call_5ab16a14944d405e80bba228","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /tmp && rm -rf aui-check && mkdir aui-check && cd aui-check && npm pack @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16 --silent >/dev/null 2>&1 && tar -xzf assistant-ui-react-0.14.16.tgz package/dist/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.js 2>/dev/null; cat package/dist/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.js 2>/dev/null | head -40; printf \"---- tap version now: \"; node -p \"require('/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis/frontend/node_modules/@assistant-ui/tap/package.json').version\"","description":"Download assistant-ui 0.14.16 and inspect useRuntimeState implementation"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nimport { ensureBinding } from \"./ensureBinding.js\";\nimport { useDebugValue, useSyncExternalStore } from \"@assistant-ui/tap/react-shim\";\n//#region src/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.ts\nfunction useRuntimeStateInternal(runtime, selector = identity) {\n\tensureBinding(runtime);\n\tconst slice = useSyncExternalStore(runtime.subscribe, () => selector(runtime.getState()), () => selector(runtime.getState()));\n\tuseDebugValue(slice);\n\treturn slice;\n}\nconst identity = (arg) => arg;\nfunction useRuntimeState(runtime, selector) {\n\treturn useRuntimeStateInternal(runtime, selector);\n}\n//#endregion\nexport { useRuntimeState, useRuntimeStateInternal };\n\n//# sourceMappingURL=useRuntimeState.js.map---- tap version now: 0.9.17\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/z523/Desktop/zizhi/ai_Python/ai_data_analysis","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"plbgip","output":"import { ensureBinding } from \"./ensureBinding.js\";\nimport { useDebugValue, useSyncExternalStore } from \"@assistant-ui/tap/react-shim\";\n//#region src/context/react/utils/useRuntimeState.ts\nfunction useRuntimeStateInternal(runtime, selector = identity) {\n\tensureBinding(runtime);\n\tconst slice = useSyncExternalStore(runtime.subscribe, () => selector(runtime.getState()), () => selector(runtime.getState()));\n\tuseDebugValue(slice);\n\treturn slice;\n}\nconst identity = (arg) => arg;\nfunction useRuntimeState(runtime, selector) {\n\treturn useRuntimeStateInternal(runtime, selector);\n}\n//#endregion\nexport { useRuntimeState, useRuntimeStateInternal };\n\n//# sourceMappingURL=useRuntimeState.js.map---- tap version now: 0.9.17\n","exitCode":0,"inBackground":false}}}]},{"id":"6aacec58b08fa821c7089847","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":64257},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"a97bebed-0e3a-42a3-8027-55f546aa696c","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Interesting — 0.14.16 has the SAME uncached getSnapshot pattern (`() => selector(runtime.getState())`). So that pattern isn't the regression itself. BUT — note a difference: 0.14.16 imports `useSyncExternalStore` from `@assistant-ui/tap/react-shim`, while 0.14.29 imports from \"react\" directly (the installed 0.14.29 file showed `import { useDebugValue, useSyncExternalStore } from \"react\"`). \n\n**`@assistant-ui/tap/react-shim`!** In 0.14.16, useSyncExternalStore comes from @assistant-ui/tap's react-shim — which might be a CACHED/WRAPPED version (tap is their \"react compiler-ish\" runtime; the shim may implement caching of getSnapshot results). And tap version floated: installed now is 0.9.17; 0.14.16's package.json requires `@assistant-ui/tap: ^0.6.1` — previously installed was probably 0.6.x. In 0.6.x, react-shim may have had a caching useSyncExternalStore wrapper; in 0.9.x the shim may have changed/been removed (0.14.29 no longer uses the shim in this file — imports react directly).\n\nHmm wait, but 0.14.16 worked with which tap? ^0.6.1 at the time → 0.6.x. Now react 0.14.29 uses tap ^0.9.x. \n\nAlso — react-shim in tap 0.6.x: let me check what tap's react-shim exports. Actually the decisive comparison: does current tap 0.9.17's react-shim exist and cache? The 0.14.29 file doesn't use the shim anyway (direct react import). \n\nSo hypothesis refinement: 0.14.16 + tap 0.6.x worked because... the same uncached pattern with primitive selectors returns primitives → fine either way. The LOOP must come from an object-returning selector somewhere. Where? Either:\n1. assistant-ui internal call sites that build objects per call (new in 0.14.17+ or triggered by our message flow), or\n2. OUR tree: `useExternalStoreRuntime` → its store getState... `convertMessage: (message) => message as ThreadMessage`? The runtime's internal selectors? e.g. ThreadPrimitive.Viewport's `useRuntimeState(runtime, (s) => ...)` — need to find object-returning selectors in 0.14.29 internals.\n\nActually — hold on. Let me reconsider. \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" is thrown when too many synchronously nested updates. Combined with the getSnapshot message: React's useSyncExternalStore, upon detecting getSnapshot instability, forces re-render → if getSnapshot stays unstable → infinite re-render → depth exceeded. For the depth to exceed, the getSnapshot must return a fresh value EVERY call. A selector like `state.thread.messages.at(-1)?.id` → primitive string → stable. So an object/array-returning selector IS running. Which call sites? Let me grep the installed dist for useRuntimeState/useAuiState callers that construct objects: patterns like `({ ... })` or `.filter(` `.map(` `.slice(` inside selectors.\n\nThat's a big grep... Alternative faster path: check @assistant-ui/store (useAuiState) implementation in installed 0.2.22 vs old 0.2.14. useAuiState is what OUR code calls and what Thread primitives call. If store 0.2.22 changed useAuiState to use runtime state naively...\n\nLet me grep @assistant-ui/store dist for useSyncExternalStore/getSnapshot.\n\nAlso — react 19.3.0: React changed behavior? In React 19.3, `useSyncExternalStore` getSnapshot instability escalation... Actually there IS a known React change: React 19.1/19.2 warned \"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop\" as console.error in dev. The throw of \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" accompanies it when the loop actually happens. With react 19.2.6 it maybe also looped? No — it worked before. \n\nHmm wait — actually, did it? The user said the bug appeared now (\"有bug输入内容后\"). Previous sessions worked (screenshots with content). So combination changed. Since 0.14.16 == 0.14.29 in this file's pattern, the delta must be elsewhere: tap 0.6→0.9 (shim), store 0.2.14→0.2.22, core 0.2.12→0.2.23, react 19.2.6→19.3.0, next 16.2.6→16.3.5, zustand 5.0.14→5.0.15.\n\nzustand 5.0.15: check zustand changelog — 5.0.15... zustand v5 useStore: `useSyncExternalStore(api.subscribe, () => selector(api.getState()), ...)`? NO — zustand v5: `const slice = React.useSyncExternalStore(api.subscribe, () => selector(api.getState()), () => selector(api.getState()))` — WAIT. Actually zustand v5's useStore does exactly this naive pattern too! From zustand source: \n\n```ts\nconst slice = React.useSyncExternalStore(\n  api.subscribe,\n  () => selector(api.getState()),\n  () => selector(api.getState()),\n)\n```\n\nYes! zustand v5 removed useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector and docs say \"selectors must return stable references\" — returning new objects throws this exact React error. So any zustand v5 usage with object-returning selector crashes. zustand 5.0.14 vs 5.0.15 — patch bump, no behavior change. Where's zustand used? @assistant-ui/react deps include zustand ^5.0.14 (saw in its package.json: \"zustand\": \"^5.0.14\"). assistant-ui internally uses zustand for... some stores.\n\nOK — I'm going too deep. Decisive empirical isolation: **restore the exact previous working versions**. Previous working versions aren't recorded... but package.json floors tell us the MINIMUM. The previous install was made whenever node_modules was last created — could be months ago → versions = latest at that time, likely well below current. To restore \"a state consistent with the floors\", pin:\n- @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16 (exact)\n- @assistant-ui/core@0.2.12\n- @assistant-ui/store@0.2.14\n- @assistant-ui/tap@0.6.1\n- react@19.2.6, react-dom@19.2.6 (exact)\n- next@16.2.6? — next 16.3.5 also floated; but pinning next affects the whole build... The browser error is React-level; react 19.3.0 is a bigger suspect (new major React behavior). Hmm.\n\nActually — WAIT. Let me reconsider whether react 19.3.0 is the real culprit. Known React issue: React 19.3 (canary/latest) tightened useSyncExternalStore: when getSnapshot is uncached AND the store updates, it now throws \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" instead of warning? If assistant-ui's internal selectors return objects sometimes (e.g. during streaming messages), react 19.2.6 might have tolerated with warning (or the code path avoided), 19.3.0 crashes.\n\nThere's a cleaner check: React 19.3.0 changelog mentions? I can't browse reliably... Actually I CAN use RealtimeSearch! Let me search for this exact error + react 19.3 / assistant-ui 0.14.29.\n\nBetter: search \"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop\" react 19.3 — see if it's a known regression. And \"assistant-ui Maximum update depth exceeded 0.14\".\n\nLet me do a quick web search to avoid blind version ping-pong.","startTime":1791428023750,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023750},{"id":"16433120-cd04-4222-b29e-43729143fe45","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"0.14.16 里居然是**同样的写法**——所以这处不是回归点。但有个关键差异：0.14.16 从 `@assistant-ui/tap/react-shim` 导入 `useSyncExternalStore`（可能是带缓存的 shim 实现），0.14.29 改成了直接从 react 导入；而且 react 也从 19.2.6 漂到了 19.3.0。先查一下这是不是已知问题，避免盲试版本："},{"id":"call_b2f8a2eaa9ce4737b73fd3c8","type":"TOOL","toolName":"web_search","params":{"max_results":"6","query":"React 19.3 \"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop\" Maximum update depth exceeded useSyncExternalStore regression"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":{"$blob":"sha256:dd3fd9a028914e6545c70e87b1f053b836bc8426af5f5733458a643b038f3258","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":5514,"compression":"none"},"metadata":{"sites":[{"content":"`getServerSnapshot`\n`getServerSnapshot`\n`<script>`\n`window.MY_STORE_DATA`\n`getServerSnapshot`\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### I’m getting an error: “The result of `getSnapshot` should be cached”\n\n`getSnapshot`\n\nThis error means your `getSnapshot` function returns a new object every time it’s called, for example:\n\n`getSnapshot`\n`function getSnapshot() {\n\n// 🔴 Do not return always different objects from getSnapshot\n\nreturn {\n\ntodos: myStore.todos\n\n};\n\n}`\n\nReact will re-render the component if `getSnapsh...","title":"useSyncExternalStore - React","url":"https://react.dev/reference/react/useSyncExternalStore","favicon":null,"source":null},{"content":"React limits the number of nested updates to prevent infinite loops.] Here's what works for me instead. const gotoNextStepFn = useOnboarding","title":"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop","url":"https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand/discussions/1936","favicon":null,"source":null},{"content":"... getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop Error: Maximum update depth exceeded. This can happen when a component repeatedly","title":"I am stuck in this wierd Zustand bug which is causing infinite rendering","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/reactjs/comments/1jz5m7i/i_am_stuck_in_this_wierd_zustand_bug_which_is","favicon":null,"source":null},{"content":"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop. This can happen when a component repeatedly calls setState","title":"Bug: Breaking change of use-subscription from 1.6.0 to 1.7 ... - GitHub","url":"https://github.com/react/react/issues/24508","favicon":null,"source":null},{"content":"Sign up\n\nSign in\n\nSign up\n\nSign in\n\nUnknown user\nWisdom Peters\n\n## Wisdom Peters\n\n# useSyncExternalStore\n\nWisdom Peters\n\n--\n\nListen\n\nShare\n\nuseSyncExternalStore is a React Hook that lets you subscribe to an external store.\n\nconst snapshot = useSyncExternalStore(subscribe, getSnapshot, getServerSnapshot?)\n\n~Reference\n\n. useSyncExternalStore(subscribe, getSnapshot, getServerSnapshot?)\n\n~Usage\n\n. Subscribing to an external store\n\n. Subscribing to a browser API\n\n. Extracting the logic to a custom Ho...","title":"Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@peterswisdom603/usesyncexternalstore-548961fb250f","favicon":null,"source":null}]}}}]},{"id":"6aacec99b58a630c138e69ed","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":39770},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"f0f872b0-200a-4935-8f15-575e9bedbde9","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Search confirms the general mechanism (uncached getSnapshot → infinite loop), and the zustand discussion confirms it's the classic zustand v5 selector issue. But it doesn't tell me whether React 19.3 vs assistant-ui is at fault. \n\nKey insight so far: the uncached pattern existed in 0.14.16 too (with tap shim) — and it WORKED before the rebuild. The delta set: assistant-ui suite (0.14.29/core 0.2.23/store 0.2.22/tap 0.9.17), react 19.3.0, next 16.3.5, zustand 5.0.15.\n\nDecision framework: restore the entire chain to the floors that package.json declared — the state the app was developed and verified against. The floors are the minimums, but since the app worked with SOME previous resolution, and we can't know exact previous versions, the safest bet is to pin the assistant-ui suite + react to exact floor versions (^0.14.16 → 0.14.16, react 19.2.6, etc.) and test. If the bug persists, next suspect next@16.3.5.\n\nBut wait — one more consideration: maybe the previous install had a NEWER-than-floor assistant-ui that worked (e.g. 0.14.20), and 0.14.16 itself has issues with react 19.3? To minimize variables: pin assistant-ui suite exact floors AND react/react-dom 19.2.6. Keep next as-is (16.3.5) initially — next version doesn't usually cause useSyncExternalStore loops; but Turbopack... Next dev overlay showed the error; the error is client React. React 19.3.0 released recently; assistant-ui 0.14.29 may not be compatible with React 19.3's stricter behavior. \n\nActually — hmm, let me think about whether react 19.3.0 changed behavior here. I recall React 19.2 introduced the dev warning \"The result of getSnapshot should be cached to avoid an infinite loop\" as a console error. In 19.3, did they escalate to throwing? If the pattern returned objects only occasionally... \n\nRather than agonizing: the empirical, low-risk move is to downgrade BOTH assistant-ui suite AND react/react-dom to floor versions, test in browser. One shot. If fixed → re-introduce exactness via save-exact + lockfile (now exists).\n\nnpm install command:\n```\nnpm install --save-exact @assistant-ui/react@0.14.16 @assistant-ui/core@0.2.12 @assistant-ui/store@0.2.14 @assistant-ui/tap@0.6.1 react@19.2.6 react-dom@19.2.6\n```\nWait — check 0.14.16's exact core/store/tap requirements first: from the tarball I downloaded, package/package.json exists. Let me read it to get exact ranges. Also does react 19.2.6 exist in npm registry — yes.\n\nAlso zustand: 5.0.15 installed; 0.14.16 requires ^5.0.14 — 5.0.15 is patch, keep.\n\nnext: keep 16.3.5 for now.\n\nAlso — @radix-ui and other deps floated too, but they're UI-level, unlikely related.\n\nActually, hold on: before downgrading react (big surface), reconsider: is it more likely assistant-ui 0.14.29 has an object-returning selector regression? The tarball comparison showed the SAME naive pattern in useRuntimeState for both versions — so within THIS file no regression. The loop needs an object-returning selector: ours are primitive. So the object-returning selector is inside assistant-ui internals (Thread/Message/Composer primitives call useRuntimeState with selectors — some return objects). If those internal selectors are unchanged between versions, the crash would have existed with react 19.2.6 too... UNLESS react 19.2.6 didn't throw for this and 19.3.0 does. That flips suspicion to REACT 19.3.0 as the escalation trigger.\n\nCheck: in React 19.2.x, useSyncExternalStore with unstable getSnapshot → dev warning only (\"The result of getSnapshot should be cached...\"), no throw, no loop... but the user's log shows \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" — thrown. Hmm, the warning itself says \"to avoid an infinite loop\" — the loop happens when getSnapshot instability ALSO triggers state updates. React's implementation: if getSnapshot changes between render and commit → force re-render → if still unstable → loop → depth exceeded → this existed in 19.2 too.\n\nSo why did it work before?? Something must have actually changed in behavior — either assistant-ui's selectors now return objects where they didn't (0.14.29 internals), or the shim in tap 0.6.x cached getSnapshot (memoized the selector result) and 0.9.x/tap-removal stopped caching. THE SHIM! 0.14.16: `import { useSyncExternalStore } from \"@assistant-ui/tap/react-shim\"` — tap's shim might wrap React's with caching (they wrote a custom shim for react-compiler compat). 0.14.29: direct react import — no caching. That's a REAL behavioral difference in the exact code path, consistent with \"same selector, old worked, new crashes\".\n\nSo culprit ranking: 1) assistant-ui suite float (tap shim removal), 2) react 19.3.0. Fix: pin assistant-ui suite to floors (0.14.16/core 0.2.12/store 0.2.14/tap 0.6.1), keep react 19.3.0. If still broken → pin react 19.2.6.\n\nLet me check tap 0.6.x's react-shim to confirm caching — npm pack @assistant-ui/tap@0.6.1 and look at react-shim. Quick.\n\nAlso get exact dep ranges from 0.14.16 package.json to pin companions correctly.","startTime":1791428023750,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023750},{"id":"41875a77-e6c4-4507-9d65-327dce1debaa","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"React 官方文档证实机制（getSnapshot 每次返回新对象 → 无限循环）。关键差异在 tap 的 shim——查 0.14.16 依赖的 `@assistant-ui/tap@0.6.x` 的 `react-shim` 是不是带缓存实现："},{"id":"call_ae9f741089fe49db8d15f53a","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /tmp/aui-check && cat package/package.json | node -e \"const p=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync(0,'utf8'));console.log(JSON.stringify({deps:p.dependencies},null,1))\" && npm pack @assistant-ui/tap@0.6.1 --silent >/dev/null 2>&1 && mkdir -p tap6 && tar -xzf assistant-ui-tap-0.6.1.tgz -C tap6 package 2>/dev/null; ls tap6/package/dist/ 2>/dev/null | head; find tap6 -name \"*react-shim*\" | he