se},"id":"a4c05969-2025-4fe7-8f15-72630bbefbdc"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789985445479},{"id":"fe0e7180-44cc-4d2d-b6e6-17781d723f8a","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"a4c05969-2025-4fe7-8f15-72630bbefbdc","reportedId":"5abb21ae-6d2c-40ba-84e5-7381f4ccd825","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":50.41,"contextUsed":129046,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":855,"totalDuration":46472},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab102a6b08fa821c70dbc96","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":45618},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"5832b7b0-7be1-4e8f-9278-0875888b1ec4","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"我理解 self.event_writer.emit(EventType.RUN_STARTED, phase=LoopPhaseStatusType.START_RUN, iteration=0) 这里执行完毕后，前端就会接收这个信息对吗，与langGraph的写入差不多一个意思\"\n\nTranslation: \"I understand that after this emit executes, the frontend will receive this message, right? Similar meaning to LangGraph's write/stream_writer?\"\n\nFrom the session history (summary), the user earlier said: \"就想原有的langGraph的 writer = runtime.stream_writer 一样,我不想知道这么多,我也不考虑他的机制,我只想知道怎么用\" — they wanted a simple usage model.\n\nNow they're confirming their mental model: emit → frontend receives. Is that accurate? Mostly yes, but with precision needed (user's terminology discipline memory — be precise, don't blur terms):\n\nThe accurate picture:\n1. `self.event_writer.emit(...)` — writer stamps the event (run_ref/event_id/timestamp), sanitizes payload, then calls `sink.publish(event)`.\n2. In the STREAM endpoints (`/run/stream`, `/run/resume/stream`), the sink is `QueueEventSink` — it does two things: (a) appends to `self.events` (for execution trace persistence), (b) `queue.put_nowait(event)` into an asyncio.Queue.\n3. The API layer's `_sse_response` runs a background task (`run_operation`) executing the controller; a separate async generator `body()` consumes from the queue, formats each event via `format_sse` into an SSE frame (`id:`/`event:`/`data:` lines), and yields it through the StreamingResponse → HTTP chunked stream → browser EventSource/fetch reader.\n4. So \"执行完毕后前端就会接收\" is approximately right, but the precise semantics: emit 只是把事件塞进内存队列(非阻塞、立即返回),真正的\"推给前端\"由 API 层的 SSE 消费循环完成。前端收到的时间 = emit 之后几乎立即(毫秒级),因为生产者和消费者在同一事件循环。The frontend receives it as an SSE frame — the browser gets the HTTP chunk as soon as it's yielded.\n5. Important distinction vs non-stream endpoints: in `/run` and `/run/resume` (non-stream), the writer is NullHarnessEventWriter — events are constructed then dropped, frontend receives nothing (response is a single JSON at the end).\n6. Comparison with LangGraph's stream_writer: conceptually similar (progress events written from inside graph nodes/tools get streamed out), but mechanically different:\n   - LangGraph `stream_writer` (get_stream_writer / runtime.stream_writer) writes custom-mode stream items that surface through `graph.astream(stream_mode=[\"custom\", ...])` — the consumer is whoever iterates the graph stream. In this repo, QueryDataTool bridges LangGraph custom events into the Harness event system: it iterates `query_graph.astream` and forwards custom events via `writer.custom(payload)` (which normalizes to EventType.TOOL_PROGRESS).\n   - Harness emit: producer-consumer with an explicit queue + SSE formatting done by the API layer. emit is fire-and-forget (returns event or None, never raises).\n   - So: \"差不多一个意思\" — same purpose (progress broadcasting to frontend), but two layers here: LangGraph's writer is the INNER graph-level channel (query_data 内部节点进度), and HarnessEventWriter is the OUTER unified channel. The tool bridges one into the other.\n\nWhere does the frontend actually receive? The SSE connection: `/api/harness/run/stream` returns `text/event-stream`. Frontend code (chat-session-view.tsx / execution-panel.tsx per commit 86c4c04) reads the event stream.\n\nAlso precise point: \"执行完毕后\" — after THIS emit line executes, the event is in the queue; the frontend receives it within milliseconds (not exactly \"after execution completes\" — after the emit call returns, the SSE loop picks it up and yields). And if the frontend is NOT on a stream endpoint, nothing is received.\n\nAlso the heartbeat: if no events for `sse_heartbeat_seconds`, the API layer sends `: heartbeat` comment lines to keep the connection alive — shows the consumer loop is always draining.\n\nDo I need to check how the frontend consumes? I know from context: EventSource/fetch SSE in chat-session-view/execution-panel. I don't need to dig deeper for this answer — the question is about the backend emit semantics.\n\nPer the session convention: answer the concept precisely; annotation? The emit chain is already annotated in writer.py (emit signature comments) and harness.py's queue三件套 comments (user added those study comments themselves: \"queue —— 内存事件队列;控制器在后台任务里产出事件,SSE 生成器从这里消费并格式化成帧\"). So the code comments already cover this. No new annotation needed — the user's own comments at harness.py:699-705 literally describe this. So this is a pure conversational answer.\n\nKeep the answer structured but tight:\n1. 对,但精确一点:emit 执行完 = 事件进了内存队列,不是直接发给前端;API 层的 SSE 消费循环几乎同时取出来格式化成帧推给浏览器。同一事件循环,毫秒级延迟,体感上就是\"发了就收到\"。\n2. 前提:走的是流式端点(/run/stream、/run/resume/stream)。非流式 /run、/run/resume 用 NullHarnessEventWriter,事件构造后直接丢弃,前端最后只拿一个 JSON。\n3. 与 LangGraph 的对照:目的相同(进度广播),机制两层:\n   - LangGraph 的 stream_writer/query_graph custom 事件:图内节点进度,消费方是 QueryDataTool 的 astream 循环\n   - QueryDataTool 把 custom 事件经 writer.custom() 归一化成 tool.progress,进 Harness 统一通道\n   - 所以 LangGraph 写入是\"里层\",HarnessEventWriter 是\"外层\",里层事件被桥接进外层\n4. 前端接收形态:SSE 帧 id:/event:/data: 三行,event_type 作为 event 字段,浏览器 EventSource 按 event 名分发。\n\nKeep it in the user's language (Chinese). No code changes needed — their own comments already document the queue trio. Answer length: moderate.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"ff3da0b2-c56d-4bea-ba70-4be899a38732","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"基本对，但把“接收”这个动作拆精确一点——**emit 执行完 ≠ 前端已收到，而是“事件进了内存队列”**，真正推给前端的是 API 层的另一个循环：\n\n```\nemit()                                     API 层(同一进程内)\n  盖章(run_ref/event_id/时间戳)              queue → format_sse → SSE 帧\n  清洗(payload)                ──queue──→      │ id: xxx\n  sink.publish(非阻塞,立即返回)                 │ event: run.started\n                                              │ data: {...}\n                                              └→ HTTP chunk → 浏览器\n```\n\n两个生产者消费者跑在**同一个事件循环**里，emit 的毫秒之后消费循环就取走推给浏览器了，所以体感上“发了就收到”——但机制上是解耦的：emit 只管投递，不管谁收。你自己在 harness.py 里写的注释(queue/event_sink/writer 三件套那段)描述的就是这条链。\n\n三个精确点：\n\n1. **前提是流式端点**。`/run/stream`、`/run/resume/stream` 的 sink 是 `QueueEventSink`(入队+留存)。非流式 `/run`、`/run/resume` 用的是 `NullHarnessEventWriter`——事件照常构造但直接丢弃，前端最后只收到一个 JSON,没有过程事件。\n\n2. **与 LangGraph 的写入：目的相同，位置不同**。LangGraph 的 `stream_writer`(query_graph 图内节点的 custom 事件)是**里层**通道——它的消费方是 `QueryDataTool` 里的 `astream` 循环；工具再把 custom 事件经 `writer.custom()` 归一化成 `tool.progress`,桥接进 Harness 的**外层**统一通道。所以不是二选一，是里层被桥接进外层，前端只认外层协议。\n\n3. **前端收到的形态**：SSE 标准三行帧(`id:`/`event:`/`data:`),`event:` 字段就是 `EventType` 的值(run.started、tool.progress…),浏览器按事件名分发渲染；流空闲超过 `sse_heartbeat_seconds` 还会发 `: heartbeat` 注释行保活。\n\n一句话：你现有的理解(“和 LangGraph 写入差不多”)在**用途**上成立——都是“执行过程中往前端广播进度”；差别是 Harness 这套多了统一的盖章/清洗/协议层，并且把 LangGraph 的里层事件也收编了。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789985492210},{"id":"967747c4-a944-4991-a2b1-73a416316d1a","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"logger.info(\n   