rnessStateSnapshot.model_validate(payload).model_dump(mode=\"json\")` — `model_dump(mode=\"json\")` converts enums to their values → strings!\n\nSo the dict genuinely holds `str` values at runtime — typing it as `HarnessStatusType` would be WRONG (a lie), because `model_dump(mode=\"json\")` returns plain strings, not enum members. The whole point of this TypedDict is: it's the JSON-safe dict representation (what gets saved to PG / passed around as plain dict), while `HarnessStateSnapshot` (the Pydantic model) is the typed/validated representation.\n\nNote the contrast: `HarnessStateSnapshot.status: HarnessStatusType` — the Pydantic model holds enum members after validation; `model_dump(mode=\"json\")` serializes them to strings. So:\n- `HarnessControlState` (TypedDict): dict view, values are JSON primitives — `status: str` is correct\n- `HarnessStateSnapshot` (ContractModel): typed view, `status: HarnessStatusType` — enum\n\nThe two are bridged by `decode_harness_state` / `encode_harness_state` (validate → dump round trip).\n\nHowever — is there a sharper typing possible? Yes: `Literal[\"running\", \"waiting_confirmation\", ...]` would be more precise than bare `str` (TypedDict with Literal pins the exact value set). But it would duplicate the enum values as literals (two sources of truth — the exact thing the user and I just discussed!). Or `str` + a comment pointing at the enum. The current choice is pragmatic: the invariant is enforced by `decode_harness_state` (model_validate will reject invalid values anyway), so the TypedDict type is advisory; the Pydantic model is the enforcement point.\n\nAlso worth explaining `total=False`: all keys optional — because the dict can be partial (e.g., `state.get(\"harness\", {})` from an old checkpoint, partial payloads flow through decode which fills defaults). _DEFAULTS builds the full dict, but the type allows partial since validation backfills.\n\nAlso note: other fields similarly use loose types: `terminal_intent: str | None` (could be Literal[\"completed\",\"failed\",\"cancelled\",\"timeout\"]), `pending_confirmation: dict[str, Any] | None` (could be a nested TypedDict), `observations: list[dict[str, Any]]`. The design philosophy: this TypedDict is the *transport* shape; the Pydantic ContractModel is the *contract*. Tightening the TypedDict would duplicate the contract without adding enforcement (mypy isn't even run here? Not sure — but even with mypy, dict values flow through JSON persistence).\n\nSo the answer: 不是不正确,是刻意的 — status/phase 在这个 dict 里运行时真的是 str(枚举的 .value),类型写枚举反而是谎言。职责分层:\n- `HarnessStateSnapshot` = 强类型契约(枚举、校验) \n- `HarnessControlState` = JSON 传输形态(纯字符串/基础类型)\n- decode/encode 是两界的桥\n\nTrade-off note: `str` 确实是最松的选择;更严一点可以写 `Literal[...]` 枚举值集合,但那会把枚举值复制一份(两处真相),而且没有运行时收益(decode 校验才是闸门)。所以 `str` + 靠 decode 兜底是合理的。可以加注释说明这一点。\n\nPer session convention: answer + add annotation. The user is reading this file right now; a short comment on the two lines (or the class docstring) would help future readers with the same confusion. The class currently has NO docstring/comment at the top. Let me add:\n\n```python\nclass HarnessControlState(TypedDict, total=False):\n    \"\"\"Harness 现场的 JSON 传输形态；强类型契约见 HarnessStateSnapshot。\n\n    status/phase 等枚举字段在这里一律是 str（枚举的 .value）——这个 dict 是\n    model_dump(mode=\"json\") 的产物/输入，合法性与取值范围由 decode_harness_state\n    的 model_validate 统一把关，不在类型层重复枚举定义。\n    \"\"\"\n\n    schema_version: int\n    ...\n    # 以下取值必须落在 HarnessStatusType 枚举内；这里标 str 因为落库/传输时是 .value 字符串\n    status: str\n    phase: str\n```\n\nHmm, per user's docstring convention: \"docstring 只写几个字角色概括,细节放行内注释\". So docstring short: \"\"\"Harness 现场的 JSON 传输形态（强类型契约见 HarnessStateSnapshot）。\"\"\" and details as inline comments on status/phase lines.\n\nKeep it tight:\n\n```python\nclass HarnessControlState(TypedDict, total=False):\n    \"\"\"Harness 现场的 JSON 传输形态；强类型契约与校验见 HarnessStateSnapshot。\"\"\"\n```\n\nAnd inline at status/phase:\n```python\n    # 运行时取值是枚举的 .value 字符串（mod