on). The controller wrapper is a thin adapter between two data shapes (whole state vs harness sub-dict).\n\nOne more angle the user might be probing: \"wrapper 的 return state + 原地赋值看起来既改又返回\" — the dual effect. I'll address that directly: 它确实\"既改原地又返回\",这是刻意的:原地赋值保证 state[\"harness\"] 引用更新,返回让调用点写成 state = ...(显式数据流)。二者缺一不可?No — 原地赋值是必须的(返回的 state 引用同一个外层 dict),返回是风格。Precisely: the function MUST do the assignment `state[\"harness\"] = ...` (that's the actual effect); the `return state` is optional-but-conventional.\n\nAnswer concisely. No code changes needed — this is a judgment question. No commit.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"a1fad973-2d8b-49ee-8642-c84a249a346a","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"不多余——而且这是你自己那条“单调用点不封装”原则的**正面对照案例**：它有 **13 个调用点**(我数了)，是 `_run` 里重复频率最高的模式。\n\n拆开看它包住了什么：\n\n1. **`state[\"harness\"] = ...(state[\"harness\"], ...)` 这个子字典搬运**。底层函数 `transition_harness_state` 只认识 harness 字典(输入输出都是它)，不认识外层 state。如果没有这层包装，13 个调用点每个都要写：\n\n```python\nstate[\"harness\"] = transition_harness_state(\n    state[\"harness\"],\n    status=HarnessStatusType.RUNNING,\n    phase=LoopPhaseStatusType.BUILD_CONTEXT,\n)\n```\n\n\"外层 state 里挂着 harness 子字典\"这个布局知识就复制到 13 处——哪天状态布局变了，改 13 处。包装之后这个知识只有一份。\n\n2. **`return state` 严格说确实可省**——dict 是引用，原地改完不返回也生效。但留着它，调用点能写成 `state = self._transition(state, ...)`,每个迁移点读起来就是一句“state 在这里推进了一步”，和 `_run` 的整体数据流风格一致。去掉的话调用点变成孤零零的 `self._transition(state, ...)`,副作用藏进了裸调用里。这是可读性取舍，不是错误。\n\n3. 分层上也各司其职，没有重叠：**校验逻辑**(迁移表、终态保护)在 store 层的 `transition_harness_state`;controller 的 `_transition` 只是薄适配器，管\"整个 state ↔ harness 子字典”的边界。薄 ≠ 多余——它是两个数据形态之间唯一的桥。\n\n判断标准回到你自己的原则：调用点数量。单处调用时它是该删的分离，13 处调用时它是该有的收敛。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789986944258},{"id":"22279530-5a4d-41e6-b313-3243d5100c0d","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"你没感觉这13个调用点都是多余的吗，我直接使用     state = {\n            ...state,\n            harness=transition_harness_state(\n            state[\"harness\"],\n            status=status,\n            phase=phase,\n            terminal_intent=terminal_intent,\n        )\n        }这么写不行吗","payload":{"query":"你没感觉这13个调用点都是多余的吗，我直接使用     state = {\n            ...state,\n            harness=transition_harness_state(\n            state[\"harness\"],\n            status=status,\n            phase=phase,\n            terminal_intent=terminal_intent,\n        )\n        }这么写不行吗","rawMessage":"你没感觉这13个调用点都是多余的吗，我直接使用     state = {\n            ...state,\n            harness=transition_harness_state(\n            state[\"harness\"],\n            status=status,\n            phase=phase,\n            terminal_intent=terminal_intent,\n        )\n        }这么写不行吗","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"be4b7ae7-5bc3-410f-8411-e54f97360b5e","requestedAt":1789987195029,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"22279530-5a4d-41e6-b313-3243d5100c0d"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789987195208},{"id":"f63f7e66-4635-4a48-a7b1-9264fc1f1475","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"22279530-5a4d-41e6-b313-3243d5100c0d","reportedId":"2bf4608f-9971-4801-a5df-0e8ecd98262e","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":61.33,"contextUsed":157012,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":1024,"totalDuration":71030},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab1097ce5abac4a6883630f","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":70008},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"e050a874-c28c-481c-a0a1-c9b946eafb5a","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user is asking: \"你没感觉这13个调用点都是多余的吗,我直接使用 state = {...state, harness=transition_harness_state(...)} 这么写不行吗\"\n\nSo they're suggesting: instead of `state = self._transition(state, status=..., phase=...)`, write inline at each call site:\n\n```python\nstate = {\n    **state,\n    \"harness\": transition_harness_state(\n        state[\"harness\"],\n        status=status,\n        phase=phase,\n        terminal_intent=terminal_intent,\n    )\n}\n```\n\nWait — their syntax `harness=transition_harness_state(...)` inside `{...state, ...}` is dict-literal syntax with `=` which is wrong; dict literals need `:`, i.e. `\"harness\": transition_harness_state(...)`. The `{...state, harness=...}` syntax is actually... `{**state, harness=x}` is invalid Python (dict display doesn't support keyword= syntax; that's only for function calls / dict(...) constructor). Actually `dict(**state, harness=...)` works if all keys are strings, but `{**state, harness=...}` is a SyntaxError. So their snippet as written is syntactically invalid — should be `{**state, \"harness\": transition_harness_state(...)}`. I should point that out gently.\n\nNow the substantive question: would inlining this at 13 call sites be better than the `_transition` helper?\n\nLet me think carefully and honestly, playing devil's advocate against my previous answer:\n\nUser's proposal at each call site:\n```python\nstate = {\n    **state,\n    \"harness\": transition_harness_state(\n        state[\"harness\"],\n        status=HarnessStatusType.RUNNING,\n        phase=LoopPhaseStatusType.BUILD_CONTEXT,\n    ),\n}\n```\n\nvs current:\n```python\nstate = self._transition(\n    state, status=HarnessStatusType.RUNNING, phase=LoopPhaseStatusType.BUILD_CONTEXT\n)\n```\n\nArguments for user's version (steelmanning):\n- Removes one indirection layer; reader sees exactly what happens (dict copy + harness replaced).\n- No dependence on a controller-internal helper.\n\nArguments against (for keeping _transition):\n1. **Verbosity × 13**: the inline version is 8 lines vs 3 lines per call site. The `_run` function is already ~200 lines; adding 5 lines × 13 = +65 lines of pure noise. The user's own memory/feedback: \"只有一处调用的私有函数不封装\" — the flip side is 13 call sites IS the case for consolidation. The noise-to-signal ratio gets worse: at every transition site, you'd have to visually filter the boilerplate `{**state, \"harness\": ...}` to find the actual information (which status/phase).\n\n2. **Semantic loss**: `_transition` names the operation (\"推进状态机一步\"). The inline version buries the intent in mechanics. Actually the user's version is arguably MORE explicit about mechanics... but the mechanics are identical at all 13 sites; the only varying part is status/phase (and occasionally terminal_intent). Naming the constant part is exactly what a helper is for.\n\n3. **Subtle difference: mutation vs copy**. Important! `self._transition` mutates `state[\"harness\"]` in place: `state[\"harness\"] = transition_harness_state(...)` — the SAME outer dict object gets its \"harness\" key updated. The user's `{**state, \"harness\": ...}` creates a NEW outer dict (shallow copy) and does NOT mutate the original. In the current codebase, are there other references to the same state dict that rely on seeing the update? Hmm — `_run` gets `state` passed in and reassigns its local. If any other component held a reference to the same dict (e.g., a checkpoint created earlier, or the LangGraph-ish state threading), the copy version would fork the state: the old reference would keep the old harness. Does anything alias `state`? In `_start`/`_run`/`_finalize`, state is threaded through locals and passed to helpers which return new/reassigned states... The codebase style is \"reassign state\" everywhere, which works with BOTH mutation and copy since everything reassigns from the return value. But `HarnessGraphState` is a dict; helpers like `_save_running_state(command, state)` receive the current state. As long as the caller passes the latest, fine.\n\n   But there's a real difference: with copy semantics, if any helper captured the state dict and read it later (async!), it would see stale data. Are there such captures? E.g., `_await_with_deadline` just awaits. The event writer doesn't hold state. The confirmation pause stores state explicitly. I don't see an aliasing hazard in the current code, but mutation-vs-copy IS a behavioral difference — switching to copy semantics silently changes what in-place observers see. It happens to be safe here, but it's a change one must verify, not a free refactor.\n\n   Actually wait — also `state = {**state, \"harness\": ...}` shallow-copies the outer dict; nested values (observations list, etc.) are shared references — but transition_harness_state already returns a fresh harness dict, so that's fine.\n\n4. **The keyword syntax error**: `{...state, harness=...}` isn't valid Python. `**state` spread + `\"harness\": ...` key is correct. Minor but worth noting since the user is learning.\n\n5. **Consistency argument**: the codebase threads state functionally (`state = self._transition(...)`, `state = self._transition(...)`). 13 sites reading uniformly beats 13 inline blocks.\n\n6. Where does `transition_harness_state` get imported? The controller already imports it (from state.py). With inline usage, the import stays. Fine.\n\n7. User's deeper point: \"13 个调用点都是多余的\" — maybe they mean the REPEATED transition+save pairs? Or the call sites themselves? I read it as: with inline dict-comprehension style, the helper becomes unnecessary, so the 13 call sites could directly call transition_harness_state. My previous answer defended the helper on \"13 call sites\" grounds. The user challenges: the helper only saves ONE line per site (`state[\"harness\"] = ...` → dict spread). Is that enough to justify a helper?\n\nHonest cost-benefit: \n- Inline: `state = {**state, \"harness\": transition_harness_state(state[\"harness\"], status=..., phase=...)}` — actually this can be ONE line if compact: `state = {**state, \"harness\": transition_harness_state(state[\"harness\"], status=S, phase=P)}`. That's ~110 chars — over typical line limits, would wrap to 3-4 lines anyway.\n- The helper: 3 lines at call site, one 15-line definition.\n\nSo the helper saves maybe 1-2 lines per site and centralizes the \"harness is a sub-key\" knowledge. The strongest argument remains: 13× repetition of a mechanical pattern whose varying part is only (status, phase, terminal_intent). The varying/constant split is textbook helper material. The user's inline alternative doesn't remove the repetition — it just removes the naming of it. The repetition of mechanics is STILL 13× (arguably the user thinks that's fine because it's \"just syntax\"?).\n\nAlso the semantic point: `_transition` enforces ONE way to mutate the harness control state within the controller. With inline spreads, someone will eventually write `{**state, \"harness\": {...harness, \"status\": ...}}` (bypassing transition_harness_state validation!) — the named helper is a chokepoint making the invalid path visible in review. That's a real maintainability point: the helper isn't just less text, it's a single gate.\n\nCounter-consideration: is `_transition` maybe TOO thin to earn its keep, per YAGNI? No — thin adapters over a frequently-called operation with 13 sites are standard. The \"single-use inline\" principle the user holds doesn't apply at 13 uses.\n\nOne more honesty check — is there anything the user's version does BETTER?\n- It avoids the \"mutate and return\" duality I acknowledged last time (their version is pure copy, no in-place mutation). That's aesthetically cleaner but changes semantics (aliasing).\n- It removes one import-level indirection. Marginal.\n\nSo my answer: 可以跑通(改对语法后),但我不建议,理由:\n1. 语法先纠错:dict 字面量里 `harness=...` 不合法,要写 `\"harness\": ...`(或者 dict(**state, harness=...) — 所有键必须是 str,这里恰好是,但不推荐)。\n2. 行数账:内联版每处 4-6 行 vs 3 行,13 处净增 ~40-60 行纯模板;而真正变化的信息(status/phase)被淹没在同样的样板里。\n3. 重复并没有消失:内联只是把\"给重复模式起名字\"去掉了,机械重复仍 13 次。helper 的价值恰是把常量部分(搬运+校验调用)命名一次。\n4. 混淆点:内联 spread 版把\"原地改\"变成\"浅拷贝新 dict\"——语义变了。当前 13 处是原地更新;如果有别处持有同一 dict 引用,拷贝版会分叉。现在代码恰好安全(都靠返回值传递),但这是一次需要全链路验证的行为变更,不是等价改写。\n5. 防御点:_transition 是唯一入口,review 时一眼看出所有迁移都走 transition_harness_state(经过迁移表校验);内联后早晚有人写出 `{**state, \"harness\": {**harness, \"status\": \"completed\"}}` 直接绕过校验。\n6. 结论:可以,但更差。这属于\"helper 的存在成本 < 13 处样板的阅读成本\"的情形。\n\nAlso tie back to their principle: 单调用点内联 vs 多调用点收敛——13 处正是收敛的那一侧。\n\nShould I demo what one call site would look like properly? Yes, briefly.\n\nNo code changes needed. Pure consultation. Keep it tight, respect their terminology preference, be direct.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"3c2b9e83-b4e4-4d52-9484-75df6d79ad16","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"语法先纠一个小错：dict 字面量里不能写 `harness=...`,得是 `\"harness\": ...`(`{**state, \"harness\": ...}` 才合法)。改对之后，你的写法是：\n\n```python\nstate = {\n    **state,\n    \"harness\": transition_harness_state(\n        state[\"harness\"],\n        status=HarnessStatusType.RUNNING,\n        phase=LoopPhaseStatusType.BUILD_CONTEXT,\n    ),\n}\n```\n\n**能跑，但我不建议换**，三个理由，按分量排：\n\n1. **重复并没有消失，只是不给它起名字了**。13 处调用点，变的只有 `status`/`phase` 两个值；搬运(`**state` + `\"harness\":` + 子字典进出)是完全相同的样板。`_transition` 的作用就是把“常量部分”命名一次，调用点只剩信息量。换成你的写法，`_run` 净增约 40-60 行纯模板，而且每一处都要用眼睛过滤样板才能找到真正的信息——**你消除的是一层缩进，换来的是 13 段噪音**。\n\n2. **语义悄悄变了：原地改 → 浅拷贝**。现在的 `_transition` 是 `state[\"harness\"] = ...`,**原地更新同一个外层 dict**;你的 `{**state, \"harness\": ...}` 是**造一个新 dict**,旧引用看不到更新。当前代码恰好安全(所有地方都靠返回值传递 state,没有别名持有)，所以这次改写不会立刻炸——但它不是等价重构，是一次需要全链路验证的行为变更。\n\n3. **少了一个唯一入口的防御**。`_transition` 在 review 时能一眼确认“所有迁移都经过迁移表校验”；放开内联后，早晚有人写出：\n\n```python\nstate = {**state, \"harness\": {**state[\"harness\"], \"status\": \"completed\"}}  # 绕过校验!\n```\n\n直接改字段、跳过 `_PHASE_TRANSITIONS` 和终态保护。命名的 helper 是把合法路径固定成唯一路径。\n\n回到你自己的判断标准：**单调用点内联，多调用点收敛**。上次 `_emit_terminal` 你删得对(1 处)；这次 13 处正是收敛的那一侧。感觉“多余”的真实来源可能是 helper 太薄——但薄是它的职责刚好小(两个数据形态之间的桥)，不是它不该存在。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789987267390},{"id":"c4d0d5a7-76f0-4af2-a6ef-8f85373bc443","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"什么叫做_PHASE_TRANSITIONS","payload":{"query":"什么叫做_PHASE_TRANSITIONS","rawMessage":"什么叫做_PHASE_TRANSITIONS","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"57ec325c-1701-4a85-891f-8474682a1c46","requestedAt":1789987322176,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"c4d0d5a7-76f0-4af2-a6ef-8f85373bc443"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789987322192},{"id":"18758e4a-2e2e-42ed-bdf6-0634ec3cb843","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"c4d0d5a7-76f0-4af2-a6ef-8f85373bc443","reportedId":"40343124-0626-428d-9dc9-c8f653f6b687","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":62.11,"contextUsed":158996,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":648,"totalDuration":45084},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab109fa23332500531b501f","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":44437},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"9d76d8c2-d966-497f-b7a2-0b55f1e0c4e4","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"什么叫做 _PHASE_TRANSITIONS\" — what is `_PHASE_TRANSITIONS`?\n\nThey're looking at state.py (their focused file). `_PHASE_TRANSITIONS` is the phase transition table defined at state.py:83-121 (from the file they have open). I've mentioned it several times in passing (\"迁移表\"), but now they want a proper explanation.\n\nExplain:\n1. What it is: a dict mapping each LoopPhaseStatusType phase → the set of phases it's allowed to move to next. It's the phase-level state machine (the micro skeleton of a run's lifecycle).\n2. Show the structure simply — maybe a compact table/diagram of the 10 phases and their allowed next steps.\n3. Where it's enforced: `transition_harness_state` at state.py:170 — `if phase not in _PHASE_TRANSITIONS[current.phase]: raise ValueError(...)`. So any transition not in the table is rejected.\n4. What it guards against: e.g., PLAN → EXECUTE_TOOL directly (skipping VALIDATE_ACTION) is illegal; WAIT_CONFIRMATION can only go to RESTORE_RUN or FINALIZATION (after resume, you must restore first); FINALIZATION only goes to itself (terminal lock); terminal status + FINALIZATION is the exit.\n5. Interpret the entries with the run flow:\n   - START_RUN → {BUILD_CONTEXT, FINALIZATION}: fresh run either builds context or goes straight to finalize (e.g., start failed)\n   - RESTORE_RUN → {BUILD_CONTEXT, FINALIZATION}: resumed run rebuilds context\n   - BUILD_CONTEXT → {BUILD_CONTEXT (self-loop, rebuild/重试), PLAN, FINALIZATION}\n   - PLAN → {PLAN, VALIDATE_ACTION, FINALIZATION}\n   - VALIDATE_ACTION → {VALIDATE_ACTION, EXECUTE_TOOL, WAIT_CONFIRMATION, FINALIZATION} — ask_user pauses from here\n   - EXECUTE_TOOL → {EXECUTE_TOOL (retry), HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT, FINALIZATION}\n   - HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT → {RECORD_OBSERVATION, WAIT_CONFIRMATION (needs_user), FINALIZATION}\n   - RECORD_OBSERVATION → {BUILD_CONTEXT (next iteration), FINALIZATION}\n   - WAIT_CONFIRMATION → {RESTORE_RUN, FINALIZATION} — resume must pass through RESTORE_RUN\n   - FINALIZATION → {FINALIZATION} — absorbing/终态锁\n6. Note the self-loops (BUILD_CONTEXT → BUILD_CONTEXT etc.) mean staying in the same phase is legal (e.g., context rebuild retry, tool retry).\n7. Relationship to the earlier discussed concepts: LoopPhaseStatusType = 阶段指针 (微观位置); this table = 阶段之间的合法迁移图; status transitions have their own guards in transition_harness_state (terminal protection, intent matching). The table only governs phase; the status rules are separate code.\n8. Note it's module-private (leading underscore) — used only inside state.py by transition_harness_state; callers can't bypass it because the transition function is the only write path.\n\nVisual: a diagram would help. Let me draw the graph:\n\n```\nSTART_RUN ──┐\nRESTORE_RUN ┘→ BUILD_CONTEXT ⇄ PLAN → VALIDATE_ACTION → EXECUTE_TOOL ⇄ HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT → RECORD_OBSERVATION ─┐\n                ↑                                                            │                    ↑             │\n                └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                    │             │\n                    (下一轮)                        WAIT_CONFIRMATION ←──────────┘ (ask_user/needs_user)          │\n                         ↑ │                                                                                      │\n                         │ └→ RESTORE_RUN → BUILD_CONTEXT ...                                                     │\n                         │                                                                                        │\n                    (所有阶段) ──→ FINALIZATION (自锁,终态唯一出口) ←─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nHmm, that's getting messy. Better to present as a list of edges per phase (compact table), then a simplified linear main path:\n\n主路径: START_RUN → BUILD_CONTEXT → PLAN → VALIDATE_ACTION → EXECUTE_TOOL → HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT → RECORD_OBSERVATION → (下一轮) BUILD_CONTEXT → ...\n\n出口: VALIDATE_ACTION → WAIT_CONFIRMATION (ask_user); HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT → WAIT_CONFIRMATION (needs_user); WAIT_CONFIRMATION → RESTORE_RUN → BUILD_CONTEXT (恢复); 所有阶段 → FINALIZATION (收口).\n\nAlso explain \"为什么 VALIDATE_ACTION 能到 WAIT_CONFIRMATION 而 PLAN 不能\": ask_user 动作在校验段被发现,暂停发生在动作提交前——对应 _run 注释里的 ⑦⑨ 步。\n\nKeep the answer focused and pedagogical. No code changes needed — the table itself is already in their open file; maybe no annotation needed. This is a pure concept question. Could consider annotating the _PHASE_TRANSITIONS dict with a comment... The entries are self-explanatory to a degree; the user asked \"什么叫做\" = they want the concept explained. I'll answer in text. If they want comments in code they'll ask (pattern: they say \"打一下注释\").\n\nFormat: short definition, the map, the enforcement point, what it prevents. Use the file's line numbers. Keep it reasonably compact.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"9df3a11b-e7c9-47b1-984d-9f6cc5384c6a","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"`_PHASE_TRANSITIONS` 是**阶段迁移表**——一张写死的图，规定“每个阶段之后允许去哪”。它在 state.py:83(你正打开的文件)，是 10 个 `LoopPhaseStatusType` 各自的“合法下一站”集合。\n\n**结构**：键 = 当前阶段，值 = 允许迁移到的阶段集合：\n\n| 当前阶段 | 允许的下一站 | 对应的业务场景 |\n|---|---|---|\n| START_RUN | BUILD_CONTEXT, FINALIZATION | 新运行先建上下文；启动即失败则直接收口 |\n| RESTORE_RUN | BUILD_CONTEXT, FINALIZATION | 恢复的运行重建上下文 |\n| BUILD_CONTEXT | 自身， PLAN, FINALIZATION | 可重试重建(自环)；建完去规划 |\n| PLAN | 自身， VALIDATE_ACTION, FINALIZATION | Planner 重试(自环) |\n| VALIDATE_ACTION | 自身， EXECUTE_TOOL, **WAIT_CONFIRMATION**, FINALIZATION | ask_user 暂停发生在这(动作提交前) |\n| EXECUTE_TOOL | 自身， HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT, FINALIZATION | 工具重试(自环) |\n| HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT | RECORD_OBSERVATION, **WAIT_CONFIRMATION**, FINALIZATION | 工具返回 needs_user 时暂停 |\n| RECORD_OBSERVATION | **BUILD_CONTEXT**, FINALIZATION | 下一轮从头重建上下文 |\n| WAIT_CONFIRMATION | **RESTORE_RUN**, FINALIZATION | 恢复必须先走 RESTORE_RUN,不许直接跳业务段 |\n| FINALIZATION | 自身 | 吸收态：收口后锁定，只原地不动 |\n\n**执行点**:`transition_harness_state`(state.py:170)——每次迁移前查表：\n\n```python\nif phase not in _PHASE_TRANSITIONS[current.phase]:\n    raise ValueError(f\"非法 Harness 阶段转换: {current.phase} -> {phase}\")\n```\n\n所以这张表就是“阶段指针能怎么走”的**唯一法律**。跳步(比如 PLAN 直接去 EXECUTE_TOOL,漏掉校验段)、倒退(比如 WAIT_CONFIRMATION 直接跳回 EXECUTE_TOOL,绕过恢复段)都会当场 `ValueError`,现场根本写不进库。\n\n**主流程串起来**就是:\n\n```\nSTART_RUN/RESTORE_RUN → BUILD_CONTEXT → PLAN → VALIDATE_ACTION\n    → EXECUTE_TOOL → HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT → RECORD_OBSERVATION ─┐\n         ↑                                                    │\n         └────────────── 下一轮(带观察重建上下文) ←────────────┘\n\n暂停出口: VALIDATE_ACTION ─(ask_user)→ WAIT_CONFIRMATION ─(resume)→ RESTORE_RUN\n          HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT ─(needs_user)→ WAIT_CONFIRMATION\n收口出口: 任何阶段 ─→ FINALIZATION(只进不出,自环锁定)\n```\n\n三个设计点：\n\n1. **自环 = 阶段内重试**。BUILD_CONTEXT→BUILD_CONTEXT、EXECUTE_TOOL→EXECUTE_TOOL 这些“自己到自己”的边，就是重试仍然停留在本阶段的表达。\n2. **两个暂停出口不对称**：ask_user 在 VALIDATE_ACTION 就拦(动作还没提交)，needs_user 在 HANDLE_TOOL_RESULT 才拦(工具已执行完、有结果了)——这正是 `_run` 注释里 ⑦“提交前拦截”和 ⑫“结果要求确认”两个位置。\n3. **表只管 phase,不管 status**。宏观状态(HarnessStatusType)的约束是另一套，写在同一个函数里：终态只能由 running/finalization + 同名 terminal_intent 提交、WAITING_CONFIRMATION↔wait_confirmation 组合校验等。微观位置和宏观状态分别把关，再由 `validate_combination` 交叉验证。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789987367456},{"id":"e23fa327-d9f8-4ae3-9e8b-207d1d7a24de","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"没有跳过啊transition_harness_state()不是一直在执行吗","payload":{"query":"没有跳过啊transition_harness_state()不是一直在执行吗","rawMessage":"没有跳过啊transition_harness_state()不是一直在执行吗","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"cb0a5d67-0e23-4604-a2c5-a1dffe70b307","requestedAt":1789987387615,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"e23fa327-d9f8-4ae3-9e8b-207d1d7a24de"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789987387636},{"id":"03927895-e7ba-487b-9889-3979e3642d15","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"e23fa327-d9f8-4ae3-9e8b-207d1d7a24de","reportedId":"45829f9a-2bb6-48d5-a0af-33a6dcd355f0","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":62.59,"contextUsed":160231,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":915,"totalDuration":36743},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab10a3cd0d0586a4a65eed0","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":35829},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"b7cdf7af-6789-4a36-9fc9-58b770b2a0ce","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user says: \"没有跳过啊transition_harness_state()不是一直在执行吗\" — \"There's no skipping; isn't transition_harness_state() always being executed?\"\n\nHmm. They seem confused by my statement that the table prevents 跳步/倒退. Their point: since every state change in the controller goes through `transition_harness_state()` (via `_transition`), it's always executed — so how could anything \"skip\" it? Or maybe they misunderstand: they think \"transition_harness_state 一直在执行\" means the function always runs fine, so where does the rejection happen?\n\nI think their confusion: I said \"跳步、倒退都会当场 ValueError,现场根本写不进库\" — they're responding \"there's no skipping — transition_harness_state is always executed [so the table check always happens]\". They may be conflating two things:\n1. The FUNCTION being called (always happens — every write goes through it)\n2. The transition being LEGAL (the table check inside may reject)\n\nTheir statement is actually correct and is precisely the design: because transition_harness_state is the ONLY write path, the table check is ALWAYS executed — that's why skipping is impossible. My earlier phrasing \"跳步会被拦\" was about hypothetical code that tried to jump phases. The user might be thinking \"既然只有这一条路,那什么情况下会出现'非法转换'?\"\n\nSo my answer should clarify:\n- 你说得对:所有写路径都走 transition_harness_state,表检查每次都执行——这正是\"跳不过去\"的原因,不是矛盾。\n- \"跳步/倒退\"不是现实发生的场景,而是**防的是未来代码写错**——防御性设计。表在检查的是\"这次调用想从 X 去 Y\"是否合法。正常主循环永远走合法边(所以你看到的一直在执行、一直通过);表的价值在于当有人写出非法迁移时(改代码、新增分支、bug),当场炸而不是把非法现场写进库。\n- 举例:假如某天有人在 _run 里写 phase=EXECUTE_TOOL 从 PLAN 直接过(想省掉校验段),transition_harness_state 会 raise ValueError → 崩在写库前 → 测试/开发当场发现,而不是生产里出现\"没有经过校验就执行工具\"的现场。\n- 另一个真实会触发的场景:数据损坏/手工改库/老版本数据 —— decode/model_validate 也会拦。\n- Also clarify the check semantics: `if phase not in _PHASE_TRANSITIONS[current.phase]: raise`. \"一直在执行\"的正是这个 if——每次都查,绝大多数时候通过。\n\nSo the core clarification: \"一直在执行\" 和 \"拦住非法迁移\" 不矛盾——函数每次都跑,表每次都查,查的结果绝大多数是放行。表不是为了拦截日常流程(日常流程全是合法边),是为了让\"非法迁移\"在代码层面不可能发生。\n\nKeep it short — this is a small clarification turn. No code changes. Maybe a tiny concrete example of what a rejected call looks like:\n\n```python\n# PLAN 阶段的现场\ntransition_harness_state(state, status=RUNNING, phase=EXECUTE_TOOL)\n# → ValueError: 非法 Harness 阶段转换: plan -> execute_tool\n```\n\nAlso tie to the earlier framing: 这和 ContractModel extra=\"forbid\" 是同一哲学——fail fast,把错误堵在写入点。","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"269f461e-42e4-4a40-9cad-4e0ee0fd5486","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"你说得对，而且这恰恰就是设计意图——**“一直在执行”和“拦住跳步”不矛盾**：\n\n- `transition_harness_state` 是**唯一写入口**，每次迁移都调用它 ✓\n- 调用时**每次都查表**:`if phase not in _PHASE_TRANSITIONS[current.phase]` ✓\n- 主循环走的全是合法边，所以**每次都放行**——你平时看到的永远是“执行了、通过了”\n\n表拦截的不是日常流程，而是**“假如哪天代码写出了非法迁移”**。日常流程根本不会触发它，它是防未来、防错误的，不是防现在的。举个具体例子：\n\n```python\n# 假设某天有人改 _run,想从 PLAN 直接跳去执行工具(漏掉校验段):\ntransition_harness_state(state, status=RUNNING, phase=EXECUTE_TOOL)\n\n# 当前 phase 是 plan,查表:plan 的合法下一站是 {plan, validate_action, finalization}\n# execute_tool 不在集合里 → 当场:\n# ValueError: 非法 Harness 阶段转换: plan -> execute_tool\n```\n\n崩在**写库之前**——非法现场根本到不了 PostgreSQL,开发和测试阶段就炸出来，而不是生产里出现“没经过校验就执行了工具”的运行记录。\n\n所以准确的说法是：\n\n| | 日常(合法边) | 异常(非法边) |\n|---|---|---|\n| transition_harness_state 执行？ | ✓ | ✓ |\n| 查表结果 | 放行，更新 phase | **raise,拒绝写入** |\n\n这和 `ContractModel(extra=\"forbid\")` 是同一套哲学：**fail fast at the write point**。合法数据感觉不到约束的存在，非法数据一个都过不去。你观察到“它一直在执行”，正说明约束长在了必经之路上，而不是散落在各处的 if 检查。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789987424583},{"id":"56c30b91-074f-47e7-8e17-8e3d8eba4b10","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"你不感觉state = {**state, \"harness\": {**state[\"harness\"], \"status\": \"completed\"}}  这样更清晰一点吗","payload":{"query":"你不感觉state = {**state, \"harness\": {**state[\"harness\"], \"status\": \"completed\"}}  这样更清晰一点吗","rawMessage":"你不感觉state = {**state, \"harness\": {**state[\"harness\"], \"status\": \"completed\"}}  这样更清晰一点吗","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isC