_state)\n   - clears pending_confirmation on WAITING_CONFIRMATION → RUNNING\n3. Assigns back to state[\"harness\"]\n\nWhereas \"update\" (dict.update or general \"set fields\") just overwrites values with no rules.\n\nSo: `_transition` = update + 校验 + 版本推进 + 特殊副作用. The \"update\" framing captures the mechanical part (写字段), misses everything that makes it a state machine.\n\nKey differences from a plain update:\n1. **update 是无条件的,transition 是有条件的** — update 任何值都能写;transition 只有迁移表允许的边才能走(上一轮刚讲过的查表)。\n2. **update 不改变其他字段;transition 会连带推进 state_version(+1)** — 版本号是乐观锁/fencing 的一部分,普通 update 永远不会想到要维护它。\n3. **transition 有校验双保险** — 前置(model_validate 现场合法)和后置(decode 候选合法),非法组合写不进去。\n4. **副作用**:WAITING_CONFIRMATION → RUNNING 时自动清 pending_confirmation。\n5. 术语上:update 是数据操作,\"transition\" 是状态机术语——状态从 A 到 B 的一次迁移,受迁移规则约束。这也是为什么叫 _transition 不叫 _update:名字声明了\"这一步有规则\"。\n\nA good analogy for the user (they know frontend/React): setState vs 直接改 state?Like `setState` vs mutating state directly — React 里你不能直接 `this.state.x = 1`,要走 setState(带 reconcile 规则)。Or: update 是\"改值\",transition 是\"改值+守门\"。\n\nFormula:\n```\n_transition(state, status, phase) ≈ 查表放行 → 写入 status/phase → state_version+1 → 再校验 → 回写\n```\nvs\n```\nupdate: state[\"harness\"][\"status\"] = ...   # 只有\"写\",没有\"守\"\n```\n\nKeep it short — this is a quick conceptual confirmation question. The answer: 形像,神不像/机械上像 update,规则上完全不是。Give the 3 concrete extras. Short response.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"329ab35f-d59e-49bb-a00f-f48db1f8a4d2","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"机械上像，规则上完全不是——**`_transition` = update + 守门**，多出来的部分恰恰是它的价值：\n\n```python\n# 如果只是 update,等价于:\nstate[\"harness\"][\"status\"] = \"running\"   # 想写什么写什么\nstate[\"harness\"][\"phase\"] = \"build_context\"\n\n# 而 _transition 实际执行的是:\n# ① 查迁移表:当前 phase → 目标 phase 这条边存在吗?不存在 → ValueError\n# ② 终态守卫:终态只能由 running/finalization + 同名 terminal_intent 提交\n# ③ 写入 status/phase/terminal_intent   ← 只有这一步像 update\n# ④ state_version + 1                   ← 版本推进,update 永远不会想到\n# ⑤ decode 再校验:候选现场组合合法(如终态必须在 finalization)才能落库\n# ⑥ 副作用:WAITING_CONFIRMATION → RUNNING 时自动清 pending_confirmation\n```\n\n三个本质差别：\n\n1. **update 无条件，transition 有条件**——update 是“写”，transition 是“查表允许才写”\n2. **update 只动你写的字段，transition 连带维护 `state_version`**——这是乐观锁/并发防护的锚点，手写 update 十次有十次会忘了加\n3. **update 不保证结果合法，transition 写前写后各校验一次**\n\n所以叫 `_transition` 不叫 `_update` 是刻意的：transition 是状态机术语——\"从状态 A **迁移**到状态 B,受迁移规则约束”；update 是数据操作——“把值改掉，仅此而已”。名字在告诉你：这一步有规则，别绕。\n\n类比 React 的话:`_transition` 之于 `transition_harness_state`,有点像 `setState` 之于直接改 `this.state`——直接改也能\"生效”，但绕过了 reconcile 的规则，出问题没人拦你。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789987656155},{"id":"8baac0df-cc49-4995-955d-03dc06126fa8","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"_transition ->updata_harness_state  ,可以这么改吗？","payload":{"query":"_transition ->updata_harness_state  ,可以这么改吗？","rawMessage":"_transition ->updata_harness_state  ,可以这么改吗？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"98f288bf-1b4a-42f9-b93f-549089104ada","requestedAt":1789987744610,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"8baac0df-cc49-4995-955d-03dc06126fa8"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789987744622},{"id":"bb9d4b7d-796f-4dee-a68c-cbc9a3b1c018","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"8baac0df-cc49-4995-955d-03dc06126fa8","reportedId":"7748dd29-6b22-46ae-a1a9-d6eab9ac273d","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":64.43,"contextUsed":164944,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":644,"totalDuration":35331},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab10ba12dd493057d7b9a32","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":34689},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"6a14c17c-0d6e-4d91-958b-751824ec456d","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"_transition -> update_harness_state, 可以这么改吗?\" — Can we rename `_transition` to `update_harness_state`?\n\nThis is exactly the terminology discipline issue we've been building through this conversation. The user just learned why it's called `_transition` and not `_update` (transition = state machine term with rules; update = plain data write). Now they propose renaming it TO `update_harness_state`.\n\nMy answer should be: 不建议 / 反对 — because:\n\n1. It would undo the semantic point from the last message. The name `_transition` declares \"this is a state machine migration with rules\". `update_harness_state` declares \"this is a data write\" — which is precisely the weaker, misleading name. If we just spent a message establishing that transition ≠ update, renaming transition → update moves in the wrong direction.\n\n2. **Name collision risk**: there's already `transition_harness_state` in state.py (the store-layer function). `_transition` is the controller's adapter for it. Renaming to `update_harness_state` would create a misleading parallel naming family: `transition_harness_state` vs `update_harness_state` — readers would think they're different operations when one is just the controller-side adapter of the other. Actually a name like `update_harness_state` suggests it's the store-layer CRUD counterpart... \n\n3. Naming convention mapping: `_transition` mirrors `transition_harness_state` — the adapter keeps the verb of the underlying operation it delegates to. That's the convention: wrapper keeps the domain verb. If anything, a \"fuller\" name would be `_transition_harness_state` or `_transition_harness` (keeping transition), not changing the verb.\n\n4. The user's terminology discipline (from memory: 术语要精确不滥用大词; they corrected me on lifecycle terminology). They care about precise terms. \"update\" is precisely the term we just established is WRONG for this operation. So by their own standard, the rename is a step backward.\n\nIf they feel `_transition` is too terse/unclear, better alternatives (if any) would keep the \"transition\" stem: e.g., `_transition_harness` — but honestly `_transition` within LoopController context is fine. Also @staticmethod with 13 call sites — rename is mechanical and cheap, but the semantic cost is real.\n\nAlso note: there IS an `update`-flavored thing in the codebase? Let me think — no need to check; the conceptual point stands.\n\nSo answer: 可以改(机械上没障碍,13 处调用点一改就行),但不该改,因为:\n- 你上一条刚理解了 transition ≠ update;改名就是把刚建立的正确语义改掉\n- \"update\" 向读者承诺\"无规则写值\",而这函数的全部价值在于有规则\n- 会和 `transition_harness_state` 形成错误的对仗:读者会以为 update_harness_state 和 transition_harness_state 是两回事,实际前者是后者的 controller 适配\n- 如果嫌 _transition 太短,保留 transition 词根的加长版可以(如 _transition_harness),换动词不行\n\nAlso per the naming rule of thumb: 名字是给读代码的人的承诺。改名的检验标准:改名后,函数的行为和名字的承诺还一致吗?update 承诺\"改值\",行为是\"受约束迁移\"→ 不一致。\n\nKeep it short and direct. No code changes (they're asking permission/judgment, not commanding). Per session pattern, answer conceptually. If they insist, it's a mechanical rename. But my recommendation: no.\n\nFormat: short, direct verdict first, then reasons. This is a quick turn — don't over-elaborate.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"6bdb1420-c25a-4bbf-9235-b3efa5928d9b","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"机械上完全可以改(纯重命名，13 处调用点一键替换)，**但语义上是倒退，我不建议**——上一条你刚理解了为什么它不叫 update,这个改名恰恰是把刚建立的正确语义改掉：\n\n1. **名字是对读者的承诺**。`update_harness_state` 承诺的是\"无规则写值\"；而这个函数的全部价值恰恰在于**有规则**(查表、终态守卫、版本推进、双校验)。改完之后，函数做的事和名字承诺的事不一致——这正是该改名的信号，现在方向反了。\n\n2. **会制造一个错误的对仗**。store 层已经有 `transition_harness_state`;controller 的 `_transition` 是它的适配器，**刻意保留同一个动词**，读者一眼看出“就是同一个操作，隔了一层”。改名成 `update_harness_state` 后，两个名字像是两件不同的事，实际是同一件——名字撒谎了。\n\n3. 按你自己的术语纪律检验：这次对话里我们已经定了——**update 是数据操作，transition 是状态机迁移**。这函数做的是后者。让名字跟行为对齐，就该保留 transition 词根。\n\n如果你是嫌 `_transition` 太短、信息量不够，加长可以，但**换词根不行**：\n\n```python\n_transition              # 现状:类内上下文里足够清楚\n_transition_harness      # 可以:明确\"迁移的是 harness 子现场\"\n_update_harness_state    # 不行:动词错了,承诺了错误的语义\n```\n\n检验一个名字该不该改，就用这条：改名后，新名字的承诺和函数的实际行为还一致吗？`_transition` 一致;`update_harness_state` 不一致。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789987780266},{"id":"5b1fa9f3-5e9f-49ba-8bd0-6bcfe1df0473","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"_transition的责任不就是修改  status=status,phase=phase,    terminal_intent=terminal_intent, 这几个状态吗，所以叫做_update_harness_state有什么问题吗？","payload":{"query":"_transition的责任不就是修改  status=status,phase=phase,    terminal_intent=terminal_intent, 这几个状态吗，所以叫做_update_harness_state有什么问题吗？","rawMessage":"_transition的责任不就是修改  status=status,phase=phase,    terminal_intent=terminal_intent, 这几个状态吗，所以叫做_update_harness_state有什么问题吗？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"2d1a753b-bea9-4dc0-9e1e-b23a21a53012","requestedAt":1789987942877,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"5b1fa9f3-5e9f-49ba-8bd0-6bcfe1df0473"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789987942920},{"id":"89205dcc-37ce-4266-9823-3138e6f20e44","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"5b1fa9f3-5e9f-49ba-8bd0-6bcfe1df0473","reportedId":"28f0b128-94a0-4c53-8304-a01bb7323f18","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":65.04,"contextUsed":166510,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":850,"totalDuration":37070},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab10c6723332500531b549a","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":36221},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"60936e05-fb25-45fd-ba7b-62b2220580f7","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user pushes back: \"_transition 的责任不就是修改 status=status, phase=phase, terminal_intent=terminal_intent 这几个状态吗,所以叫做 _update_harness_state 有什么问题吗?\"\n\nTheir argument: the function's responsibility is just modifying those few fields (status, phase, terminal_intent), so calling it \"update\" is accurate.\n\nI need to engage seriously with this argument, not just repeat myself. Is their premise correct? Let me look at what `transition_harness_state` actually does again (state.py:151-188):\n\n```python\ndef transition_harness_state(state, *, status, phase, terminal_intent=None):\n    current = HarnessStateSnapshot.model_validate(state)      # 校验现场\n    # 终态检查:已是终态 → 同名+FINALIZATION 幂等返回,否则拒绝\n    if current.status in terminal_statuses: ...\n    # 查迁移表\n    if phase not in _PHASE_TRANSITIONS[current.phase]: raise\n    # intent 处理\n    intent = terminal_intent if terminal_intent is not None else current.terminal_intent\n    # 终态只能由 running/finalization 同名 intent 提交\n    if status in terminal_statuses and (current.phase is not FINALIZATION or status.value != intent): raise\n    candidate = {\n        **encode_harness_state(state),\n        \"status\": status.value,\n        \"phase\": phase.value,\n        \"terminal_intent\": intent,\n        \"state_version\": current.state_version + 1,   # 版本+1\n    }\n    if current.status is WAITING_CONFIRMATION and status is RUNNING:\n        candidate[\"pending_confirmation\"] = None      # 副作用:清确认\n    return decode_harness_state(candidate)\n```\n\nSo the user's premise is factually incomplete: the function does NOT just modify those three fields. It:\n1. May REJECT the modification (查表/终态守卫) — a pure update never refuses\n2. Modifies a FOURTH field the caller didn't pass: state_version (+1)\n3. May modify a FIFTH field: pending_confirmation → None (side effect)\n4. Derives/normalizes: terminal_intent 继承当前值(不传时保留)\n5. Validates before and after\n\nSo the honest answer to \"责任不就是修改这几个字段吗\": 不止——你列的三个字段是**输入参数**,但函数的责任范围还包括它**自行决定**改的字段(state_version、pending_confirmation)和它**有权拒绝**的修改(非法迁移)。恰恰是\"会拒绝\"这一点,让\"update\"这个名字失真:没有一个叫 update 的东西会说\"不\"。\n\nLet me make this vivid and concrete:\n\n- 你调 `dict.update()` 或 `state[\"harness\"][\"status\"] = x`,它永远不会说不行。\n- 你调 `_transition`,传 status=COMPLETED、当前在 execute_tool 阶段——它会抛 ValueError,什么都不改。\n- 一个会拒绝执行的名字叫 update,就像一个会把你拦下的门叫\"通道\"——不是不能叫,但名字丢掉了它最重要的行为特征。\n\nAlso the framing: 责任的边界不是\"我传了什么参数\",而是\"它对现场做了什么、能拒绝什么\"。参数是 3 个,行为是 6 件。\n\nAnother angle — the \"what would a reader predict\" test: 名字是读者预测行为的唯一线索。看到 update_harness_state,读者预测:无条件改字段。实际:可能拒绝、可能多改两个字段。预测失真 = 名字失败。\n\nAnd: if we renamed to update, then transition_harness_state (store layer) — what would it be? The user's proposal breaks the two-layer naming correspondence.\n\nConcrete demonstration with the actual code paths — show the four fields changed, not three:\n\n```python\ncandidate = {\n    **encode_harness_state(state),\n    \"status\": status.value,          # 你传的\n    \"phase\": phase.value,            # 你传的\n    \"terminal_intent\": intent,       # 你传的,或不传时自动继承\n    \"state_version\": current.state_version + 1,   # 它自己决定的\n}\nif WAITING_CONFIRMATION → RUNNING:\n    candidate[\"pending_confirmation\"] = None      # 它自己决定的\n```\n\nSo \"修改这几个字段\"低估了它:它改 5 个字段,还可能拒绝改。\n\nKeep the response focused: 直接回答\"有什么问题\"——问题是你列的不全,而漏掉的部分(会拒绝、改第四五个字段)正是 update 这个词承诺不了的部分。Name = promise test again. Short-ish. No code changes.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"1e0c14cc-5550-4b2e-885b-00501bd126e9","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"你的论据里藏了一个事实漏洞，问题就出在这：**它改的不止那三个字段，而且它有权力“拒绝修改”**。看实际代码(state.py:179-188):\n\n```python\ncandidate = {\n    **encode_harness_state(state),\n    \"status\": status.value,                        # ① 你传的\n    \"phase\": phase.value,                          # ② 你传的\n    \"terminal_intent\": intent,                     # ③ 你传的,不传时自动继承旧值\n    \"state_version\": current.state_version + 1,    # ④ 它自己决定 +1,你没传\n}\nif current.status is WAITING_CONFIRMATION and status is RUNNING:\n    candidate[\"pending_confirmation\"] = None       # ⑤ 它自己决定清除,你没传\n```\n\n三个输入参数，**五处实际写入**，外加前后两次整体校验和查表守卫。“责任就是改这几个字段”这个前提本身不成立。\n\n而“会拒绝”是致命的一条。对比一下：\n\n```python\nstate[\"harness\"].update({\"status\": \"completed\"})   # update:永远不会说不行\n_transition(state, status=COMPLETED, phase=FINALIZATION)\n# 若当前在 execute_tool 阶段 → ValueError,什么都没改\n```\n\n**update 的语义承诺是“无条件改值”；这函数最重要的行为特征是“条件不满足时拒绝改”**。一个会把你拦在门外的操作叫 update,就像一个会查证件的岗亭叫“通道”——不是不能叫，是名字把最关键的行为特征丢了。\n\n名字的检验标准还是那条：读者看到名字会预测什么行为？\n\n| 名字 | 读者预测 | 实际行为 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `update_harness_state` | 无条件改字段 | 可能拒绝；改 5 个字段；版本+1;前后校验 |\n| `_transition` | 状态机迁移一步，受规则约束 | ✓ 完全一致 |\n\n预测一致的名字才是好名字。你现在的困惑(“不就是改几个字段吗”)恰好反向证明了这个名字的必要性——因为它做的是**迁移**，不是**改字段**，而你列的三个字段只是迁移的输入，不是迁移的全部。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789987980264},{"id":"8eb59b60-2039-4bf9-8627-82107472969a","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"transition_harness_state  叫这个可以吗，感觉transition根本不知道在做什么","payload":{"query":"transition_harness_state  叫这个可以吗，感觉transition根本不知道在做什么","rawMessage":"transition_harness_state  叫这个可以吗，感觉transition根本不知道在做什么","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","name":"state.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE","filePath":"app/agent/state_result_store/state.py","selection":[77,117]}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"247c8d81-33f0-463d-b3af-3ba076d6e236","requestedAt":1789988115253,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"8eb59b60-2039-4bf9-8627-82107472969a"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]},"taskReminderInjected":true},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1789988115273},{"id":"cffcc26b-beaf-4b65-87ac-2c328fdf5fcc","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"8eb59b60-2039-4bf9-8627-82107472969a","reportedId":"8f874c8f-2f40-46a9-a565-f2567a0836a9","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","tokenUsage":{"usagePercentage":66.16,"contextUsed":169367,"contextLimit":256000,"needCompression":true,"savedPercentage":0},"performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":691,"totalDuration":61296},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab10d14d0d0586a4a65f37d","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":60607},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"a1617a3a-ecd3-43cb-b74a-864d6d7710eb","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"transition_harness_state 叫这个可以吗,感觉 transition 根本不知道在做什么\"\n\nWait — the function IS called `transition_harness_state` already (state.py:151). Let me re-read their question.\n\n\"transition_harness_state 叫这个可以吗\" — Hmm. They're asking whether the name `transition_harness_state` is OK? Or are they proposing... Let me parse carefully.\n\n\"transition_harness_state 叫这个可以吗\" — \"is it OK to call it transition_harness_state\" — but it's already called that! So maybe they mean:\n\nOption A: They're asking whether the CURRENT name `transition_harness_state` is good — expressing doubt: \"感觉 transition 根本不知道在做什么\" — \"I feel like 'transition' doesn't tell you what it's doing\".\n\nSo this is the reverse direction from before! Earlier they wanted to rename `_transition` → `_update_harness_state` (I argued transition is the right verb). Now they're saying: \"transition\" as a word doesn't tell them what the function does. They're questioning whether `transition_harness_state` (the store-layer function, the name they quoted) is a good name.\n\nWait — or Option B: maybe they misread and think the current name is something else? No — the function is `transition_harness_state` in state.py which they have open. The controller wrapper is `_transition`. Two messages ago they asked to rename `_transition` → `_update_harness_state`. Now they ask about `transition_harness_state` itself.\n\n\"叫这个可以吗\" — \"calling it THIS, is that OK?\" — perhaps they're asking \"is it OK that it's called this?\" i.e., evaluating the current name. \"感觉transition根本不知道在做什么\" — \"I feel 'transition' gives no idea what it's doing\" — they find \"transition\" too abstract/vague.\n\nSo the user's complaint: the word \"transition\" is a domain/CS term that, to them, doesn't convey the operation. They want a more self-evident name.\n\nHow to respond? Key points:\n\n1. First — precision: `transition_harness_state` is the CURRENT name of the store-layer function (state.py:151). So \"叫这个可以吗\" — it already is called this. The question is whether this name is good.\n\n2. The complaint \"transition 不知道在做什么\" deserves a serious answer. Is \"transition\" jargon? It's standard state-machine terminology. The function's domain IS a state machine (phases, transitions table). For anyone working in this domain, \"transition\" is the precise word. The name reads as: \"对 harness 控制状态做一次(受规则约束的)阶段迁移\".\n\n3. The deeper point: a name can't explain everything — that's what the docstring is for. The function HAS a docstring: \"\"\"执行阶段转换，并阻止业务阶段直接伪造终态。\"\"\" So: name = 定位词(这是状态机迁移), docstring = 行为细节(查表+终态保护). The name's job is to tell you WHICH KIND of operation, not ALL of the operation.\n\n4. Their feeling \"transition 不知道在做什么\" is actually a knowledge-gap signal, not a naming failure — transition is THE standard term for state machines (数据库 migration, FSM transition, React 之前聊的生命周期都是领域词汇). Learning the domain term once unlocks reading every state-machine codebase afterward. Renaming to something like \"move_harness_state_to\" would trade precision for familiarity and lose the connection to the migration table `_PHASE_TRANSITIONS` (the table is literally named \"phase transitions\" — the function name and table name are a matched pair!).\n\nThat's a strong concrete point: `_PHASE_TRANSITIONS` (迁移表) and `transition_harness_state` (迁移函数) are a matched naming pair. Rename the function away from \"transition\" and you break the correspondence between the table and the only function that enforces it.\n\n5. Also, per their own terminology discipline memory: they corrected me for imprecise terms (\"生命周期\"滥用). Here, \"transition\" is precisely the established term. If they'd asked \"what would be clearer\", alternatives:\n   - `advance_harness_state` — hmm, \"advance\" suggests forward movement only; transitions include the WAIT_CONFIRMATION → RESTORE_RUN, and FINALIZATION self-loop; advance is okay-ish but loses the state-machine jargon link.\n   - `move_to_phase` / `set_phase` — loses \"受约束\"含义, sounds like a setter (back to update territory).\n   - `transition_to(state, phase=...)` — API shape change, not name.\n   The current name is good. The complaint is really about the word \"transition\" being unfamiliar — the fix is learning the term, not renaming.\n\n6. But — hold on. Should I be more humble here? The user has a real point that jargon names impede beginners. Is there a case for renaming? Consider: this is a domain-heavy codebase (SDD-driven, state machine design). The whole file is about state transitions. The term appears in docs? The as-built/SDD docs likely use \"状态转换/迁移\". Renaming would touch store + controller + docs. The benefit would be... familiarity for someone who doesn't know FSM terminology. The cost: losing the matched pair with _PHASE_TRANSITIONS, losing standard jargon, churn. Net: keep.\n\n7. Also answer the literal question \"叫这个可以吗\": 可以,而且这是好名字 — then explain why it feels opaque and what fills the gap (docstring + the paired table + the concept).\n\nTeaching angle: give them the mental hook for \"transition\": 状态机里的\"一次迁移\" = 从状态 A 走到状态 B 的那一步,带着规则。The function: transition_harness_state(state, status=新状态, phase=新阶段) = \"把现场从当前位置迁移到新位置\"。\n\nAlso can point to the ecosystem: 数据库 schema migration、前端路由 navigation、React 状态... hmm, careful with analogies (user's memory: 类比只借结构不借名字). FSM transition is not an analogy — it's the same concept family. Keep it: 有限状态机(FSM)的标准词汇,数据库迁移 migration 同族——领域词.\n\nName = 定位 + 承诺; docstring = 行为; 类型签名 = 细节. Three-layer information architecture. The name shouldn't try to say everything.\n\nConcrete recommendation: keep the name. If reading the file, the docstring at state.py:158 already says what it does. If they want, I could add a comment on the function pointing at _PHASE_TRANSITIONS? Actually the docstring \"执行阶段转换，并阻止业务阶段直接伪造终态\" — could be slightly enriched? Per their convention (docstring 短), current is fine. Maybe no code change. Actually — their question is purely about naming judgment. Answer, no code edit.\n\nStructure:\n1. 先纠正一个事实:它现在就叫 transition_harness_state(state.py:151)——所以你问的是\"这个名字好不好\"。\n2. \"transition 不知道在做什么\"的感觉从哪来:它是一个领域词(FSM 状态机的\"迁移\"),不是日常英语动词。第一次见不知道,知道之后比任何通俗词都准。\n3. 为什么仍然可以(好):①和 _PHASE_TRANSITIONS 是配对命名(表+执行表的那个函数);②函数有 docstring 补行为;③名字的任务是定位,不是百科。\n4. 如果改成通俗词会丢什么:set_phase/advance 之类要么退回 setter 语义(就是 update 问题重演),要么丢掉和迁移表的配对。\n5. 心智钩子:transition = \"带规则的一步\"。数据库的 migration、状态机的 transition,同一家族。\n\nKeep it compact.","startTime":1791428023754,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023754},{"id":"942ad976-9a75-4041-9084-f2b98aeb5cf8","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"先对齐一个事实：它**现在就叫** `transition_harness_state`(state.py:151)——所以你真正问的是“这个名字起得好不好”，你的感受是“transition 这个词看不出在干什么”。\n\n这个感受值得认真对待，但结论是：**这名字可以，而且是配好的**。分三层说：\n\n**1. “看不懂”的来源是领域词，不是名字失败。** transition 是状态机(FSM)的标准词汇——“迁移”= 从状态 A 走到状态 B 的那一步，且这一步受规则约束。数据库的 migration(迁移)、刚才聊的 `_PHASE_TRANSITIONS`(迁移表)，全是同一家族。第一次见确实不知道，但这是**学一次就解锁**的词：学会之后，你读任何状态机代码库、任何迁移表，这个词都在准确地工作。换成通俗词省下的那一下 lookup,代价是永久丢掉和整个领域的连接。\n\n**2. 名字和表是配对的，拆开就断**。state.py 里这对命名是刻意呼应的：\n\n```\n_PHASE_TRANSITIONS          ← 迁移表:规则存在哪(哪些边合法)\ntransition_harness_state    ← 迁移函数:唯一执行这张表的地方\n```\n\n函数名里的 transition 就是表的回指。改叫 `advance_harness_state` / `set_phase` 之类，读者要去猜“那个表是谁在执行”；保留词根，对应关系自明。而且 `set_phase`/`advance` 又会滑回你上次问的 update 陷阱——听起来像无规则赋值。\n\n**3. 名字的职责是“定位”，不是“百科”**。一个名字只负责告诉你**这是哪一类操作**；具体行为由 docstring 和签名负责，三层分工：\n\n```python\ndef transition_harness_state(...) -> HarnessControlState:\n    \"\"\"执行阶段转换，并阻止业务阶段直接伪造终态。\"\"\"\n    #      ↑ 名字:这是状态机迁移      ↑ docstring:它守什么规则\n```\n\n你觉得“transition 不知道在做什么”，本质是**这个词对你还没形成条件反射**——这正是这次走查该收获的东西：以后在任何代码里看到 transition,你的第一反应应该是“哦，带规则的一步，附近肯定有一张表或一组约束”。这是领域词汇的投资，不是命名缺陷。"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1789988176873},{"id":"5b1c66db-a5bd-42b3-82f2-2d2e88cd031d","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"    def _transition(\n        state: HarnessGraphState,\n        *,\n        status: HarnessS