ured). extra is for future structured log collection; a \"step\" field there makes sense and stays out of the console line. But then the step wouldn't appear in console output (format only shows %(message)s)... For \"根据 logger 判断当前代码位置\" the step needs to be VISIBLE — if it's only in extra, the console log won't show it (format string only includes message). So to serve their purpose (locate code from logs), step should be in the MESSAGE, not just extra. Or both: message shows it, extra carries it structured.\n\nActually wait — house style: extra={\"run_id\": ...} duplicates what's already in the message. The convention in this file: message contains human-readable values, extra repeats them as structured keys. So doing both is consistent: message \"step=入口迁移\" + extra {\"step\": \"入口迁移\"}.\n\nHmm, but honestly — simplest faithful implementation of their ask:\n\n```python\n        logger.info(\n            \"Harness step=%s phase=%s: run_id=%s turn_id=%s\",\n            \"入口预检后迁移构建上下文\",\n            state[\"harness\"][\"phase\"],\n            ...\n            extra={\"step\": \"入口预检后迁移构建上下文\", \"run_id\": ..., \"turn_id\": ...},\n        )\n```\n\nHmm, that's getting verbose. Alternatively make step the static prefix directly in the message text:\n\n```python\n        logger.info(\n            \"Harness step=入口预检-迁移BUILD_CONTEXT phase=%s: run_id=%s turn_id=%s\", ...\n```\n\nWait — \"直接写死中文汉字\" — they explicitly want Chinese hardcoded. OK.\n\nDesign decision: hardcoded step string in message + extra. Since they explicitly asked \"手写\" (hardcoded, hand-written), accept it — this is their call, and it does serve the landmark purpose. My earlier \"read from state\" for phase stays (they said 不折腾状态了 — don't fuss over the state/phase part anymore; keep phase dynamic as-is, add step hardcoded).\n\nWhat Chinese step name? The site is step ① in _run: 入口,after deadline check,transition to BUILD_CONTEXT,save. Something like \"入口:迁移到构建上下文\" or \"启动迁移-构建上下文\". Keep it short: \"入口迁移构建上下文\"? Or align with my ① annotation: \"①入口迁移\". Hmm — my annotations use ①②③; the step label could match: \"1-入口迁移\" ... The annotation numbers are in comments, not greppable strings. The step string should be self-explanatory in logs: e.g. \"入口-迁移到BUILD_CONTEXT\" — mixing? They said 中文汉字. \"入口-迁移到构建上下文\" is clear.\n\nWait — should I also reconsider: they said \"增加一个 'step': xxx\" — maybe they want it as an extra key ONLY: extra={\"step\": \"...\"}. But then invisible in console... Actually wait, let me check: is the format string \"%(asctime)s | %(levelname)s | %(name)s | %(message)s\" — yes, extra keys invisible in console. For their stated goal (根据 logger 判断当前代码位置), the console MUST show it → message must include it. I'll put it in the message AND in extra (following the house pattern of duplicating into extra for structured collection).\n\nNaming the step value: concise Chinese, identifies the location. \"入口预检后进入构建上下文\"? I'd go: \"入口:迁移到构建上下文\" — but colon inside might clash with the message format... fine. Let me keep: \"入口迁移到构建上下文\" (no punctuation).\n\nActually hold on — maybe simpler and cleaner: since step is handwritten and the message template is per-site anyway, make the WHOLE message per-site instead of generic \"Harness phase=%s\":\n\n```python\nlogger.info(\n    \"Harness 入口迁移构建上下文: phase=%s run_id=%s turn_id=%s\",\n    state[\"harness\"][\"phase\"], ...\n```\n\nHmm, but user asked specifically for `\"step\": xxx` — a step field. I'll do:\n\n```python\n        # step 手写定位代码位置：日志里直接看到这是哪一步（约定与 _run 注释的步骤号对应）\n        logger.info(\n            \"Harness step=%s phase=%s: run_id=%s turn_id=%s\",\n            \"1-入口迁移构建上下文\",\n            state[\"harness\"][\"phase\"],\n            ...\n            extra={\"step\": \"1-入口迁移构建上下文\", ...},\n        )\n```\n\nShould the step include the annotation number \"1\"? My _run annotations use ①-⑭ circled numbers. Using \"1\" vs \"①\" — grep-wise ① is unicode, fine in logs. Aligning log step with the code anno