f the client generates run_id, then the frontend polls status immediately after POST /run/stream fails/aborts — explaining the \"不存在\" poll.\n\nLet me check: grep class HarnessRunRequest in harness.py.\n\nActually, regardless of where the frontend got it, the DB evidence is decisive: turn committed, run never created. The status endpoint correctly reports 不存在. The interesting question for the user is \"why is my run missing\" — answer: the run died between turn registration and run creation (likely backend restart mid-request — they're editing code today with reload; or an assembly/LLM precondition error). And the side effect: the conversation now has an orphaned running turn which may block new runs (\"当前会话已有未完成的 Harness 运行\").\n\nLet me quickly check HarnessRunRequest to see if run_id comes from the client (one grep), and check whether there's any cleanup for orphan turns (there probably isn't — could be a 疑点). Then answer.","startTime":1791428023757,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023757},{"id":"12790c5a-d069-486c-8725-fa9989ef3341","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"时间线拼出来了。最后确认一个环节——前端从哪拿到这个 run_id（看请求模型是否客户端生成）："},{"id":"call_61e99950797247cfb0d5fad1","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"grep -n -A 12 \"class HarnessRunRequest\" app/api/routers/harness.py | head -16; echo -------; grep -rn \"run_id\" frontend/components/insight-agent/chat-session-view.tsx | grep -i \"generat\\|crypto\\|uuid\\|randomUUID\\|makeId\" | head -3; grep -rn \"randomUUID\\|uuidv4\\|crypto.randomUUID\" frontend/lib frontend/components/insight-agent 2>/dev/null | grep -v \".next\" | head -5","description":"Check whether run_id is client-generated"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\n94:class HarnessRunRequest(BaseModel):\n95-    \"\"\"创建 Harness 运行的请求；用户认证完成前暂时携带 user_id。\"\"\"\n96-\n97-    input_text: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=20_000)\n98-    # 当前前端尚未接入登录；后续由认证依赖替换，而不是修改 Harness 状态模型。\n99-    us