"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/memory/types/working.py","name":"working.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false,"sendMode":"normal","clientRequestId":"ffa2822a-fbec-4ece-ab4f-3d74b483c259","requestedAt":1790155599120,"localPermissionMode":"full-access","codex":{"startGoal":false,"startPlan":false,"compact":false},"id":"ad1cb758-af95-416b-b72f-2f9b7614aa3b"},"discard":false,"context":{"conversationId":21049217,"taskId":3511606,"capabilitySnapshot":{"version":1,"skillFingerprint":"cc89f1bf6393a278da603fb8c6345718b0afff8a","subAgentsFingerprint":"fd5f5328b64d04b5298af7f280460d92b7f026b2","sentNestedSkillKeys":[]}},"disabledRollback":false,"appliedRules":[],"deviceType":"Local","requestedAt":1790155599133},{"id":"1fa0df63-4485-415c-9155-cb166e546d43","v2":true,"quotaExceedMessage":"","discard":false,"userMessageId":"ad1cb758-af95-416b-b72f-2f9b7614aa3b","reportedId":"","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Comate"},"role":"assistant","status":"cancelled","performanceMetrics":{"firstTokenLatency":774},"appliedRuleNames":[],"content":{},"elements":[{"id":"6ab39b50e5abac4a6887422e","discard":false,"metrics":{},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"7ced955b-417e-48b5-822c-0423184cb43a","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The user asks: \"什么叫重建页面，sse断开后还可以继续吗\" — what does \"rebuild the page/UI\" mean, and after SSE disconnects, can it continue?\n\nTwo questions:\n1. What does 重建界面 mean (I said \"重建界面\" in the earlier answer about status usage)\n2. Can the run continue after SSE breaks?\n\nKey facts from the codebase (as-built chapters):\n- SSE 断开 → 客户端断连 → §4.3: \"SSE body() 检测到断连 cancel task 并 shield（harness.py:561-569）→ 控制器 asyncio.CancelledError 分支 → 收口任务 create_task(_finalize(CANCELLED))\" — **the run does NOT continue! Client disconnect = CANCELLED terminal state** (for the /run/stream path).\n\nWait — careful. There are two disconnect scenarios:\n1. **用户主动关闭页面/断开** during an active stream → server detects disconnect → cancels the task → run finalized as CANCELLED. The run does NOT keep running.\n2. **刷新页面** — same thing: the SSE connection drops → run cancelled.\n\nHmm wait, is that right? Let me recheck §4.3 from the as-built doc: \"cancelled：客户端断开 — SSE body() 检测到断连 cancel task 并 shield → 控制器 asyncio.CancelledError 分支：_prepare_interruption_state → 收口任务 create_task(_finalize(CANCELLED))\".\n\nSo yes: when the SSE connection breaks, the backend **cancels the run** and finalizes it as CANCELLED. The run does not continue server-side.\n\nBUT — there's a nuance. The disconnect detection: harness.py:561-569 in the stream generator. If the connection breaks, the server notices via the generator being closed / request.is_disconnected. So for the /run/stream endpoint, disconnect = cancel = CANCELLED.\n\nSo \"SSE 断开后还可以继续吗\" — the honest answer: **不能**。SSE 断开即取消，run 走 CANCELLED 终态收口（落库、释放 active_run）。这就是为什么\"重建界面\"不等于\"续跑\"——刷新后前端恢复的是**历史**（execution-trace 回放）+ **终态**（status 查询），而不是把中断的运行接回来。\n\nAnd \"重建界面\" (rebuild UI) means: the frontend re-renders the execution panel state from persisted data:\n- `POST /conversations/execution-trace` 历史事件回放（toHistoricalStreamEvent）→ 恢复已完成分组的显示\n- `GET /run/status` → 查终态（或 waiting_confirmation）\n- 如果 status 显示 waiting_confirmation → 恢复确认卡片，可以走 /run/resume/stream 继续这个 run（resume 是真正的\"继续\"——从 BUILD_CONTEXT 重走一轮）\n\nWait — important nuance: WAITING_CONFIRMATION runs DO survive disconnects? §3.1/3.4: WAITING_CONFIRMATION is a paused state, not connected to the SSE lifecycle... When the run pauses for confirmation, does the SSE stream end? The LoopPausedResult ends the HTTP response normally (\"HTTP 响应在 LoopPausedResult 后正常结束\"). So during waiting_confirmation the stream has already ended normally (server finished the response; no active SSE). If the user refreshes then, the run is alive in DB, and resume re-enters _run from BUILD_CONTEXT. So \"继续\" is possible ONLY through the confirmation-resume path, not via SSE reconnect.\n\nAlso what about the orphan case we just diagnosed? If the backend process dies (not a clean disconnect), the run row may stay 'running' forever (like the 3f20190a/ed5dcff1 rows with status='running' from 9-21 — actually those are stuck running runs from crashes!). Interesting: the two 'running' status rows from 2026-09-21 are likely orphans from backend restarts too. That connects: SSE断开（干净断连）→ CANCELLED 收口；进程死亡 → 连收口都没有 → 永久 running 孤儿。\n\nSo the answer structure:\n1. \"重建界面\"的含义：前端用持久化数据把执行面板画回来——execution-trace 历史回放（已完成的分组）+ status 快照（终态/等待确认）。数据从 PG 来，不是从 SSE 来。\n2. SSE 断开后 run 还继续吗：**不继续**。/run/stream 检测到断连 → asyncio.CancelledError → _finalize(CANCELLED)——干净取消、落库、释放 active_run（§4.3）。所以刷新页面 = 主动取消这次运行。\n3. 唯一的\"继续\"路径：waiting_confirmation 暂停态（stream 正常结束、run 活在库里）→ /run/resume/stream 从 BUILD_CONTEXT 重走一轮。这不是 SSE 重连，是新的请求。\n4. 补充（呼应上午的孤儿诊断）：如果断开不是干净断连而是进程死亡，连 CANCELLED 收口都没有 → 永久 running 孤儿（库里那两条 9-21 的 running 就是）。\n\nKeep it concise per user's recent preference (they asked for 简洁 last time). Use a small diagram/table. No code changes needed — pure explanation. Maybe cite harness.py:561-569, controller.py:205-227, as-built §4.3/§3.4.","startTime":1791428023757,"lastModifiedTime":1791428023757},{"id":"48db524a-df60-4acf-ae57-134eaed7cd6a","type":"TEXT","end":true,"content":"两个"}]}],"deviceType":"Local","completedAt":1790155636761},{"id":"d8b73b6f-0104-47c7-9a2e-5438a1b24cd3","summary":"","role":"user","status":"success","content":"@router.get(\"/run/status\")他的主要用途是在于刷新页面、切回会话？","payload":{"query":"@router.get(\"/run/status\")他的主要用途是在于刷新页面、切回会话？","rawMessage":"@router.get(\"/run/status\")他的主要用途是在于刷新页面、切回会话？","model":{"displayName":"Auto","modelId":"auto","requestType":"COMATE_DEFAULT_MODE","mode":"NORMAL"},"agent":{"agentId":1,"agentName":"Comate","agentImage":"zulu"},"metrics":{"model":"Zulu","function":""},"knowledgeList":[{"id":"app/agent/memory/types/working.py","name":"working.py","type":"CURRENT_FILE"}],"isCurrentFileSelected":false